    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/233223": {
      "title": "Tobacco Extension Agronomist",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | Tobacco Extension Agronomist Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) Tobacco Extension Agronomist Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please attach a Cover Letter, resume/CV, and contact information for three (3) professional references. Posting Details Posting Information Posting Number PG194764EP Internal Recruitment No Working Title Tobacco Extension Agronomist Anticipated Hiring Range Commensurate with Experience ($92,500 - $110,000) Work Schedule Core Business Hours: Monday - Friday; 8:00 AM - 5:00 PM; flexible and variable based on business needs. Job Location Raleigh, NC Department Crop and Soil Sciences About the Department The Department of Crop and Soil Sciences integrates research, extension, and teaching across diverse disciplines to advance agricultural and environmental systems. Its mission is to develop future leaders in crop, soil, and environmental sciences; enhance crop plants and products; and design innovative, sustainable crop production and soil management systems for agricultural and urban landscapes. The department is committed to generating and delivering science-based knowledge that serves producers and end users of food, feed, turf, biofuels, and fiber in North Carolina, across the nation, and globally. Wolfpack Perks and Benefits As a Pack member, you belong here, and can enjoy exclusive perks designed to enhance your personal and professional well-being. As you consider this opportunity, we encourage you to review our Employee Value Proposition and learn more about what makes NC State the best place to learn and work for everyone. What we offer: Medical , Dental , and Vision Flexible Spending Account Retirement Programs Disability Plans Life Insurance Accident Plan Paid Time Off and Other Leave Programs 12 Holidays Each Year Tuition and Academic Assistance And so much more! Attain Work-life balance with our Childcare benefits, Wellness & Recreation Membership , and Wellness Programs that aim to build a thriving wolfpack community. Disclaimer: Perks and Benefit eligibility is based on Part-Time or Full-Time Employment status. Eligibility and Employer Sponsored Plans can be found within each of the links offered. Essential Job Duties The Department of Crop and Soil Sciences at NC State University invites applications for an Assistant Professor and Crop Production Management Specialist. Supported through the Collins Endowment Distinguished Fellowship, this position will provide statewide leadership in applied tobacco agronomy through an integrated program of Extension, research, and teaching focused on improving the sustainability, productivity, and profitability of North Carolina’s flue-cured and burley tobacco industries. In this role, you will work alongside growers, industry partners, county Extension agents, researchers, and agricultural professionals to address real-world crop production challenges and translate research into practical solutions. You will help shape tobacco production recommendations, support producers through emerging challenges, and strengthen the connection between university research and on-farm practices. This position provides an opportunity to build upon NC State’s longstanding leadership in tobacco agronomy while advancing innovation in crop management, sustainability, and production efficiency. Key Responsibilities fall within three key areas outlined below: Extension: Provide statewide Extension leadership and technical support to tobacco growers, county Extension agents, crop consultants, NCDA &CS regional agronomists, agribusiness partners, and other industry stakeholders. Develop and deliver educational programs through grower meetings, field days, county agent trainings, farm visits, and stakeholder workshops. Translate research findings into practical recommendations that address production challenges and support informed decision-making. Maintain and update the NC Flue-Cured Tobacco Production Guide to ensure producers and agricultural professionals have access to current production recommendations and best management practices. Build and strengthen partnerships with state, regional, and national tobacco organizations to advance the tobacco production industry. Research: Develop an applied research program focused on improving flue-cured and burley tobacco production systems. Evaluate new products, technologies, and production practices, including precision agriculture approaches, to improve crop productivity, sustainability, and profitability. Investigate management strategies related to climate variability, pest management, herbicide-resistant weeds, and other emerging production challenges. Conduct on-farm research and demonstrations to evaluate practical solutions under producer conditions. Collaborate with the Director of the Official Variety Testing Program to evaluate tobacco cultivars across multiple environments. Partner with NC State faculty and external collaborators on research related to pesticide residue expectations and the evaluation of new agricultural chemicals for tobacco production. Teaching: Co-teach the undergraduate course CS 116/216 – Agronomic Crops – Cotton, Peanuts, and Tobacco during the fall semester. Provide approximately five weeks of instruction during the fall and spring semesters and two weeks every other summer. In this role, you will have the opportunity to make a meaningful impact through Extension, research, and teaching while contributing to the continued success of North Carolina agriculture.If you are passionate about applying agricultural research to real-world challenges, building strong relationships with industry and community partners, and preparing the next generation of agricultural professionals, we encourage you to apply. Other Responsibilities n/a Qualifications Minimum Education and Experience Ph.D. Degree in Weed Science, Agronomy, or a closely related field. Experience in agronomic aspects of flue-cured tobacco production preferred. Candidate should have excellent written and oral communication skills. Other Required Qualifications Demonstrated knowledge of row crop agronomy principles, including soil science, crop production systems, crop management practices, and sustainable agricultural approaches. Ability to develop and execute applied agronomic research that addresses real-world production challenges. Proficiency in collecting, analyzing, and interpreting field-based data to inform research findings and practical agronomic recommendations. Experience with statistical analysis methods and software used to evaluate agricultural research data. Ability to communicate complex scientific information effectively through research publications, Extension resources, technical reports, presentations, and stakeholder engagement. Preferred Qualifications Experience applying tobacco agronomy principles, conducting field-based research, and/or incorporating emerging technologies to address agricultural production challenges. Ability to develop and deliver Extension programs that translate research into practical solutions for growers, consultants, and industry professionals. Ability to build and maintain strong relationships with growers, Extension agents, researchers, and agricultural stakeholders. Record of research, teaching, Extension, and service activities consistent with appointment at the Assistant Professor level. Required License(s) or Certification(s) A valid NC Driver’s License and the ability to obtain an NC Driver’s License within 60 days of hire and must be maintained throughout employment. Valid NC Driver's License required Yes Commercial Driver's License required No Recruitment Dates and Special Instructions Job Open Date 07/28/2026 Anticipated Close Date 8/24/2026; if posting is still active we are accepting and reviewing applications Special Instructions to Applicants Please attach a Cover Letter, resume/CV, and contact information for three (3) professional references. Position Details Position Number 00104093 Position Type Tenured/Tenure-Track Faculty Full Time Equivalent (FTE) (1.0 = 40 hours/week) 1.0 Appointment 12 Month Recurring Mandatory Designation - Adverse Weather Non Mandatory - Adverse Weather Mandatory Designation - Emergency Events Mandatory - Medical Emergencies Department ID 110901 - Crop and Soil Sciences EEO NC State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal opportunities for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, and veteran status. The University encourages all qualified applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities, to apply. Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodations in the application and interview process are welcome to contact 919-513-0574 to speak with a representative of the Office of Equal Opportunity. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at (919) 515-2135 or workatncstate@ncsu.edu . Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. Degree(s) must be obtained prior to start date in order to meet qualifications and receive credit. NC State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn of this opportunity? NCSU Website Job Alert (automated email from our system) NCSU Executive Search Services Monster.com CareerBuilder.com InsideHigherEd.com Other Online Job Board Carolina Job Finder / Employment Guide Job / Career Fair The Chronicle of Higher Education Professional Journal Print Advertisement (Newspaper / Periodical) Professional Organization Direct Contact from NCSU HR Representative / Recruiter NCSU Employee Referral Social Media (LinkedIn, Twitter, Facebook, Other) Other If you learned about this vacancy from \"other source\" or \"other website\", please provide the source. (Open Ended Question) * Do you have a Ph.D. Degree in Weed Science, Agronomy, or a closely related field? Yes No * Are you proficient in collecting, analyzing, and interpreting field data to develop actionable agronomic recommendations? Yes No * Do you, or will you, have a valid NC Drivers license or the ability to obtain one within 60 days of hire? Yes No Application Materials Required Required Documents Cover Letter Transcripts Resume/CV Optional Documents NC STATE UNIVERSITY RALEIGH, NC 27695 PHONE: (919) 515-2011 Privacy Accessibility Emergency Information Policies NC State Home © 2019 NC State University. All rights reserved To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
