      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | Temporary Internship Program Assistant Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) Temporary Internship Program Assistant Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Attach: Cover Letter Resume Contact information for 3 references Posting Details Position Information Posting Number PG194846TM Position Number 11ASO3395 Position Type Temporary Essential Job Duties Supporting with the overall coordination, including logistics, administration, planning professional development and evaluation of the summer internships for the Center for Environmental Farming Systems. Specific duties include: Internship recruiting Planning and coordinating logistics or professional development Tracking and documenting activities Assist with paying farmers Support interns with day-to-day activities as needed Schedule: Spring work schedule is approximately 10 hours per week and summer is 20-25 hours. *Possibility of extending after August Is Time Limited No If Yes, Appointment Length Wolfpack Perks and Benefits As a Pack member, you belong here, and can enjoy exclusive perks designed to enhance your personal and professional well-being. What we offer: Health Insurance for Temporary Employees Enhance your career with LEAD courses Attend non-revenue generating sporting events for free. Attain Work-life balance with our Childcare discounts , Wellness & Recreation Membership , and Wellness Programs that aim to build a thriving wolfpack community. Disclaimer: Perks and Benefit eligibility is based on Part-Time or Full-Time Employment status. Eligibility and Employer Sponsored Plans can be found within each of the links offered. Department Information Job City & State Raleigh, NC Department CEF