    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/234488": {
      "title": "Position Information",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | Temporary Transformational Scholars Supervisor for Eastern/Central NC Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) Temporary Transformational Scholars Supervisor for Eastern/Central NC Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number PG196179TM Position Number 13JGM4 Position Type Temporary Essential Job Duties Overview of the College of Education: As one of the nation’s top-ranked colleges of education, NC State’s College of Education leads the way in North Carolina in preparing extraordinary educators, conducting transformational research, and engaging communities where they are to improve the educational outcomes of all learners and advance the greater good.The college’s faculty are widely-recognized thought leaders who use their research to transform the practice of teaching, learning, and leading. They have particular strengths in improving technology-enhanced learning and teaching; fostering community-based learning and PK-16 partnerships; and innovating leadership and workforce development, educational policy, and evaluation. About two-thirds of the faculty are grant active. They are engaged in over 225 active projects totaling $151 million, making them the most productive in terms of research activity compared with other colleges of education in North Carolina and among the Top 5% in the nation. In FY24, the college’s research expenditures exceeded $20 million.The college has over 1,600 students studying across five graduate certificates, seven undergraduate majors, two undergraduate minors, 13 master’s degrees, three Ph.D., and two Ed.D. programs housed in three academic departments: Educational Leadership, Policy, and Human Development; Science, Technology, Engineering, and Mathematics Education; and Teacher Education and Learning Sciences, with approximately 130 tenure-track and professional-track faculty, 110 support and professional staff, and about 160 graduate and teaching assistants. The College of Education is also home to the Belk Center for Community College Leadership and Research, the Friday Institute for Educational Innovation, and Elevate, NC State’s inclusive postsecondary education program for students with intellectual and developmental disabilities.The college has over 18,000 living alumni, with over 6,000 working in public schools in every county in North Carolina. Those who are teachers rate among the highest in effectiveness on surveys of school employers in North Carolina. This role will support student teachers placed in Harnett, Duplin, Edgecombe, and Wilson counties. It is ideal for someone within commuting distance to those areas, as the work will primarily be performed on-site within these counties. The Transformational Scholars Student Teaching Supervisor plays a vital role in supporting and mentoring student teachers participating in the Transformational Scholarship Program. This is a temporary, part-time position running from November to May. This program focuses on developing teacher leaders committed to serving rural eastern North Carolina communities. Supervisors will provide guidance, observation, feedback, and support to ensure student teachers’ success while adhering to program requirements and donor stipulations. This position requires strong communication, collaboration, and organizational skills. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: Relationship Building: Supervisors will foster strong working relationships with their assigned student teachers This involves initial meetings, planning sessions, and establishing effective communication channels. Supervision and Evaluation Supervise and provide regular feedback to assigned Transformational Scholars student teachers. Conduct formal observations, utilizing established rubrics, and provide constructive feedback to promote growth and development. Complete all required documentation and evaluations in a timely manner. This includes: Weekly check-in meetings (virtual or in-person) with each student teacher. Bi-weekly in-person visits to each student teacher’s classroom. Mentoring and Support: Offer ongoing mentorship and support to student teachers, addressing challenges and celebrating successes. Serve as a liaison between student teachers, cooperating teachers, and university faculty. Assist in conflict resolution and provide guidance on best practices. Community Liaison: Actively connect student teachers with relevant community resources, organizations, and individuals. This may involve identifying and facilitating partnerships with local businesses, non-profits, community leaders, and other stakeholders to enrich the student teachers’ learning experience and expand their professional networks. Supervisors will help student teachers leverage these community connections to benefit their students and teaching practice. Program Coordination: Collaborate with program coordinators and fellow supervisors to ensure the effective implementation of the program. Attend relevant meetings and contribute to the overall success of the Transformational Scholars Program. Curriculum Alignment: Ensure that student teaching placements align with the program curriculum and learning objectives. Work closely with cooperating teachers to provide relevant support and materials. Communication: Maintain consistent and clear communication with student teachers, cooperating teachers, program administrators, and other relevant stakeholders. Provide timely updates and address concerns effectively. Travel: Travel to various school districts in eastern North Carolina to supervise student teachers Temporary position Dates of employment: August 16th-May 15th 2026 This role will support student teachers placed in Harnett, Duplin, Samson, Edgecombe, and Wilson counties. It is ideal for someone within commuting distance to those areas, as the work will primarily be performed on-site within these counties. . Schedule: 5-12 hours a week, subject to change based on needs Is Time Limited Yes If Yes, Appointment Length September-May 16th 2026 Wolfpack Perks and Benefits This role will support student teachers placed in Harnett, Duplin, Samson, Edgecombe, and Wilson counties. It is ideal for someone within commuting distance to those areas, as the work will primarily be performed on-site within these counties. Department Information Job City & State Harnett, Duplin, Edgecombe and Wilson counties Department College of Education System Information Classification Title Temporary-Technical/Paraprofessional Working Title Temporary Transformational Scholars Supervisor for Eastern/Central NC Position Information Requirements and Preferences Work Schedule Schedule: 5-12 hours a week, subject to change based on needs Other Work/Responsibilities Responsibilities include: Fall Semester Relationship Building: Supervisors will foster strong working relationships with their assigned student teachers (4-5 per supervisor). This involves initial meetings, planning sessions, and establishing effective communication channels. A portion of the stipend is allocated to this crucial groundwork. Supervision and Evaluation): Supervise and provide regular feedback to assigned Transformational Scholars student teachers (4-5 per supervisor). Conduct formal observations, utilizing established rubrics, and provide constructive feedback to promote growth and development. Complete all required documentation and evaluations in a timely manner. This includes: Weekly check-in meetings (virtual or in-person) with each student teacher. Bi-weekly in-person visits to each student teacher’s classroom. Mentoring and Support: Offer ongoing mentorship and support to student teachers, addressing challenges and celebrating successes. Serve as a liaison between student teachers, cooperating teachers, and university faculty. Assist in conflict resolution and provide guidance on best practices. Community Liaison: Actively connect student teachers with relevant community resources, organizations, and individuals. This may involve identifying and facilitating partnerships with local businesses, non-profits, community leaders, and other stakeholders to enrich the student teachers’ learning experience and expand their professional networks. Supervisors will help student teachers leverage these community connections to benefit their students and teaching practice. Program Coordination: Collaborate with program coordinators and fellow supervisors to ensure the effective implementation of the program. Attend relevant meetings and contribute to the overall success of the Transformational Scholars Program. Curriculum Alignment: Ensure that student teaching placements align with the program curriculum and learning objectives. Work closely with cooperating teachers to provide relevant support and materials. Communication: Maintain consistent and clear communication with student teachers, cooperating teachers, program administrators, and other relevant stakeholders. Provide timely updates and address concerns effectively. Travel: Travel to various school districts in eastern North Carolina to supervise student teachers Schedule: 5-12 hours a week, subject to change based on schedule This role will support student teachers placed in Harnett, Duplin, Edgecombe, Samson, and Wilson counties. It is ideal for someone within commuting distance to those areas, as the work will primarily be performed on-site within these counties. Minimum Experience/Education Minimum experience and education: Bachelor’s degree in Education or a related field required. Minimum of 5 years of successful teaching experience in a K-12 setting, with a demonstrated commitment to equitable and inclusive education. North Carolina teaching license required. Experience mentoring or supervising student teachers preferred. Proven ability to work collaboratively and communicate effectively with varied stakeholders. Strong organizational and time-management skills. Proficiency in using technology for communication, documentation, and evaluation. Commitment to the mission and values of the Transformational Scholars Program. Valid driver’s license and reliable transportation. This role will support student teachers placed in Harnett, Duplin, Samson, Edgecombe, and Wilson counties. It is ideal for someone within commuting distance to those areas, as the work will primarily be performed on-site within these counties. Department Required Skills The Transformational Scholars Student Teaching Supervisor plays a vital role in supporting and mentoring student teachers participating in the Transformational Scholarship Program. This is a temporary, part-time position running from November to May. This program focuses on developing teacher leaders committed to serving rural eastern North Carolina communities. Supervisors will provide guidance, observation, feedback, and support to ensure student teachers’ success while adhering to program requirements and donor stipulations. This position requires strong communication, collaboration, and organizational skills. Preferred Years Experience, Skills, Training, Education N/A Required License or Certification N.A Valid NC Driver's License required? No Commercial Driver's License Required? No Recruitment Recruitment Details Anticipated Hiring Range $23.08/hour Recruitment Dates Job Open Date 08/31/2026 Applicant Information Quick Link https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/234364 EEO NC State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal opportunities for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, and veteran status. The University encourages all qualified applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities, to apply. Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodations in the application and interview process are welcome to contact 919-513-0574 to speak with a representative of the Office of Equal Opportunity. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at (919) 515-2135 or workatncstate@ncsu.edu. Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. Degree(s) must be obtained prior to start date in order to meet qualifications and receive credit. NC State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * This role will primarily take place in Harnett, Duplin, Edgecombe, and Wilson counties, which are outside of the Raleigh area. Do you understand that the work will primarily be performed in these counties? Yes No * Please confirm you understand this position is temporary and is estimated to be around 5-12 hours per week contingent on schedule of the student teachers. Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Contact Information for References Optional Documents NC STATE UNIVERSITY RALEIGH, NC 27695 PHONE: (919) 515-2011 Privacy Accessibility Emergency Information Policies NC State Home © 2019 NC State University. All rights reserved To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
