    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/223243": {
      "title": "UTS - Temporary Electronics Specialist at UNC Chapel Hill (2nd Shift)",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | UTS - Temporary Electronics Specialist at UNC Chapel Hill (2nd Shift) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) UTS - Temporary Electronics Specialist at UNC Chapel Hill (2nd Shift) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number PG194838TM Position Number 48CK21 Position Type Temporary Essential Job Duties This position serves as part of the Life Safety/Electronics-Specialty Shop team, ensuring the smooth operation of critical safety and monitoring systems across campus. The role involves both preventive maintenance and hands-on installations or modifications to essential systems that support the safety, security, and functionality of the university. As an Electronics Specialist, you will perform tasks such as: Conducting routine and preventive maintenance inspections on: Life Safety Systems Fire Detection and Suppression Systems Security Systems CCTV (Closed-Circuit Television) Systems Equipment Monitoring Systems Other miscellaneous electronic systems and subsystems Installing, maintaining, and modifying fire detection and suppression systems, Life Safety equipment, card access systems, CCTV , and equipment monitoring tools. Responding to repair requests and troubleshooting issues with various electronic components to ensure systems operate at peak performance. Coordinating with other teams and vendors to guarantee timely inspections and installations. Schedule of M-F 4:00 pm to 12:30 am (2nd Shift) Is Time Limited Yes If Yes, Appointment Length Wolfpack Perks and Benefits Department Information Job City & State Chapel Hill, NC Department System Information Classification Title Temporary-Professional NonFaculty Working Title UTS - Temporary Electronics Specialist at UNC Chapel Hill (2nd Shift) Position Information Requirements and Preferences Work Schedule M-F,  4:00 pm to 12:30 am 100% on site Other Work/Responsibilities N/A Minimum Experience/Education High School Diploma or completion of GED Department Required Skills Experience working with security systems, and CCTV systems . Strong problem-solving skills and ability to troubleshoot electronic systems. Knowledge of safety codes and regulations related to Life Safety systems is preferred. Ability to collaborate effectively with colleagues, contractors, and vendors. Preferred Years Experience, Skills, Training, Education Experience working with fire alarm systems Required License or Certification N/A Valid NC Driver's License required? No Commercial Driver's License Required? No Recruitment Recruitment Details Anticipated Hiring Range $26.44 an hour Recruitment Dates Job Open Date 01/14/2025 Applicant Information Quick Link https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/213795 EEO NC State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal opportunities for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, and veteran status. The University encourages all qualified applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities, to apply. Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodations in the application and interview process are welcome to contact 919-513-0574 to speak with a representative of the Office of Equal Opportunity. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at (919) 515-2135 or workatncstate@ncsu.edu . Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. Degree(s) must be obtained prior to start date in order to meet qualifications and receive credit. NC State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Contact Information for References Optional Documents Cover Letter NC STATE UNIVERSITY RALEIGH, NC 27695 PHONE: (919) 515-2011 Privacy Accessibility Emergency Information Policies NC State Home © 2019 NC State University. All rights reserved To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
