    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/233524": {
      "title": "Clinical Research Technician – Small Animal Surgery",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | Clinical Research Technician – Small Animal Surgery Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) Clinical Research Technician – Small Animal Surgery Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. In addition to your completed application, please attach a cover letter, resume, and contact information for at least three professional references. Posting Details Job Posting Information Posting Number PG195150SP Internal Recruitment No Working Title Clinical Research Technician – Small Animal Surgery Anticipated Hiring Range $45,000 - $50,000 Work Schedule Monday - Friday, between the hours of 8am to 5pm, with occasional flexibility depending on study needs, cadaveric research sessions, or clinical research activities. Job Location Raleigh, NC Department Department of Clinical Sciences About the Department The Small Animal Surgery Service within the Department of Clinical Sciences supports the clinical, research, and educational missions of the College of Veterinary Medicine. Research activities include surgical oncology, orthopedic surgery, minimally invasive surgery, interventional procedures, and other areas of small animal clinical and translational research. Wolfpack Perks and Benefits As a Pack member, you belong here, and can enjoy exclusive perks designed to enhance your personal and professional well-being. As you consider this opportunity, we encourage you to review our Employee Value Proposition and learn more about what makes NC State the best place to learn and work for everyone. What we offer: Medical , Dental , and Vision Flexible Spending Account Retirement Programs Disability Plans Life Insurance Accident Plan Paid Time Off and Other Leave Programs 12 Holidays Each Year Tuition and Academic Assistance And so much more! Attain Work-life balance with our Childcare benefits, Wellness & Recreation Membership , and Wellness Programs that aim to build a thriving wolfpack community. Disclaimer: Perks and Benefit eligibility is based on Part-Time or Full-Time Employment status. Eligibility and Employer Sponsored Plans can be found within each of the links offered. Essential Job Duties Join a collaborative clinical and surgical research team dedicated to advancing veterinary medicine through high-quality research. Working with Dr. Bae and Dr. McPhetridge, the Research Technician provides critical technical, administrative, and operational support that helps ensure the successful execution of multiple active research studies. This position plays an integral role in coordinating research activities, maintaining accurate data and regulatory records, and supporting studies from planning through completion while contributing to the overall success of the research program. Key Responsibilities Research Coordination & Study Management Coordinate prospective and retrospective clinical research studies, ensuring research activities are organized, completed on schedule, and conducted in accordance with study protocols. Perform medical record reviews, collect research data, maintain study databases, and coordinate owner questionnaires and follow-up communications to support accurate and complete data collection. Research Operations & Regulatory Support Coordinate and support cadaveric research activities while assisting with regulatory documentation and study compliance requirements. Manage research purchasing, inventory, and supply coordination to support the day-to-day operational needs of multiple active research projects. Collaboration & Administrative Support Partner with clinicians, residents, students, staff, and pet owners to facilitate research activities and ensure effective communication throughout the research process. Maintain organized research records, support confidential data management, and provide administrative and operational assistance that contributes to the overall efficiency of the research program. If you are a highly organized professional who enjoys supporting collaborative research, managing multiple priorities, and working closely with clinicians, researchers, students, and clients, we encourage you to apply. If you have strong attention to detail, excellent communication skills, and are committed to advancing veterinary clinical research through accurate, organized, and compliant study coordination, we’d love to have you join our team. Other Responsibilities Qualifications Minimum Experience/Education Demonstrated possession of the competencies necessary to perform the work. Preferred Qualifications RVT Strong organizational skills with exceptional attention to detail and the ability to manage multiple projects simultaneously. Excellent professional communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to collaborate effectively with clinicians, residents, students, staff, and pet owners. Experience using Microsoft Excel, REDCap, or similar database management tools, with the ability to maintain accurate and confidential clinical research records. Experience in veterinary clinical research, veterinary hospital operations, retrospective medical record review, owner/client communication, research purchasing and inventory management, and coordination of cadaveric or laboratory-based research projects. Required License or Certification N/A Valid NC Driver's License required No Commercial Driver's License Required? No Recruitment Dates and Special Instructions Job Open Date 08/04/2026 Earliest Close Date---- (Positions will be posted until 5:00 PM ET on this date. Positions remaining posted after this date are still accepting applications but may close at any time.) 08/11/2026 Notice to Applicants Please note that the work history on your resume must also be included in your application. Special Instructions In addition to your completed application, please attach a cover letter, resume, and contact information for at least three professional references. Position Details Position Number 00112227 Position Type SHRA Position Classification Band Title Research Technician Position Classification Band Level Journey Position Classification Salary Range $ 34,320  -  $ 72,734 Salary Grade Equivalency MH06 Alternate Option If no applicants apply who meet the required competency level and training & experience requirements, then management may consider other applicants. Salary would be determined based on competencies, equity, budget, and market considerations. Full Time Equivalent (FTE) (1.0 = 40 hours/week) 1.0 Appointment 12 Month Recurring Mandatory Designation - Adverse Weather Non Mandatory - Adverse Weather Mandatory Designation - Emergency Events Non Mandatory - Emergency Event Time Limited Position Yes Time-Limited Appointment Length (if applicable) 2 years, with possibility of extension depending on funding Department Id 195001 - Department of Clinical Sciences EEO NC State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal opportunities for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, and veteran status. The University encourages all qualified applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities, to apply. Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodations in the application and interview process are welcome to contact 919-513-0574 to speak with a representative of the Office of Equal Opportunity. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at (919) 515-2135 or workatncstate@ncsu.edu . Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. Degree(s) must be obtained prior to start date in order to meet qualifications and receive credit. NC State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn of this opportunity? NCSU Website NCSU Executive Search Services Monster.com CareerBuilder.com InsideHigherEd.com Other Online Job Board Carolina Job Finder / Employment Guide Job / Career Fair The Chronicle of Higher Education HERC Professional Journal Print Advertisement (Newspaper / Periodical) Professional Organization Direct Contact from NCSU HR Representative / Recruiter NCSU Employee Referral Social Media (LinkedIn, Twitter, Facebook, Other) Other If you learned about this vacancy from \"other source\" or \"other website\", please provide the source. (Open Ended Question) * Do you have previous Research Technician experience? Yes No Application Materials Required Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Contact Information for References Optional Documents NC STATE UNIVERSITY RALEIGH, NC 27695 PHONE: (919) 515-2011 Privacy Accessibility Emergency Information Policies NC State Home © 2019 NC State University. All rights reserved To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/223316": {
      "title": "Open Rank Non Tenure Track in Media Arts, Design and Technology",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | Open Rank Non Tenure Track in Media Arts, Design and Technology Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) Open Rank Non Tenure Track in Media Arts, Design and Technology Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applicants should attach a resume/CV, cover letter, and contact information for three references to online application. Portfolios must be made available upon request. Posting Details Posting Information Posting Number PG192554EP Internal Recruitment No Working Title Open Rank Non Tenure Track in Media Arts, Design and Technology Anticipated Hiring Range Dependent upon course load Work Schedule Varies depending on course schedule Job Location Raleigh, NC Department Media Arts, Design and Technology About the Department The Department of Media Arts Design and Technology is positioned within the College of Design at North Carolina State University, with allied academic departments of Graphic and Industrial Design, Landscape Architecture, and the School of Architecture. The Department of Media Arts, Design and Technology offers two undergraduate degree programs, the studio-based Bachelor of Art and Design and the non-studio-based Bachelor of Arts in Design Studies, and a Master of Art and Design. Students in our studio-based bachelor and master’s program engage in narrative and storytelling through a number of media and platforms including Mixed Media, Animation, VR/AR, Interaction Design, Illustration, and wearable technologies. Students in our Design Studies program engage in critical design issues shaping the field and practice of design through design research, writing and criticism. Students and faculty in Media Arts, Design and Technology seek opportunities and challenge the status quo through technological possibility, materiality, and look locally, nationally and globally for inspiration, application and impact. The Design Studies program in the Media Arts Design and Technology (MADTech) Department is known for its innovative interdisciplinary research and broad-based professional design education. Wolfpack Perks and Benefits As a Pack member, you belong here, and can enjoy exclusive perks designed to enhance your personal and professional well-being. What we offer: Medical , Dental , and Vision Flexible Spending Account Retirement Programs Disability Plans Life Insurance Accident Plan Paid Time Off and Other Leave Programs 12 Holidays Each Year Tuition and Academic Assistance And so much more! Attain Work-life balance with our Childcare benefits, Wellness & Recreation Membership , and Wellness Programs that aim to build a thriving wolfpack community. Disclaimer: Perks and Benefit eligibility is based on Part-Time or Full-Time Employment status. Eligibility and Employer Sponsored Plans can be found within each of the links offered. Essential Job Duties The Department of Media Arts, Design and Technology is accepting applications for part-time non-tenure-track faculty appointments for a one-semester or one-year appointment with the possibility of renewal. Rank to be determined based upon education and professional experience. Specific teaching opportunities include art studios at all levels, including advanced comprehensive studios and/or special topic seminar courses. Applications will be reviewed as these part-time non-tenure-track teaching opportunities arise. Other Responsibilities Appointments may be available on a semester or academic year basis, with the possibility of renewal. Other duties as assigned. Qualifications Minimum Education and Experience Terminal Master’s degree in a field relevant to the specific area of instruction (i.e. Art, Design, other art-related course), or relevant master’s degree with professional practice in that related field. Other Required Qualifications Demonstrated ability or aptitude in the areas specific to the courses to be taught. Demonstrated potential for directing activities specific to the courses to be taught. Ability and willingness to participate in departmental and University affairs. Demonstrated leadership in the professional field and community. MAD Tech Studio Faculty Applicants: Demonstrated professional or scholarly competency with a mix of traditional and leading-edge technologies and methods. Design Studies Faculty Applicants Skills: Ability to teach design theory, design writing, and design research Demonstrated professional or scholarly competency with a mix of research, writing, and practical application. Preferred Qualifications Experience in teaching at the college level Digital and computer-based coding skills Required License(s) or Certification(s) N/A Valid NC Driver's License required No Commercial Driver's License required No Recruitment Dates and Special Instructions Job Open Date 05/03/2023 Anticipated Close Date Open Until Filled Special Instructions to Applicants Applicants should attach a resume/CV, cover letter, and contact information for three references to online application. Portfolios must be made available upon request. Position Details Position Number 12ADN05 Position Type Non-Tenure-Track Faculty Full Time Equivalent (FTE) (1.0 = 40 hours/week) .225 -1.0 FTE Appointment < 9 Months Recurring Mandatory Designation - Adverse Weather Non Mandatory - Adverse Weather Mandatory Designation - Emergency Events Non Mandatory - Emergency Event Department ID 120501 - Art and Design EEO NC State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal opportunities for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, and veteran status. The University encourages all qualified applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities, to apply. Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodations in the application and interview process are welcome to contact 919-513-0574 to speak with a representative of the Office of Equal Opportunity. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at (919) 515-2135 or workatncstate@ncsu.edu . Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. Degree(s) must be obtained prior to start date in order to meet qualifications and receive credit. NC State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn of this opportunity? NCSU Website Job Alert (automated email from our system) NCSU Executive Search Services Monster.com CareerBuilder.com InsideHigherEd.com HigherEdJobs.com Other Online Job Board Carolina Job Finder / Employment Guide Job / Career Fair The Chronicle of Higher Education Professional Journal Print Advertisement (Newspaper / Periodical) Radio / Television Advertisement Professional Organization Higher Education Recruitment Consortium (HERC) Direct Contact from NCSU HR Representative / Recruiter NCSU Employee Referral Social Media (LinkedIn, Twitter, Facebook, Other) Other * If you learned about this vacancy from \"other source\" or \"other website\", please provide the source. (Open Ended Question) Do you have doctor's degree, an equivalent degree, or equivalent professional experience? Yes No Application Materials Required Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Contact Information for References Optional Documents NC STATE UNIVERSITY RALEIGH, NC 27695 PHONE: (919) 515-2011 Privacy Accessibility Emergency Information Policies NC State Home © 2019 NC State University. All rights reserved To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
