    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/234301": {
      "title": "Temporary Financial Operations Specialist",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | Temporary Financial Operations Specialist Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) Temporary Financial Operations Specialist Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Attach: Cover letter Resume Contact information for at least 3 references Posting Details Position Information Posting Number PG196176TM Position Number 11ASO3751 Position Type Temporary Essential Job Duties The Temporary Financial Operations Specialist provides accounting and financial operations support within the College of Agriculture and Life Sciences ( CALS ) Business Services unit. Business Services is transitioning to a cross-functional service model in which employees develop proficiency across multiple financial operations functions. Employees will support Accounts Payable, Accounts Receivable, Travel, and Procurement Card (PCard) operations and may be assigned primary responsibilities based on operational needs. Work assignments may shift across functional areas to support workload balancing, team coverage, and continuity of business operations. Primary Responsibilities: Process and support Accounts Payable, Accounts Receivable, Travel, and Procurement Card (PCard) transactions, as assigned. Process, review, reconcile, and analyze financial transactions for accuracy, completeness, and compliance with university policies and procedures. Apply accounting principles and established business processes to transactions across multiple funding sources. Review financial activity for appropriate documentation, classification, and compliance with applicable university, state, federal, and sponsor requirements. Research and resolve transaction discrepancies while maintaining accurate financial records and supporting documentation. Assist with financial monitoring, reconciliation, reporting activities, and audit support. Utilize university financial systems, including PeopleSoft, ServiceNow, and reporting tools, to process, review, and monitor financial activity. Provide customer service and guidance to departments regarding financial processes, documentation requirements, and transaction status. Collaborate with campus partners to resolve financial issues and support efficient business operations. Identify opportunities to improve processes, strengthen internal controls, and enhance operational effectiveness. Participate in cross-training and provide backup coverage across Business Services functions as operational needs require. Perform other duties as assigned Is Time Limited No If Yes, Appointment Length Wolfpack Perks and Benefits As a Pack member, you belong here, and can enjoy exclusive perks designed to enhance your personal and professional well-being. As you consider this opportunity, we encourage you to review our Employee Value Proposition and learn more about what makes NC State the best place to learn and work for everyone. What we offer: Health Insurance for Temporary Employees Enhance your career with LEAD courses Attend non-revenue generating sporting events for free. Attain Work-life balance with our Childcare discounts , Wellness & Recreation Membership , and Wellness Programs that aim to build a thriving wolfpack community. Disclaimer: Perks and Benefit eligibility is based on Part-Time or Full-Time Employment status. Eligibility and Employer Sponsored Plans can be found within each of the links offered. Department Information Job City & State Raleigh, NC Department CBO System Information Classification Title Temporary-Technical/Paraprofessional Working Title Temporary Financial Operations Specialist Position Information Requirements and Preferences Work Schedule 40/hrs per week between Monday-Friday, 8am-5pm Other Work/Responsibilities n/a Minimum Experience/Education Bachelor’s degree in business administration or accounting; or Associate’s degree in business administration or accounting and one year of experience or equivalent combination of training and experience. Department Required Skills Knowledge of basic accounting principles. Experience with financial systems (PeopleSoft or similar). Strong organizational skills and ability to manage high transaction volume and competing priorities. Ability to work independently with accuracy, attention to details, timeliness, and professionalism. Preferred Years Experience, Skills, Training, Education Experience in a research-intensive higher education or state institution. Knowledge of University financial policies and compliance requirements. Experience providing accounting guidance or training to non-financial personnel. Proficiency with reporting tools, Excel, and enterprise financial systems such as  PeopleSoft Financial System. Experience managing multiple funding sources and sponsored programs. Required License or Certification n/a Valid NC Driver's License required? No Commercial Driver's License Required? No Recruitment Recruitment Details Anticipated Hiring Range $25/hr Recruitment Dates Job Open Date 08/28/2026 Applicant Information Quick Link https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/234151 EEO NC State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal opportunities for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, and veteran status. The University encourages all qualified applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities, to apply. Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodations in the application and interview process are welcome to contact 919-513-0574 to speak with a representative of the Office of Equal Opportunity. If you have general