    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/234605": {
      "title": "Position Information",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | Student Success Navigators  for Elevate (IPSE) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) Student Success Navigators  for Elevate (IPSE) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. N/A Posting Details Position Information Posting Number PG195829TM Position Number 13JGM45 Position Type Temporary Essential Job Duties Note: This position is open only to currently enrolled NC State students who are in good academic standing. Primary purpose of this position: NC State’s inclusive postsecondary education program for students with intellectual and developmental disabilities, Elevate is seeking a motivated and reliable Student Success Navigator to support in study halls, courses to promote self-determined learning among Elevate students. This role provides the opportunity to support students individually and in small groups in developing skills such as time management, navigation, and assignment completion. Job Responsibilities: Provide 5 to 15 hours per week of support, including academic and social mentoring responsibilities Provide individualized academic support in study sessions and Elevate program or inclusive Courses Provide individualized support during Elevate’s Living Learning class or workshops Assist students with navigation, assignment planning, and time management, including use of Google Suite tools and other mobile applications Support Elevate students with independent living, social goal, and academic goal attainment including attending events/ activities and facilitating event/ activity registration Document activities completed with Elevate students, as instructed by Elevate staff Participate in trainings led by Social or Academic Peer Coaches or Elevate program staff Clearly communicate availability and provide adequate notice if scheduling conflicts arise Opportunities to serve as a job coach for on campus student employment internship(s) Eligibility Requirements: Must be an undergraduate or graduate student currently enrolled at NC State University Strong academic, organizational, and interpersonal skills Must have a passion for inclusion Proficiency with Google Suite tools and digital scheduling and communication mechanisms used by the Elevate program Is Time Limited Yes If Yes, Appointment Length August 16, 2026 -May 15th, 2027 Wolfpack Perks and Benefits Department Information Job City & State Raleigh, NC Department IPSE's Elevate Program System Information Classification Title Temporary-Technical/Paraprofessional Working Title Student Success Navigators  for Elevate (IPSE) Position Information Requirements and Preferences Work Schedule Schedule: 5 to 15 hours per week Other Work/Responsibilities Minimum Experience/Education Eligibility Requirements: Must be an undergraduate or graduate student currently enrolled at NC State University Strong academic, organizational, and interpersonal skills Must have a passion for inclusion Proficiency with Google Suite tools and digital scheduling and communication mechanisms used by the Elevate program Department Required Skills Job Responsibilities: Provide 5 to 15 hours per week of support, including academic and social mentoring responsibilities Provide individualized academic support in study sessions and Elevate program or inclusive Courses Provide individualized support during Elevate’s Living Learning class or workshops Assist students with navigation, assignment planning, and time management, including use of Google Suite tools and other mobile applications Support Elevate students with independent living, social goal, and academic goal attainment including attending events/ activities and facilitating event/ activity registration Document activities completed with Elevate students, as instructed by Elevate staff Participate in trainings led by Social or Academic Peer Coaches or Elevate program staff Clearly communicate availability and provide adequate notice if scheduling conflicts arise Opportunities to serve as a job coach for on campus student employment internship(s) Eligibility Requirements: Must be an undergraduate or graduate student currently enrolled at NC State University Strong academic, organizational, and interpersonal skills Must have a passion for inclusion Proficiency with Google Suite tools and digital scheduling and communication mechanisms used by the Elevate program Preferred Years Experience, Skills, Training, Education N/A Required License or Certification N.A Valid NC Driver's License required? No Commercial Driver's License Required? No Recruitment Recruitment Details Anticipated Hiring Range $15/hour Recruitment Dates Job Open Date 08/18/2026 Applicant Information Quick Link https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/228098 EEO NC State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal opportunities for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, and veteran status. The University encourages all qualified applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities, to apply. Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodations in the application and interview process are welcome to contact 919-513-0574 to speak with a representative of the Office of Equal Opportunity. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at (919) 515-2135 or workatncstate@ncsu.edu . Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. Degree(s) must be obtained prior to start date in order to meet qualifications and receive credit. NC State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a full time NCSU student in good academic standing? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Contact Information for References Optional Documents Cover Letter NC STATE UNIVERSITY RALEIGH, NC 27695 PHONE: (919) 515-2011 Privacy Accessibility Emergency Information Policies NC State Home © 2019 NC State University. All rights reserved To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
