    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/234524": {
      "title": "Associate Vice Chancellor, Integrated Strategic Communications",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | Associate Vice Chancellor, Integrated Strategic Communications Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) Associate Vice Chancellor, Integrated Strategic Communications Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please include a resume, cover letter, contact information for at least three professional references and a writing example as a part of your application materials. Inquiries may be directed to Meena Raghavan, Recruiter, Talent Acquisition, at 919-513-5921 or mraghav3@ncsu.edu Posting Details Posting Information Posting Number PG194684EP Internal Recruitment No Working Title Associate Vice Chancellor, Integrated Strategic Communications Anticipated Hiring Range Commensurate with Education and Experience Work Schedule Core Business Hours are Monday - Friday; 8:00 AM - 5:00 PM Job Location Raleigh, NC Department Chancellor's Office And Staff About the Department University Communications and Marketing is the central agency responsible for shaping and sharing the story of NC State University. As the stewards of the NC State brand, we drive the university’s reputation and visibility through integrated marketing, strategic communications, and digital engagement. We are a team of creators, strategists, and problem-solvers dedicated to the “Think and Do” spirit. We collaborate across the university to elevate NC State’s profile as a premier public research institution, supporting enrollment, research, alumni engagement, and institutional prestige. What we do: Increase awareness and preference of the university’s distinctive benefits Create consistency in university wide messaging and the brand platform including visual identity Provide support for public relations and communications efforts across the institution Develop rapid, thoughtful engagement with emerging issues and crisis communications Develop effective marketing, graphic design, communication and web strategy, creative services and professional counsel for campus partners Support a strong and cohesive culture throughout the university Wolfpack Perks and Benefits As a Pack member, you belong here, and can enjoy exclusive perks designed to enhance your personal and professional well-being. As you consider this opportunity, we encourage you to review our Employee Value Proposition and learn more about what makes NC State the best place to learn and work for everyone. What we offer: Medical , Dental , and Vision Flexible Spending Account Retirement Programs Disability Plans Life Insurance Accident Plan Paid Time Off and Other Leave Programs 12 Holidays Each Year Tuition and Academic Assistance And so much more! Attain Work-life balance with our Childcare benefits, Wellness & Recreation Membership , and Wellness Programs that aim to build a thriving wolfpack community. Disclaimer: Perks and Benefit eligibility is based on Part-Time or Full-Time Employment status. Eligibility and Employer Sponsored Plans can be found within each of the links offered. Essential Job Duties This is a repost: Previous applicants need not reapply We are seeking a collaborative leader with significant experience leading strategic communications, media relations, and reputation management within complex, high-visibility organizations. This executive role serves as a university’s spokesperson and primary reputation promoter and guardian, shaping how NC State engages with news media, navigates complex issues, and translates research and institutional impact into clear public understanding. This is a role where steady judgment, sound decision-making, and clear communication in fast-moving, high-pressure environments are essential. As a leader in this position, you will build trust through transparency and consistency when circumstances are evolving and visibility is high. You will foster alignment across internal partners, media, and executive stakeholders, ensuring clarity in moments of complexity and providing confident direction that strengthens institutional credibility and response. Through a responsive, relationship-driven approach, you will strengthen the university’s readiness and performance in high-stakes environments. You will build and sustain a robust network of media relationships at the local, national, and global level—securing credible earned coverage that positions NC State as a trusted source of expertise and innovation. Overseeing Public Relations, Strategic Communications and Media, and Research Communications, you ensure the university’s “Think and Do” impact is communicated with clarity, coherence, and purpose. Key responsibilities fall within the five core functional areas outlined below. Strategic Media Relations & Brand Visibility Build and sustain relationships with local, national, and international media to elevate NC State expertise and research. Lead proactive storytelling that highlights student success, faculty achievement, and institutional and research impact. Oversee news operations, ensuring timely, accurate, and high-quality news content. Issues Management & Crisis Communications Lead crisis and issues management with clarity and composure in high-pressure situations. Advise university leadership on emerging issues, reputational risk, and sensitive communications. Coordinate cross-campus response to ensure aligned and consistent messaging during critical incidents. Research Communications & Impact Storytelling Translate complex research into clear, compelling narratives that demonstrate public value. Partner with research leadership to increase visibility in prestige, trade, and industry media. Executive Communications & Thought Leadership Shape leadership messaging, including speeches, op-eds, and institutional narratives. Align executive communications with broader reputation and media strategy to ensure consistency and trust. Collaboration & Culture Collaborate and partner closely with the AVC for Brand and Integrated Strategic Operations and the AVC for Integrated Content Strategy Develops and mentors team, with a strong focus on division-wide culture If you are a communications leader who thrives in complex, high-visibility environments and is motivated by shaping how a major institution is understood, trusted, and represented in the public sphere, we encourage you to apply. Other Responsibilities In addition to the core responsibilities of this role, there will be opportunities to represent the division through engagement with a wide range of internal and external constituents, including university leadership, public officials, representatives from the UNC System and peer institutions, students, parents, alumni, faculty, staff, and members of the public. These opportunities will be assigned in collaboration with the Vice Chancellor of Communications and Marketing in support of evolving departmental and institutional priorities. Qualifications Minimum Education and Experience Post-baccalaureate degree in Journalism, Communications, Public Relations or a related field; or a Bachelor’s degree with equivalent broad-based independent experience in executive-level strategic communications. An equivalent combination of education and experience may be substituted for the advanced degree. Minimum of 10 years of progressive experience in communications, public relations, or related field, with at least 5 years in leadership role(s). Other Required Qualifications Demonstrated ability to synthesize complex information (such as scientific research or crisis scenarios) into clear, compelling narratives for varied audiences. Proven mastery in managing high-stakes issues and crisis communications, with a track record of maintaining organizational trust and clarity under pressure. Established history of cultivating trust-based relationships with media and influencers; ability to leverage these networks to secure high-impact earned media. Demonstrated skill in providing candid, strategic counsel to C-suite executives or senior government officials regarding sensitive public relations matters. Proven ability to lead and integrate varied teams (e.g., former journalists, science writers, crisis managers) toward shared strategic goals Demonstrated experience leading or supporting organizational change in complex environments, including aligning teams, communicating transitions clearly, and sustaining performance during periods of strategic or operational shift. Preferred Qualifications Experience working within a Research 1 (R1) university or a science/technology-focused organization, with specific skill in communicating STEM topics to lay audiences. Proficiency in integrating social media listening and digital engagement tools into crisis response and reputation management strategies. Experience navigating the intersection of public relations, government affairs, and higher education policy. Required License(s) or Certification(s) N/A Valid NC Driver's License required No Commercial Driver's License required No Recruitment Dates and Special Instructions Job Open Date 08/27/2026 Anticipated Close Date 9/09/2026; if posting is active we are still accepting and reviewing applications. Special Instructions to Applicants Please include a resume, cover letter, contact information for at least three professional references and a writing example as a part of your application materials. Inquiries may be directed to Meena Raghavan, Recruiter, Talent Acquisition, at 919-513-5921 or mraghav3@ncsu.edu Position Details Position Number 00112065 Position Type EPS/SAAO Full Time Equivalent (FTE) (1.0 = 40 hours/week) 1.0 Appointment 12 Month Recurring Mandatory Designation - Adverse Weather Non Mandatory - Adverse Weather Mandatory Designation - Emergency Events Non Mandatory - Emergency Event Department ID 010101 - Chancellor's Office And Staff EEO NC State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal opportunities for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, and veteran status. The University encourages all qualified applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities, to apply. Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodations in the application and interview process are welcome to contact 919-513-0574 to speak with a representative of the Office of Equal Opportunity. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at (919) 515-2135 or workatncstate@ncsu.edu . Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. Degree(s) must be obtained prior to start date in order to meet qualifications and receive credit. NC State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn of this opportunity? NCSU website Craigslist Indeed.com Carolina Job Finder/Employment Guide NC Works Dress for Success Technical/Trade School Program Job Fair (Identify Job Fair in question #2 below) Direct Contact from NSCU Representative (identify person in question #2 below) Other Monster.com Other online job board NCSU employee referral Social Media (LinkedIn, Twitter, Facebook, Ohter) If you learned about this vacancy from \"other source\" or \"other website\", please provide the source. (Open Ended Question) Briefly describe your experience leading earned media strategy and building relationships with journalists or editorial leaders. What types of outlets and coverage outcomes were you responsible for? (Open Ended Question) Provide an example of a high-stakes or reputational issue you managed or supported. What was your role in shaping the response, and what was the outcome? (Open Ended Question) Application Materials Required Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Contact Information for References Short Writing Sample Optional Documents NC STATE UNIVERSITY RALEIGH, NC 27695 PHONE: (919) 515-2011 Privacy Accessibility Emergency Information Policies NC State Home © 2019 NC State University. All rights reserved To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
