    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/229449": {
      "title": "Position Information",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | Equine and Farm Animal Attendant (weekends, afterhours) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) Equine and Farm Animal Attendant (weekends, afterhours) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number PG195908TM Position Number 19PLS05728 Position Type Temporary Essential Job Duties This temporary position will be responsible for maintaining a clean and sanitary hospital through routine stall/cage maintenance, hospital cleaning and disinfection, and waste removal. Restrain and provide basic husbandry for equine and farm animal patients. Small animal hospital backup, same duties. Is Time Limited No If Yes, Appointment Length Wolfpack Perks and Benefits As a Pack member, you belong here , and can enjoy exclusive perks designed to enhance your personal and professional well-being. As you consider this opportunity, we encourage you to review our Employee Value Proposition and learn more about what makes NC State the best place to learn and work for everyone. What we offer: Health Insurance for Temporary Employees Enhance your career with LEAD courses Attend non-revenue generating sporting events for free. Attain Work-life balance with our Childcare discounts , Wellness & Recreation Membership , and Wellness Programs that aim to build a thriving wolfpack community. Disclaimer: Perks and Benefit eligibility is based on Part-Time or Full-Time Employment status. Eligibility and Employer Sponsored Plans can be found within each of the links offered. Department Information Job City & State Raleigh, NC Department System Information Classification Title Temporary-Skilled Trades Working Title Equine and Farm Animal Attendant (weekends, afterhours) Position Information Requirements and Preferences Work Schedule Sat - Tues, 4:00 PM - 3:00 AM Other Work/Responsibilities N/A Minimum Experience/Education High School diploma or equivalent. Demonstrated experience in the handling and restraint of equine patients, including mares with foals, pregnant mares, and stallions, as well as othr farm animals. Proficiency in animal husbandry practices, cleaning and disinfection protocols, and basic facility maintneance skills are also required. Department Required Skills Must be able to lift up to 70 pounds. Ability to operate equipment such as forklifts, pressure washers, and basic power tools. Responsible for inventory management and accurately measuring and diluting chemicals according to established guidelines. Demonstrates safe, humane handling of all patients at all times. Must communicate effectively, work collaboratively within a team, and comply with all institutional policies and procedures, including safety requirements. Ability to commute to Reedy Creek Equine Farm to provide care. Preferred Years Experience, Skills, Training, Education Experience in restraining and providing husbandry care for equine and Farm Animal species is required. Preferred qualifications include prior experience working in a veterinary setting, working knowledge of infectious disease control programs, and familiarity with established safety programs. Candidates should demonstrate compliance with OSHA standards and awareness of veterinary accreditation and certification guidelines such as AAHA , AVMA , and related regulatory bodies. Required License or Certification Must have a valid NC driver’s license Valid NC Driver's License required? Yes Commercial Driver's License Required? No Recruitment Recruitment Details Anticipated Hiring Range $15.00 - $18.75 Recruitment Dates Job Open Date 04/13/2026 Applicant Information Quick Link https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/229448 EEO NC State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal opportunities for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, and veteran status. The University encourages all qualified applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities, to apply. Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodations in the application and interview process are welcome to contact 919-513-0574 to speak with a representative of the Office of Equal Opportunity. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at (919) 515-2135 or workatncstate@ncsu.edu. Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. Degree(s) must be obtained prior to start date in order to meet qualifications and receive credit. NC State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have experience handling and caring for horses? Yes No * Please describe any experience you have with equine and/or large animal care/animal husbandry you have. (Open Ended Question) Do you have experience operating a forklift, pressure washer and other basic power tools? (Open Ended Question) Do you have a valid NC driver's license or the ability to obtain one within 30 days of start date? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Contact Information for References Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter NC STATE UNIVERSITY RALEIGH, NC 27695 PHONE: (919) 515-2011 Privacy Accessibility Emergency Information Policies NC State Home © 2019 NC State University. All rights reserved To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
