    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/234535": {
      "title": "IT Manager, Student Information System",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | IT Manager, Student Information System Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) IT Manager, Student Information System Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please include a resume, cover letter and contact information for at least three professional references. This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Applicants must be authorized to work in the United States without the need for current or future sponsorship. Posting Details Posting Information Posting Number PG194837EP Internal Recruitment No Working Title IT Manager, Student Information System Anticipated Hiring Range Commensurate with experience Work Schedule Standard business hours M-F with some nights and weekends as necessary Job Location Raleigh, NC Department Enterprise Application Services About the Department Enterprise Application Services ( EAS ) is in the Office of Information Technology ( OIT ) division at North Carolina State University. EAS is responsible for the design, implementation, operation, enhancement & maintenance of the University’s enterprise business applications. This includes: development, operation & maintenance of enterprise administrative systems (Faculty Excellence (FE Portal), Financials, HR, Lab Management, MyPack Portal, Non-Credit ( REPORTER ), Research Administration ( RED ), and Student Information Systems, etc.), configuration management, database administration, maintenance, enhancements, and application integration. Wolfpack Perks and Benefits As a Pack member, you belong here, and can enjoy exclusive perks designed to enhance your personal and professional well-being. As you consider this opportunity, we encourage you to review our Employee Value Proposition and learn more about what makes NC State the best place to learn and work for everyone. What we offer: Medical , Dental , and Vision Flexible Spending Account Retirement Programs Disability Plans Life Insurance Accident Plan Paid Time Off and Other Leave Programs 12 Holidays Each Year Tuition and Academic Assistance And so much more! Attain Work-life balance with our Childcare benefits, Wellness & Recreation Membership , and Wellness Programs that aim to build a thriving wolfpack community. Disclaimer: Perks and Benefit eligibility is based on Part-Time or Full-Time Employment status. Eligibility and Employer Sponsored Plans can be found within each of the links offered. Essential Job Duties This position performs technical and functional duties associated with application development and provides managerial leadership within the EAS Student Information System ( SIS ) Team. It is responsible for ensuring exceptional customer service and support. Maintaining and enhancing the partnership between the IT systems and the central office business owners and campus community impacting over 50,000 customers of the Student Information System is a core expectation. This position requires an expert in business process analysis with highly advanced technical solution development skills needed to support highly complex systems and associated integrations across campus. Excellent verbal, written, organization and project management skills are essential. This team directly supports the SIS Financial Aid module in collaboration with the Office of Scholarships and Financial Aid and the SIS Student Financials module in collaboration with the University Cashier’s Office. This position leads initiatives of high complexity and is expected to interact with leadership positions in customer and IT units to ensure that developed solutions align with business needs. This position manages a team of application analysts performing business process analysis, change request evaluation, functional and technical specification development, coding, unit and system test development and execution, code migration, production support & system maintenance. Duties and Responsibilities Functional/Technical Knowledge & Leadership Working manager that participates and supervises a team of application analysts to design, build and/or implement practical, cost effective business solutions. These solutions must seamlessly integrate within a technically complex enterprise system that has broad and institution-wide impacts Research and/or develop new technologies and keep abreast of new technologies to evaluate feasibility for organizational needs Translate high level organizational goals into actionable technical plans and objectives Interpret complex financial and operational reports and data, explain complex business processes and technological functions, advise and inform/persuade data stewards and other policymaking bodies of the appropriate resource and technology solutions Provide technical leadership on various committees and task forces to address audits, disaster recovery, federal and state regulations, and security Ensure that application development efforts align closely with business requirements, from design to delivery, and that applications are user friendly, scalable, secure, and can be efficiently maintained once deployed Maintain a thorough knowledge of the assigned applications’ technical and functional capabilities and weaknesses Use persuasion and negotiation to build cooperation and consensus towards decision Work effectively across customers, technical teams, and the enterprise to understand and communicate requirements, status updates, issues, problems, and solutions with a focus on more detailed, “closer to the ground” issues Manage vendor relationships and escalate technical support within vendor organizations as needed Planning and Organizing Prepare and present detailed development and/or implementation plans for projects and monitor project status Coordinate long-term project planning for large development projects Make significant changes in the organizational structure, methods and procedures to respond to new goals and programs Plan for utilization of staff, equipment and other resources Ensure the development of internal policies and procedures Develop/ensure the development of, and give final approval to, unit rules, standards and guidelines governing quality and quantity of work Determine applicability in controversial or precedent-setting situations Determine budget needs and recommend, with significant influence, priorities based on program mission, costs and projected revenues Prepare comprehensive project plans that encompass the entire software development life cycle ( SDLC ); ensure these plans dovetail into larger plans as needed Maintain a strong knowledge of the SDLC at NC State University combined with outstanding organization and communication skills Maintain a deep understanding of software development project management methodologies and tools (Microsoft Project, QuickBase, Stat, etc.) and a thorough understanding of project expectations and procedures Strategic Development & Program Management Define business strategies and contribute to the enterprise’s vision (typically through participation in customer strategic planning) Determine needs and establish goals and objectives that incorporate a broad range of internal and external factors when solving problems and making decisions Clearly translate technical issues into understandable terms for audiences with varying degrees of technical expertise so that decisions can be reached; these audiences can include members from all levels of the university Recognize and act on strategic opportunities for success Weigh alternatives and consequences to make informed decisions on long-term operational issues Evaluate organizational readiness and capacity for change and adjust accordingly Continuously evaluate new technology and refine supported applications and solutions to align with customer needs and expectations Clearly communicate plans with current and potential project stakeholders, campus wide. Plan strategically for the adoption of application technologies and independently prioritizes the team’s work to best meet the immediate and long term goals of the university Maintain a clear understanding of the organization, the strengths and weaknesses of current processes and a clear understanding of larger organizational priorities Think creatively and communicate effectively in order to contribute in practical ways towards the growth and success of the organization and future strategies Human Resource Function Recruit, hire and supervise staff and direct the development, enhancement, and maintenance of workflow processes and application support for a varied group of entities Involve the director, other managers and staff in the development and establishment of long and short range goals and priorities for the department, including the development and maintenance of corresponding policies and procedures Facilitate the growth and development of team members Pursue disciplinary actions as needed Review accomplishments to assure that program missions and goals are being met Conduct final review for most difficult, controversial or sensitive work. Ensure team members understand concepts related to the organization’s policies Provide coaching, conduct annual performance reviews, and manage the total skill set of the unit. Actively seek resources and opportunities for employee training and growth Determine staffing needs and motivational techniques to build and maintain a productive and cohesive team Provide feedback and mentoring of staff to help them meet future goals and expectations Other Responsibilities Qualifications Minimum Education and Experience Master’s degree and at least two years’ of relevant experience; or Bachelor’s degree with at least three years’ of relevant experience; or an equivalent combination of education, training and relevant experience. 1‐2 years of supervisory experience. Other Required Qualifications Minimum of three (3) years of previous application development experience Experience with Oracle/PeopleSoft and/or Student Information Systems is preferred Preferred Qualifications Excellent verbal and written communication skills in both technical and non-technical subjects including the ability to communicate effectively at all levels of the organization Strong project management, organizational and time management skills with the ability to manage multiple projects concurrently, set team priorities, meet deadlines, conduct and direct research into IT issues and products, and to take initiative in the development and completion of projects Previous experience in a higher education institution Ability to build consensus among internal and external teams and persuade other decision-makers, make frequent presentations at customer meetings and correspond in writing and verbally to people at all levels of the university Ability to receive and provide constructive criticism when appropriate and mentor/train supervised managers and less experienced managers and team members as necessary Required License(s) or Certification(s) N/A Valid NC Driver's License required No Commercial Driver's License required No Recruitment Dates and Special Instructions Job Open Date 09/01/2026 Anticipated Close Date 9/16/2026; if posting is still active we are accepting and reviewing applications. Special Instructions to Applicants Please include a resume, cover letter and contact information for at least three professional references. This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Applicants must be authorized to work in the United States without the need for current or future sponsorship. Position Details Position Number 00065140 Position Type EPS/SAAO Full Time Equivalent (FTE) (1.0 = 40 hours/week) 1.0 Appointment 12 Month Recurring Mandatory Designation - Adverse Weather Mandatory - Adverse Weather Mandatory Designation - Emergency Events Mandatory - Fire/Explosions, Mandatory - Medical Emergencies, Mandatory - Hazardous Material Incidents, Mandatory - Transportation Accidents, Mandatory - Evacuations/Natural Hazards, Mandatory - Utilities/Infrastructure Failure, Mandatory - Threats of Violence/Terrorism/Interpersonal Emergencies Department ID 515001 - Enterprise Application Services EEO NC State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal opportunities for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, and veteran status. The University encourages all qualified applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities, to apply. Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodations in the application and interview process are welcome to contact 919-513-0574 to speak with a representative of the Office of Equal Opportunity. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at (919) 515-2135 or workatncstate@ncsu.edu . Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. Degree(s) must be obtained prior to start date in order to meet qualifications and receive credit. NC State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn of this opportunity? NCSU Website NCSU Executive Search Services Monster.com CareerBuilder.com InsideHigherEd.com Other Online Job Board Carolina Job Finder / Employment Guide Job / Career Fair The Chronicle of Higher Education HERC Professional Journal Print Advertisement (Newspaper / Periodical) Professional Organization Direct Contact from NCSU HR Representative / Recruiter NCSU Employee Referral Social Media (LinkedIn, Twitter, Facebook, Other) Other If you learned about this vacancy from \"other source\" or \"other website\", please provide the source. (Open Ended Question) Application Materials Required Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Contact Information for References Optional Documents NC STATE UNIVERSITY RALEIGH, NC 27695 PHONE: (919) 515-2011 Privacy Accessibility Emergency Information Policies NC State Home © 2019 NC State University. All rights reserved To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
