    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/234334": {
      "title": "Position Information",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | UTS - Temporary Graphic Designer at UNC Chapel Hill Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) UTS - Temporary Graphic Designer at UNC Chapel Hill Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number PG196174TM Position Number 48TT04 Position Type Temporary Essential Job Duties Is Time Limited Yes If Yes, Appointment Length 6 months to a year Wolfpack Perks and Benefits As a Pack member, you belong here, and can enjoy exclusive perks designed to enhance your personal and professional well-being. As you consider this opportunity, we encourage you to review our Employee Value Proposition and learn more about what makes NC State the best place to learn and work for everyone. What we offer: Health Insurance for Temporary Employees Enhance your career with LEAD courses Attend non-revenue generating sporting events for free. Attain Work-life balance with our Childcare discounts , Wellness & Recreation Membership , and Wellness Programs that aim to build a thriving wolfpack community. Disclaimer: Perks and Benefit eligibility is based on Part-Time or Full-Time Employment status. Eligibility and Employer Sponsored Plans can be found within each of the links offered. Department Information Job City & State Chapel Hill, NC Department System Information Classification Title Temporary-Technical/Paraprofessional Working Title UTS - Temporary Graphic Designer at UNC Chapel Hill Position Information Requirements and Preferences Work Schedule Monday-Friday, Onsite, 8:00 AM-5:00 PM Other Work/Responsibilities Key responsibilities include: Design and produce high-quality print and digital materials that support the department’s marketing, advancement, events, programs, and institutional priorities. Create and update event collateral, including invitations, save-the-dates, programs, signage, name badges, displays, donor materials, and related promotional pieces. Develop graphics for email campaigns, websites, social media, digital advertising, and other online communications. Design and format presentations, briefing materials, proposals, reports, sponsorship materials, and other advancement communications. Support creative needs associated with the department’s upcoming facility transformation, new exhibits, immersive technology, and major public and donor-facing initiatives. Translate project briefs, messaging, and content into compelling visual concepts that align with established UNC and department brand standards. Adapt existing designs and campaigns into multiple sizes, formats, and applications while maintaining visual consistency. Prepare production-ready files and coordinate specifications for commercial printing, signage, displays, and other physical installations. Edit, retouch, crop, and optimize photography and other visual assets for print and digital use. Maintain organized project files, editable source files, fonts, images, and final production assets to ensure materials can be easily accessed and reused by the organization. Work collaboratively with Advancement, Marketing, Programs, Guest Relations, and other department staff to understand project objectives and meet communications needs. Incorporate feedback and complete revisions efficiently, often within short production timelines. Provide design support for high-priority and time-sensitive projects as needs arise. Review finished materials for visual quality, brand consistency, accuracy, accessibility, and production readiness. Coordinate with external printers, vendors, photographers, or other creative partners when necessary. Help strengthen and maintain a consistent visual identity across the department’s expanding portfolio of communications and experiences. Perform other graphic design and creative production duties as assigned in support of the department’s mission and strategic priorities. Minimum Experience/Education 3-5 years of experience in graphic design Department Required Skills Strong graphic design and visual communication skills, with a portfolio demonstrating high-quality print and digital work. Proficiency in Adobe Creative Suite, particularly InDesign, Illustrator, Photoshop, and Acrobat Ability to work within established brand standards while creating fresh, engaging visual concepts. Experience designing event collateral, including invitations, signage, programs, presentations, digital displays, and promotional materials. Strong layout, typography, color, and composition skills Experience preparing files for professional printing and production, including bleed, crop, color profiles, and print specifications. Ability to create graphics optimized for web, email, social media, and digital advertising Experience creating or adapting PowerPoint presentation graphics and templates Ability to resize, reformat, and adapt creative assets efficiently across multiple platforms and formats. Strong attention to detail, particularly with proofreading, brand consistency, image quality, and production specifications. Ability to manage multiple projects and competing deadlines in a fast-paced environment Comfortable receiving feedback and making revisions quickly while maintaining design quality Strong organizational and file-management skills, including maintaining clear naming conventions and editable source files Ability to collaborate effectively with marketing, advancement, events, and program staff Demonstrated ability to take a creative brief or general concept and translate it into a polished visual product with limited supervision. Familiarity with accessible design practices and designing for varied audiences Photography, photo editing, illustration, motion graphics, or basic video-editing skills are desirable. Familiarity with Canva and other rapid-production design platforms is a plus Experience in higher education, museums, science organizations, nonprofits, fundraising, or cultural institutions is preferred. Preferred Years Experience, Skills, Training, Education N/A Required License or Certification N/A Valid NC Driver's License required? No Commercial Driver's License Required? No Recruitment Recruitment Details Anticipated Hiring Range $25.00 an hour Recruitment Dates Job Open Date 08/26/2026 Applicant Information Quick Link https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/234183 EEO NC State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal opportunities for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, and veteran status. The University encourages all qualified applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities, to apply. Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodations in the application and interview process are welcome to contact 919-513-0574 to speak with a representative of the Office of Equal Opportunity. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at (919) 515-2135 or workatncstate@ncsu.edu. Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. Degree(s) must be obtained prior to start date in order to meet qualifications and receive credit. NC State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have at least 3-5 years of experience as a graphic designer? Yes No * Do you have a portfolio that you can submit if needed? Yes No * Do you have familiarity and experience with Canva? Yes No * Do you have experience in higher education, museums, science organizations, non-profits, fundraising, or cultural institutions? This is not required for the position but preferred. Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Contact Information for References Optional Documents NC STATE UNIVERSITY RALEIGH, NC 27695 PHONE: (919) 515-2011 Privacy Accessibility Emergency Information Policies NC State Home © 2019 NC State University. All rights reserved To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
