    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/233584": {
      "title": "IT System Administrator",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | IT System Administrator Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) IT System Administrator Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. In addition to your application please submit a resume, cover letter, and the contact information for at least three professional references. Posting Details Posting Information Posting Number PG194798EP Internal Recruitment No Working Title IT System Administrator Anticipated Hiring Range $80,000 - $90,000 (commensurate with education/experience) Work Schedule Monday through Friday, 8 am - 5 pm with occasional additional hours and rotating 24x7 on-call support responsibilities outside regular work hours. Job Location Raleigh, NC Department Shared Services About the Department The Office of Information Technology ( OIT ) at NC State University provides a broad range of IT services to support our students, faculty, and staff. The Automated Workload Services ( AWS ) team, in the Shared Services Department of OIT , administers software packages for business process automation, Electronic Data Interchange ( EDI ) processing, and report management. Utilizing these tools, the team manages large volumes of business processing 24×7, 365 days/year, according to varying university business cycles. The team is also responsible for monitoring and maintaining Configuration Items in the ServiceNow Configuration Management Database ( CMDB ). Wolfpack Perks and Benefits As a Pack member, you belong here, and can enjoy exclusive perks designed to enhance your personal and professional well-being. As you consider this opportunity, we encourage you to review our Employee Value Proposition and learn more about what makes NC State the best place to learn and work for everyone. What we offer: Medical , Dental , and Vision Flexible Spending Account Retirement Programs Disability Plans Life Insurance Accident Plan Paid Time Off and Other Leave Programs 12 Holidays Each Year Tuition and Academic Assistance And so much more! Attain Work-life balance with our Childcare benefits, Wellness & Recreation Membership , and Wellness Programs that aim to build a thriving wolfpack community. Disclaimer: Perks and Benefit eligibility is based on Part-Time or Full-Time Employment status. Eligibility and Employer Sponsored Plans can be found within each of the links offered. Essential Job Duties As a member of the AWS team, you will bridge the gap between business needs and technology. You will work closely with application development teams to identify areas for process improvement and implement efficient solutions to meet business requirements. Using your technical and business knowledge to integrate and analyze data from multiple sources to draw conclusions and make recommendations, identify and investigate incidents, and collaborate with cross-functional teams to resolve or escalate issues and track them to resolution. You will be expected to work independently and handle multiple concurrent time-sensitive tasks that require attention to detail using various software technologies necessary to support the University’s enterprise applications and business operations requirements. Responsibilities include: Process Automation Develop, implement, and execute production and test processes and processing schedules using IBM Workload Scheduler, or other scheduling automation applications Develop, implement, and execute secure data transmissions using EDI or similar tools Configure and implement reports and bursting rules within the report distribution and archiving solution Assist with automation efforts and onboard new resources to ensure the completeness and accuracy of the ServiceNow Configuration Management Database Use scripting languages to connect, enhance functionality, and optimize back-end applications System software administration Configure and administer automated workload scheduling software Configure and administer secure data transmission software Assist in planning and implementation of software upgrades required to support functional enhancements or maintenance agreement Perform routine daily and ad hoc administrative tasks, monitor performance, address errors, and modify configurations to meet business requirements Monitor and maintain Configuration Items in the ServiceNow Configuration Management Database Other Responsibilities Technical Knowledge Serve as a subject matter expert for automated workload scheduling, EDI processing, report distribution and CMDB integrity Perform system level administration to troubleshoot incidents across software, OS, storage and network layers Technical Solutions Development Analyze requirements to design and implement efficient solutions to meet business needs Create automation and scripting solutions to extend software functionality, and improve reliability, consistency, and operational efficiency Technical Support Perform analysis on errors, investigate root causes and either resolve or collaborate with other technical teams in development of resolution Participate in an on call rotation, and work extended hours and weekends as necessary in support of business processes Customer Service Communicate technical concepts and potential solutions clearly to non technical stakeholders Partner with customers, cross functional OIT teams, vendors and trading partners to identify solutions to meet business needs and areas for process improvement Planning and Organizing Participate in the lifecycle management of software solutions by planning, coordination and implementation of patching and upgrades Develop and maintain documentation, operational standards and technical reference materials to ensure clarity and consistency Qualifications Minimum Education and Experience Bachelor’s degree in Information Technology, Computer Science, or a related discipline; or an equivalent combination of training and experience. All degrees must be received from appropriately accredited institutions. Other Required Qualifications Production support experience in a 24×7 enterprise environment Experience managing batch processes with workload scheduling management software such as IBM Workload Scheduler, CA-7 and Control-M or experience with Electronic Data Interchange mapping and software such as B2B Integrator and Boomi Demonstrated unix skills including basic shell scripting experience Ability to communicate effectively, work independently, and collaboratively as part of a team Capable of quickly learning new tools and processes, be detail oriented, and possess strong interpersonal, time management and organizational skills Experience with ERP applications such as PeopleSoft or SAP Experience with ServiceNow or a similar ticket management tool Preferred Qualifications Three or more years experience with IBM Workload Scheduler administration, including advanced skills such as creation and maintenance of operational run books, job modification, scheduling and rerun/restart Three or more years experience with IBM B2B Integrator and advanced knowledge of EDI mapping Unix software configuration and system administration experience Three or more years of scripting experience with languages such as Python, PowerShell or Bash scripting Three or more years of ServiceNow experience including CMDB Discovery and CMDB Dashboards ITIL certification Required License(s) or Certification(s) N/A Valid NC Driver's License required No Commercial Driver's License required No Recruitment Dates and Special Instructions Job Open Date 08/05/2026 Anticipated Close Date Open until filled Special Instructions to Applicants In addition to your application please submit a resume, cover letter, and the contact information for at least three professional references. Position Details Position Number 00041140 Position Type EPS/SAAO Full Time Equivalent (FTE) (1.0 = 40 hours/week) 1.0 Appointment 12 Month Recurring Mandatory Designation - Adverse Weather Mandatory - Adverse Weather Mandatory Designation - Emergency Events Mandatory - Fire/Explosions, Mandatory - Medical Emergencies, Mandatory - Hazardous Material Incidents, Mandatory - Transportation Accidents, Mandatory - Evacuations/Natural Hazards, Mandatory - Utilities/Infrastructure Failure, Mandatory - Threats of Violence/Terrorism/Interpersonal Emergencies Department ID 517101 - Shared Services EEO NC State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal opportunities for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, and veteran status. The University encourages all qualified applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities, to apply. Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodations in the application and interview process are welcome to contact 919-513-0574 to speak with a representative of the Office of Equal Opportunity. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at (919) 515-2135 or workatncstate@ncsu.edu . Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. Degree(s) must be obtained prior to start date in order to meet qualifications and receive credit. NC State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn of this opportunity? NCSU Website NCSU Executive Search Services Monster.com CareerBuilder.com InsideHigherEd.com Other Online Job Board Carolina Job Finder / Employment Guide Job / Career Fair The Chronicle of Higher Education HERC Professional Journal Print Advertisement (Newspaper / Periodical) Professional Organization Direct Contact from NCSU HR Representative / Recruiter NCSU Employee Referral Social Media (LinkedIn, Twitter, Facebook, Other) Other If you learned about this vacancy from \"other source\" or \"other website\", please provide the source. (Open Ended Question) * Please briefly describe your software support / administration experience.  In your response, please list / describe the software you have supported as well as the duties you performed in supporting it (i.e. patching, testing, etc.). (Open Ended Question) Application Materials Required Required Documents Resume Contact Information for References Cover Letter Optional Documents NC STATE UNIVERSITY RALEIGH, NC 27695 PHONE: (919) 515-2011 Privacy Accessibility Emergency Information Policies NC State Home © 2019 NC State University. All rights reserved To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/223323": {
      "title": "Position Information",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | Banquet Bartender Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) Banquet Bartender Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number PG195277TM Position Number 47BanquetBartender0725 Position Type Temporary Essential Job Duties JOIN THE PACK ! We are seeking enthusiastic individuals to Join our Pack as a Banquet Bartender. Essential job duties include: Able to work all types of events anywhere on campus Able to work by themselves Proper set up and break down of bars. Setup events, work the event, and clean up after the event, including removing all catering items from the event space(s), washing any dirty catering items and returning all cleaned and restocked items to the appropriate places within the catering stock rooms. Communicating with clients and guests as needed Catering support during down time Making sure the kitchen is clean before they leave when in Talley (taking out trash, sinks and counters are clean, floors are swept and mopped, dishwasher is drained and turned off). Able to check for identification ensuring no minors are being served. Other duties as assigned to ensure NC State Dining business needs are met. Position may be asked to assist in other locations as necessary. NC State Dining provides campus wide food services to students, staff, and faculty on the North Carolina State University Campus. NC State Dining operates 11 cafes, 3 food courts and 6 dining halls, 3 markets, 2 restaurants, vending, a nutritional counseling service, and a catering department. The department employs approximately 1000 temporary and student employees and approximately 190 permanent EHRA and SHRA employees. This is an hourly position, that includes a State required 32-day break at the end of 11 months. Excellent performance during this time may provide an opportunity to renew employment and/or advance. Is Time Limited No If Yes, Appointment Length Wolfpack Perks and Benefits As a Pack member, you belong here, and can enjoy exclusive perks designed to enhance your personal and professional well-being. What we offer: Health Insurance for Temporary Employees Enhance your career with LEAD courses Attend non-revenue generating sporting events for free. Attain Work-life balance with our Childcare discounts , Wellness & Recreation Membership , and Wellness Programs that aim to build a thriving wolfpack community. Disclaimer: Perks and Benefit eligibility is based on Part-Time or Full-Time Employment status. Eligibility and Employer Sponsored Plans can be found within each of the links offered. Department Information Job City & State Raleigh, NC Department NC State Dining System Information Classification Title Temporary-Skilled Trades Working Title Banquet Bartender Position Information Requirements and Preferences Work Schedule All shifts are available including weekends. Please list your availability in the appropriate section of the application. Other Work/Responsibilities • Be an ambassador for NC State Dining and the university as a whole and enrich the quality of life for the campus community and support student success. • Work as a cohesive team member and play an integral part in creating a positive work environment. Minimum Experience/Education • High School Diploma or equivalency. • Demonstrated possession of the competencies necessary to perform the work will also be considered. • At least six months of bartending experience of providing full bar service including set-up, breakdown, mixed drinks, etc Department Required Skills Must be at least 21 years of age. General knowledge of beer and wine, including the proper handling of beer and wine Proper operation and service of keg beer Work for extended periods of time without sitting. Position requires standing for long periods of time, walking, bending, twisting, pulling and pushing. Ability to work in a fast-paced environment Ability to communicate effectively and professionally with customers, supervisors, and peers. Ability to follow written and/or verbal instructions. Provide outstanding customer service, including the ability to remain professional and respectful under pressure when dealing with difficult situations. Excellence in completing all tasks. Ability to adapt to the changing customer volume level with a sense of urgency. Ability to work well as part of a team and independently as necessary. Must be able to lift up to 30 lbs with or without reasonable accommodation. Preferred Years Experience, Skills, Training, Education • At least one year of bartending experience. Required License or Certification n/a Valid NC Driver's License required? No Commercial Driver's License Required? No Recruitment Recruitment Details Anticipated Hiring Range $14 per hour Recruitment Dates Job Open Date 07/14/2025 Applicant Information Quick Link https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/220893 EEO NC State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal opportunities for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, and veteran status. The University encourages all qualified applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities, to apply. Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodations in the application and interview process are welcome to contact 919-513-0574 to speak with a representative of the Office of Equal Opportunity. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at (919) 515-2135 or workatncstate@ncsu.edu . Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. Degree(s) must be obtained prior to start date in order to meet qualifications and receive credit. NC State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn of this opportunity? NCSU Website Job Alert (automated email from our system) NCSU Executive Search Services Monster.com CareerBuilder.com InsideHigherEd.com HigherEdJobs.com Other Online Job Board Carolina Job Finder / Employment Guide Job / Career Fair The Chronicle of Higher Education Professional Journal Print Advertisement (Newspaper / Periodical) Radio / Television Advertisement Professional Organization Higher Education Recruitment Consortium (HERC) Direct Contact from NCSU HR Representative / Recruiter NCSU Employee Referral Social Media (LinkedIn, Twitter, Facebook, Other) Other If you learned about this vacancy from \"other source\" or \"other website\", please provide the source. (Open Ended Question) * Tell us about your previous bartending experience. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter NC STATE UNIVERSITY RALEIGH, NC 27695 PHONE: (919) 515-2011 Privacy Accessibility Emergency Information Policies NC State Home © 2019 NC State University. All rights reserved To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
