    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/232912": {
      "title": "Extension Agent, FCS (Assistant, Associate, or Full Agent)",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | Extension Agent, FCS (Assistant, Associate, or Full Agent) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) Extension Agent, FCS (Assistant, Associate, or Full Agent) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Special Instructions to applicants: In addition to your application, please submit a resume, cover letter and the contact information for at least three (3) professional references. Posting Details Position Information Posting Number PG190882CE Position Number SC-00002619-0726 Position Type NC Cooperative Extension Department Information Job City & State Fayetteville, NC Department NCCE Cumberland County System Information Working Title Extension Agent, FCS (Assistant, Associate, or Full Agent) Appointment 12 Month Recurring Job Type Full-Time - Permanent FTE 1.00 Position Information Position Overview Essential Job Duties Are you looking for a rewarding career that will let you give back to your community? NC State Extension extends research-based knowledge to all North Carolinians, helping them transform science into everyday solutions that improve their lives and grow our state. We are the model of excellence in non-formal, research-based education that advances agriculture, the environment, human health and well-being, youth and communities, while creating prosperity for all North Carolinians. Working for NC State Extension allows you to teach without being tied to a classroom and school bell. The position may be hired at the Assistant, Associate, or Full Agent level if the selected candidate meets the required qualifications. While our employees are located in NC County offices, they reap the benefits of employment at NC State University. Some of our benefits include: · Paid time off · Paid tuition · Health Insurance · Flexible Scheduling · Retirement Savings · Supplemental Benefits Programs · WolfPerks! You Belong Here! At NC State, our goal is for all employees to reach their fullest potential at work. As you consider this opportunity, we encourage you to review our Employee Value Proposition ( https://news.hr.ncsu.edu/you-belong-here/ ) and learn more about what makes NC State the best place to learn and work for everyone. Essential responsibilities for the position include planning, marketing, conducting and evaluating educational programs in Family and Consumer Sciences ( FCS ) for Cumberland County. Emphasis of the Family and Consumer Sciences program is on nutrition, food safety, health and wellness, local foods and cooking, chronic disease reduction, and volunteer management. The position will conduct viable, proactive research-based educational programs in these areas for both adult and youth audiences. The position will collaborate with Extension agents in the region on common educational program initiatives. All agents are expected to have a youth component in their programming. Primary Function of Organizational Unit North Carolina Cooperative Extension gives our residents easy access to the resources and expertise of NC State University and NC A&T State University. Through educational programs, publications and events, Cooperative Extension agents deliver unbiased, research-based information to North Carolina citizens. To learn more NC Cooperative Extension, Cumberland County Center go to: https://cumberland.ces.ncsu.edu/ Primary Function of Organizational Unit * Other Duties and Responsibilities Duties and Responsibilities * Other Work/Responsibilities The agent in this position will provide leadership for the development, implementation, evaluation, and marketing of an effective educational program in family and consumer sciences ( FCS ), including the areas of foods, nutrition, and health. The agent will implement programs through delivery methods which enhance learning and skill development. Delivery methods may include workshops, classes, seminars, technical assistance, field trips, tours, and other methods. The agent will align the programs to meet the needs of the county population and support the mission of the organization. Programs may include food safety training courses, cooking local foods, Steps to Health, Extension Master Food Volunteers, More in My Basket, Better Living Series, and other programs. The agent will also seek grants or other appropriate funding sources, to support expanded or innovative programming. The agent will collaborate and network with other agencies, groups, and organizations with similar missions. The professional in this position must be self-motivated, energetic, enjoy working with individuals as well as groups, be able to work with diverse audiences, and have the ability to manage multiple tasks with little supervision. The successful candidate is expected to be a team player working with the Extension staff and other organizations, possess a high degree of subject matter competence, and have the ability to work independently. The agent will be responsible for managing and working closely with volunteers in the Cumberland County Extension Volunteer Association. The agent will promote the volunteer program to gain community support, develop and implement strategies to recruit new volunteers, conduct ongoing evaluation of the program and services delivered by volunteers and implement improvements as necessary, review policies and procedures to reflect the overall values of the organizations, provide educational opportunities, mentor volunteers, and other volunteer management duties. There is a strong demand for food preservation information from home audiences. Attending training in food safety and food preservation is expected. Supervisory Number of Permanent Employees this Position Supervises 0 Percent of Time Spent 0% Requirements and Preferences Identify if the Position is Mandatory / Essential / Key Not Applicable Work Schedule Monday - Friday- 8 AM - 5 PM Business Hours - Evenings and Weekends as required Minimum Experience/Education One of the following educational requirements: – A Bachelor’s degree with a cumulative grade point average of 2.5 overall or a 3.0 in family and consumer sciences (formerly known as home economics) or a related field (based on a 4.0 scale). The minimum GPA requirement will be waived for NCCE Program Associates with a Bachelor’s degree. – A Bachelor’s degree and the completion of at least one-half of coursework in a Master’s degree curriculum with a cumulative grade point average 3.0 or higher with at least one degree in family and consumer sciences (formerly known as home economics) or a related field, or – Completion of a Master’s degree with at least one degree in family and consumer sciences (formerly known as home economics) or a related field. Department Required Skills The person in this position must be self-directed and possess a strong work ethic. The successful candidate should be energetic, innovative, and a good manager of time and other resources. Organizational, interpersonal, marketing, and networking skills are desirable. Other skills needed include knowledge and experience in educational presentations, public relations and marketing, print media, leadership, and computer usage. The ability to evaluate programs and document contacts and impacts is essential. Preferred Years Experience, Skills, Training, Education A Master’s degree at time of hiring is desirable, with at least one degree in family and consumer sciences, nutrition or related sciences. The expectation is that a Master’s degree will be pursued after hiring. Grantsmanship skills and experience with the ability to secure and manage outside funding resources in order to develop innovative programming is desired. Required License or Certification Valid Driver’s License and reliable, personal transportation required. Valid North Carolina driver’s license is required within 60 days of hire and must be maintained Valid NC Driver's License required? Yes Commercial Driver's License Required? No Physical Required? No List any other medical/drug tests required Recruitment Recruitment Details Anticipated Hiring Range Minimum Bachelor's $40,000; Minimum Master's $45,000; Minimum Doctorate $50,000 Commensurate with experience. Internal Transfer Only No Recruitment Dates Job Open Date 07/17/2026 Applicant Information Quick Link https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/232707 EEO NC State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal opportunities for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, and veteran status. The University encourages all qualified applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities, to apply. Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodations in the application and interview process are welcome to contact 919-513-0574 to speak with a representative of the Office of Equal Opportunity. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at (919) 515-2135 or workatncstate@ncsu.edu . Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. Degree(s) must be obtained prior to start date in order to meet qualifications and receive credit. NC State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn of this opportunity? NCSU Website Job Alert (automated email from our system) NCSU Executive Search Services Monster.com CareerBuilder.com InsideHigherEd.com HigherEdJobs.com Other Online Job Board Carolina Job Finder / Employment Guide Job / Career Fair The Chronicle of Higher Education Professional Journal Print Advertisement (Newspaper / Periodical) Radio / Television Advertisement Professional Organization Higher Education Recruitment Consortium (HERC) Direct Contact from NCSU HR Representative / Recruiter NCSU Employee Referral Social Media (LinkedIn, Twitter, Facebook, Other) Other * If you learned about this vacancy from \"other source\" or \"other website\", please provide the source. (Open Ended Question) * All agent positions require a minimum education requirement of: A. A Bachelor's degree with a cumulative grade point average of 2.5 overall or 3.0 in major field of study (based on a 4.0 scale); B. A Bachelor's degree and the completion of at least one-half of coursework in a Master's degree curriculum with a cumulative grade point average of 3.0 or higher; C. A completed Master's degree. Do you meet this minimum education requirement? Yes, I meet the requirement listed in section A above. Yes, I meet the requirement listed in section B above. Yes, I meet the requirement listed in section C above. No, however I am in my last semester of study. No, I do not meet this requirement. Application Materials Required Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Contact Information for References Optional Documents NC STATE UNIVERSITY RALEIGH, NC 27695 PHONE: (919) 515-2011 Privacy Accessibility Emergency Information Policies NC State Home © 2019 NC State University. All rights reserved To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/234433": {
      "title": "Lead Project Manager",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | Lead Project Manager Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) Lead Project Manager Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please include as attachments a resume/CV, cover letter, and contact information for at least 3 professional references. This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Applicants must be authorized to work in the United States without the need for current or future sponsorship. Posting Details Posting Information Posting Number PG194844EP Internal Recruitment No Working Title Lead Project Manager Anticipated Hiring Range $71,000 - $75,000 Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 8:00a.m. - 5:00p.m.; flexible work arrangement may be available depending on business needs. Job Location Raleigh, NC Department DELTA About the Department DELTA’s role within the Office of the Provost is to advance the integration and support of learning technologies in NC State’s academic programs and courses, both on campus and at a distance. DELTA supports distance-based credit programs and courses for the university, and provides enterprise academic technology and instructional support services for all modes of course delivery. Working with NC State instructors and partners, DELTA leads the way in designing, creating, implementing and supporting extraordinary digital learning experiences for our community of learners. DELTA applies expertise in technologies and pedagogies to create and nurture innovative, effective and impactful digital learning experiences for our community of instructors and learners with a collaborative, service-oriented and innovative mindset. Wolfpack Perks and Benefits As a Pack member, you belong here, and can enjoy exclusive perks designed to enhance your personal and professional well-being. As you consider this opportunity, we encourage you to review our Employee Value Proposition and learn more about what makes NC State the best place to learn and work for everyone. What we offer: Medical , Dental , and Vision Flexible Spending Account Retirement Programs Disability Plans Life Insurance Accident Plan Paid Time Off and Other Leave Programs 12 Holidays Each Year Tuition and Academic Assistance And so much more! Attain Work-life balance with our Childcare benefits, Wellness & Recreation Membership , and Wellness Programs that aim to build a thriving wolfpack community. Disclaimer: Perks and Benefit eligibility is based on Part-Time or Full-Time Employment status. Eligibility and Employer Sponsored Plans can be found within each of the links offered. Essential Job Duties In this role, you will provide project and change management expertise to lead complex, cross-team initiatives across DELTA . This role brings structure, collaboration, and organizational excellence to projects that span technology, instructional development, media production, marketing, communications, support, governance, and other strategic priorities. The Lead Project Manager independently manages high-impact projects, coordinates teams and resources, advises colleagues, and helps advance organizational excellence practices across DELTA and the university. Reporting to the Director, Project Management, this position works in a collaborative, team-based environment and serves as a trusted resource for project management, change management, coaching, and organizational improvement. Key Responsibilities: Lead the prioritization, definition, coordination, and management of complex DELTA projects, processes, and initiatives involving multiple teams, deliverables, resources, and organizational impacts. Partner with development teams, production managers, faculty, clients, vendors, and university colleagues to define project scope, goals, deliverables, dependencies, resources, and timelines. Analyze proposed projects and resource requirements to support effective prioritization and organizational planning. Develop project schedules, timelines, reports, and workflows that promote visibility, accountability, and effective resource management. Facilitate feasibility discussions, resolve competing priorities, negotiate deadlines, and bring teams together to address challenges related to scope, resources, timelines, and deliverables. Lead teams and groups without formal supervisory authority, providing direction, coaching, and informal leadership to colleagues. Manages and mediates complex conversations involving competing priorities, differing perspectives, sensitive topics, or organizational tensions with sound judgment and professionalism. Serve as a subject-matter expert and thought leader in project and change management, applying methodologies and practices such as Agile, Scrum, Prosci, and ADKAR . Collaborate with senior leadership to align projects and organizational practices with DELTA’s strategic goals. Research, evaluate, and implement emerging project and change management tools, techniques, and practices to improve efficiency and effectiveness. Administer DELTA’s project management system and lead related training, updates, and process improvements. Review and recommend improvements to procedures, workflows, and project management practices. Provide consultation, training, presentations, and guidance on project and change management across DELTA and the university. Represent DELTA and NC State University on campus committees, interest groups, conferences, and presentations, sharing project and organizational excellence expertise. Build and maintain strong professional relationships across DELTA and the university while fostering effective collaboration and communication. Mentor new project managers and part-time employees and, as needed, provide oversight of part-time staff. The successful candidate will bring excellent written and verbal communication skills, strong interpersonal and organizational abilities, and the confidence to communicate effectively with individuals and groups at all levels. You will be comfortable coordinating across technical, design, instructional, production, and administrative teams and working with internal and external clients and vendors. Experience with web-based collaboration tools and project management platforms such as ClickUp or Monday is highly valued. Most importantly, you will bring the ability to lead through influence, navigate competing priorities, build productive relationships, and use project and change management expertise to move complex work forward. Other Responsibilities Acts as point of contact for the organization regarding information across projects to facilitate resource and timeline planning. Keeps current with developments in project and change management professions (best practices and technologies in support of project and change management). Ensures accuracy of data and compliance within approved project standards Qualifications Minimum Education and Experience Bachelor’s degree in project management, communications, psychology, education, organizational science, or related field. 2+ years experience in project management, including managing time and documenting priorities, milestones and deliverables. An equivalent combination of education and experience may be considered. Other Required Qualifications Ability to coordinate with design staff, technical staff, coworkers, and internal/external clients and vendors. Superior comfort level speaking in groups, particularly when mediating between competing priorities, ideas or needs. Familiarity with web-based communication and collaboration tools. Expertise with project management applications (e.g. Basecamp, TeamworkPM, MS Project). Ability to lead groups or teams without formal supervisory authority. Preferred Qualifications Master’s degree in project management, communications, psychology, education, organizational science, business, or related field. Experience with Agile methodology and practice. Experience working in a higher education setting. Experience working with technology professionals, projects, and products. Certified Agile Coach, Certified Scrum Product Owner, Certified ScrumMaster, PMI Project Management Professional, Prosci Certified Change Practitioner, or other project management or change management certifications. Required License(s) or Certification(s) N/A Valid NC Driver's License required No Commercial Driver's License required No Recruitment Dates and Special Instructions Job Open Date 08/31/2026 Anticipated Close Date Open Until Filled Special Instructions to Applicants Please include as attachments a resume/CV, cover letter, and contact information for at least 3 professional references. This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Applicants must be authorized to work in the United States without the need for current or future sponsorship. Position Details Position Number 00106616 Position Type EPS/SAAO Full Time Equivalent (FTE) (1.0 = 40 hours/week) 1.00 Appointment 12 Month Recurring Mandatory Designation - Adverse Weather Non Mandatory - Adverse Weather Mandatory Designation - Emergency Events Non Mandatory - Emergency Event Department ID 339001 - DELTA EEO NC State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal opportunities for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, and veteran status. The University encourages all qualified applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities, to apply. Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodations in the application and interview process are welcome to contact 919-513-0574 to speak with a representative of the Office of Equal Opportunity. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at (919) 515-2135 or workatncstate@ncsu.edu . Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. Degree(s) must be obtained prior to start date in order to meet qualifications and receive credit. NC State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn of this opportunity? NCSU website Craigslist Indeed.com Carolina Job Finder/Employment Guide NC Works Dress for Success Technical/Trade School Program Job Fair (Identify Job Fair in question #2 below) Direct Contact from NSCU Representative (identify person in question #2 below) Other Monster.com Other online job board NCSU employee referral Social Media (LinkedIn, Twitter, Facebook, Ohter) If you learned about this vacancy from \"other source\" or \"other website\", please provide the source. (Open Ended Question) * How do you think a project manager contributes value to a project and the overall success of an organization? (Open Ended Question) * Describe a situation where you've used your interpersonal and communication skills to facilitate a discussion of competing ideas or needs. (Open Ended Question) * How do you build buy-in and achieve alignment with team members and stakeholders who do not directly report to you? (Open Ended Question) * What project and/or change management methodologies have you implemented and managed in your experience? Please describe a time you applied one of these methodologies in practice. What was the outcome, and what would you do differently if faced with a similar situation in the future? (Open Ended Question) Application Materials Required Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Contact Information for References Optional Documents NC STATE UNIVERSITY RALEIGH, NC 27695 PHONE: (919) 515-2011 Privacy Accessibility Emergency Information Policies NC State Home © 2019 NC State University. All rights reserved To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
