    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/234038": {
      "title": "Landscape Construction Project Manager",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | Landscape Construction Project Manager Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) Landscape Construction Project Manager Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please include as attachments a resume/CV, cover letter, and contact information for at least 3 professional references. This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Applicants must be authorized to work in the United States without the need for current or future sponsorship. Posting Details Posting Information Posting Number PG194786EP Internal Recruitment No Working Title Landscape Construction Project Manager Anticipated Hiring Range $67,000 - $72,000 Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 7:00 AM - 3:30 PM Job Location Raleigh, NC Department Landscape Maintenance & Operations About the Department The NC State University Facilities Division is home to nearly 900 professionals who plan , build and maintain the spaces that foster an environment where innovation, learning, and community thrive. Through this work, we help create spaces that empower students, faculty, and staff to reach their full potential. Operating year-round, we manage more than 16.7 million gross square feet of built space and oversee 4,733 acres of campus infrastructure through a series of core departments, each composed of multiple specialized units: Design & Construction Business Operations Campus Operations and Maintenance Campus Planning and Strategic Investment Whether responding to a maintenance request, shaping future facilities or creating spaces that inspire discovery, our team is grounded in excellence, service and stewardship. Join the pack and become part of one of the largest and most respected employers in the state, helping shape the future of our campus community. Take a look below to see what we offer! Wolfpack Perks and Benefits As a Pack member, you belong here, and can enjoy exclusive perks designed to enhance your personal and professional well-being. As you consider this opportunity, we encourage you to review our Employee Value Proposition and learn more about what makes NC State the best place to learn and work for everyone. What we offer: Medical , Dental , and Vision Flexible Spending Account Retirement Programs Disability Plans Life Insurance Accident Plan Paid Time Off and Other Leave Programs 12 Holidays Each Year Tuition and Academic Assistance And so much more! Attain Work-life balance with our Childcare benefits, Wellness & Recreation Membership , and Wellness Programs that aim to build a thriving wolfpack community. Disclaimer: Perks and Benefit eligibility is based on Part-Time or Full-Time Employment status. Eligibility and Employer Sponsored Plans can be found within each of the links offered. Essential Job Duties Do you have a passion for landscape construction and enjoy turning plans into well-executed projects? NC State University is seeking a Landscape Construction Project Manager to help shape and improve the campus landscape through thoughtful planning, strong project management, and a commitment to quality. In this role, you will manage landscape construction projects from planning and design through construction and final closeout. You’ll collaborate with University project managers, designers, consultants, contractors, and Facilities leadership to keep projects on schedule, within budget, and aligned with university standards. Your expertise in landscape construction, horticulture, hardscaping, irrigation, and stormwater systems will help ensure projects are built to last and successfully transition into ongoing campus maintenance. This is an opportunity to see your work become part of the NC State campus while working with a collaborative team dedicated to creating safe, functional, beautiful, and sustainable outdoor spaces. If you’re ready to bring your landscape construction expertise to projects that have a lasting impact on the NC State campus, we encourage you to apply! Key responsibilities and duties include but are not limited to: Manage landscape construction projects from planning and design through construction and final closeout, monitoring scope, schedules, budgets, milestones, and overall project progress . Use AiM, shared documentation, and team collaboration tools to track project information and maintain accurate project records. Identify and resolve project challenges and operational roadblocks while adapting project scope to meet university priorities. Develop, review, and update Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs) to promote consistent and efficient project delivery. Manage project documentation, including contracts, competitive bids, product warranties, project records, and final closeout materials. Serve as the primary point of contact for project-related communication and provide timely, clear updates to stakeholders and leadership. Collaborate with University Project and Design Managers, designers, consultants, contractors, and internal Facilities teams throughout planning, design, and construction. Provide concise project status, milestone, and issue updates during weekly leadership meetings. Build strong working relationships with Grounds Leadership, Landscape Construction Services, Waste Reduction and Recycling, Grounds Planning, and other campus partners. Participate in design reviews and evaluate project plans to ensure alignment with university standards and industry best practices. Apply knowledge of landscape construction, plant and tree identification, hardscape construction, commercial irrigation systems, and stormwater control measures (SCMs) . Conduct project site inspections to verify construction meets approved designs, specifications, quality standards, and campus expectations. Identify construction issues and coordinate solutions with project partners to maintain quality and project objectives. Lead project closeout activities, including final inspections and walk-throughs, verification and filing of as-built drawings, and transition of completed projects to the Grounds Maintenance team. Other Responsibilities Other tasks and responsibilities may be assigned based on the needs of the organization and evolving priorities. Qualifications Minimum Education and Experience Bachelor’s degree in the assigned discipline; or equivalent combination of training and experience. Other Required Qualifications Must be able to communicate effectively verbally with supervisors and the general public and understand verbal and written instructions and other communications regarding work assignments and other matters. Project management experience. Must have knowledge of building codes and regulations. Must be physically able to inspect areas that require climbing on ladders and bending to reach low areas. Preferred Qualifications Understands aspects of Excel, Microsoft Word, Microsoft projects, RS Means, AiM, and AutoCad software. Strong organizational abilities with an aptitude for multitasking. Exceptional problem-solving skills and proactive judgement. Ability to work independently and exercise sound judgment. Identifying, assessing, and mitigating potential project issues. Reading and understanding Blueprints and Plan Documents Required License(s) or Certification(s) Must have valid driver’s license Must be able to obtain a valid NCDL within 60 days of hire and must be maintained Valid NC Driver's License required Yes Commercial Driver's License required No Recruitment Dates and Special Instructions Job Open Date 08/18/2026 Anticipated Close Date Open Until Filled Special Instructions to Applicants Please include as attachments a resume/CV, cover letter, and contact information for at least 3 professional references. This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Applicants must be authorized to work in the United States without the need for current or future sponsorship. Position Details Position Number 00062921 Position Type EPS/SAAO Full Time Equivalent (FTE) (1.0 = 40 hours/week) 1.00 Appointment 12 Month Recurring Mandatory Designation - Adverse Weather Mandatory - Adverse Weather Mandatory Designation - Emergency Events Mandatory - Fire/Explosions, Mandatory - Medical Emergencies, Mandatory - Hazardous Material Incidents, Mandatory - Transportation Accidents, Mandatory - Evacuations/Natural Hazards, Mandatory - Utilities/Infrastructure Failure, Mandatory - Threats of Violence/Terrorism/Interpersonal Emergencies Department ID 445060 - Landscape Maintenance & Operations EEO NC State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal opportunities for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, and veteran status. The University encourages all qualified applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities, to apply. Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodations in the application and interview process are welcome to contact 919-513-0574 to speak with a representative of the Office of Equal Opportunity. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at (919) 515-2135 or workatncstate@ncsu.edu . Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. Degree(s) must be obtained prior to start date in order to meet qualifications and receive credit. NC State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn of this opportunity? NCSU website Craigslist Indeed.com Carolina Job Finder/Employment Guide NC Works Dress for Success Technical/Trade School Program Job Fair (Identify Job Fair in question #2 below) Direct Contact from NSCU Representative (identify person in question #2 below) Other Monster.com Other online job board NCSU employee referral Social Media (LinkedIn, Twitter, Facebook, Ohter) If you learned about this vacancy from \"other source\" or \"other website\", please provide the source. (Open Ended Question) * A valid driver's license (DL) is required and a North Carolina Driver's License (NCDL) must be obtained within 60 days of hire and maintained as a condition of employment. Do you have a valid driver's license or the ability to obtain one prior to start date, and the ability to obtain a North Carolina Driver's License within 60 days of hire? Yes, I have a valid NCDL and will maintain it as a condition of employment. Yes, I have a valid DL from another state and will obtain a NCDL within 60 days of hire and maintain it as a condition of employment. Yes, I have a valid DL from another state but cannot or will not obtain a NCDL within 60 days of hire. No, I do not have a valid DL from any state, but I will obtain a it within 60 days of hire and maintain it as a condition of employment. No, I do not have a valid DL from any state and cannot or will not obtain it. * How do you establish accountability when managing a project with multi shops/subcontractors with success? (Open Ended Question) * How do you execute and manage the critical path during the initial phases of a project? (Open Ended Question) Application Materials Required Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Contact Information for References Optional Documents NC STATE UNIVERSITY RALEIGH, NC 27695 PHONE: (919) 515-2011 Privacy Accessibility Emergency Information Policies NC State Home © 2019 NC State University. All rights reserved To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
