    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/230485": {
      "title": "Temporary Agroecology Lab Coordinator",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | Temporary Agroecology Lab Coordinator Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) Temporary Agroecology Lab Coordinator Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Attach: Letter of interest describing why you are a good fit for the position-specifying your interest in half-time or full-time position CV/Resume Contact information for at least 2 references Posting Details Position Information Posting Number PG195924TM Position Number 11ASO3688 Position Type Temporary Essential Job Duties The Agroecology Lab Coordinator will work under the supervision of the Agroecology Professor to support the establishment and growth of the Agroecology Lab, the undergraduate Agroecology Major, and the Agroecology Education Farm. The coordinator will assist in a variety of tasks aimed at enhancing the functionality and efficacy of the program while contributing to ongoing agroecological research and education projects. The coordinator will play a key role in developing and fostering relationships with farmers, private and public sector actors in the region to support collaborative research and community-based outreach efforts. The coordinator will collaborate with the Agroecology Education Farm manager and Sustainable Agriculture Systems Unit technician at the Lake Wheeler Field Lab to ensure smooth project execution and coordination across various activities. The coordinator will also assist in reviewing and summarizing relevant scientific literature, drafting reports and educational materials to enhance agroecology curriculum. Responsibilities will likely include: Network with organizations in the public sector (e.g., non-profits, community-based entities) striving to improve access to food and education Create outreach and education materials, such as videos, social media posts, brochures for the Agroecology Major, the Agroecology Education Farm, and the Sustainable Agriculture Systems Unit at the Lake Wheeler Field Lab Assist with the implementation of long-term demonstration cropping systems at the Sustainable Agriculture Systems Unit Assist with grant-writing Set up long-term data collection and automation at the Sustainable Agriculture Systems Unit, such as an on-site weather station, soil moisture probes, harvest record-keeping, irrigation systems. Maintain Agroecology Lab and Agroecology Education Farm websites Lead administrative tasks for Agroecology Education Farm tours This position will be best served by a good communicator with strong computer and organizational skills. It is expected that the person serving in this role will develop skills and knowledge on the job so a good attitude, strong interest in sustainable agriculture, and enthusiasm to learn will be essential. Is Time Limited No If Yes, Appointment Length Wolfpack Perks and Benefits As a Pack member, you belong here, and can enjoy exclusive perks designed to enhance your personal and professional well-being. As you consider this opportunity, we encourage you to review our Employee Value Proposition and learn more about what makes NC State the best place to learn and work for everyone. What we offer: Health Insurance for Temporary Employees Enhance your career with LEAD courses Attend non-revenue generating sporting events for free. Attain Work-life balance with our Childcare discounts , Wellness & Recreation Membership , and Wellness Programs that aim to build a thriving wolfpack community. Disclaimer: Perks and Benefit eligibility is based on Part-Time or Full-Time Employment status. Eligibility and Employer Sponsored Plans can be found within each of the links offered. Department Information Job City & State Raleigh, NC Department Crop and Soil Sciences System Information Classification Title Temporary-Technical/Paraprofessional Working Title Temporary Agroecology Lab Coordinator Position Information Requirements and Preferences Work Schedule Monday-Friday, 20-40/hrs per week Other Work/Responsibilities n/a Minimum Experience/Education Combination of training and experience required to perform the duties Department Required Skills Proficient with Microsoft Offie Suite (Excel, Work, PowerPoint) for data analysis, reporting and communication Excellent verbal in written communication skills Ability to work independently when needed Preferred Years Experience, Skills, Training, Education BS in agroecology, agriculture, environmental science, or ecology-related discipline or a 4-year degree with a strong familiarity of agriculture Required License or Certification Valid driver’s license Valid NC Driver's License required? Yes Commercial Driver's License Required? No Recruitment Recruitment Details Anticipated Hiring Range $16-$20/hr Recruitment Dates Job Open Date 04/15/2026 Applicant Information Quick Link https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/229565 EEO NC State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal opportunities for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, and veteran status. The University encourages all qualified applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities, to apply. Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodations in the application and interview process are welcome to contact 919-513-0574 to speak with a representative of the Office of Equal Opportunity. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at (919) 515-2135 or workatncstate@ncsu.edu . Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. Degree(s) must be obtained prior to start date in order to meet qualifications and receive credit. NC State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). How did you learn of this opportunity? NCSU Website Job Alert (automated email from our system) NCSU Executive Search Services Monster.com CareerBuilder.com InsideHigherEd.com HigherEdJobs.com Other Online Job Board Carolina Job Finder / Employment Guide Job / Career Fair The Chronicle of Higher Education Professional Journal Print Advertisement (Newspaper / Periodical) Radio / Television Advertisement Professional Organization Higher Education Recruitment Consortium (HERC) Direct Contact from NCSU HR Representative / Recruiter NCSU Employee Referral Social Media (LinkedIn, Twitter, Facebook, Other) Other If you learned about this vacancy from \"other source\" or \"other website\", please provide the source. (Open Ended Question) * Do you have the combination of training and experience required to perform the duties and responsibilities of the position? Yes No Do you possess a BS in agroecology, agriculture, environmental science, or ecology-related discipline OR a 4-year degree with a strong familiarity of agriculture? Yes No * Do you have excellent written and verbal communication skills? Yes No * Are you proficient in MS Office Suite? Yes No * Do you have a valid driver's license? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Contact Information for References Resume/CV Optional Documents NC STATE UNIVERSITY RALEIGH, NC 27695 PHONE: (919) 515-2011 Privacy Accessibility Emergency Information Policies NC State Home © 2019 NC State University. All rights reserved To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved wil