    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/234674": {
      "title": "Social Media Manager, Enterprise Content",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | Social Media Manager, Enterprise Content Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) Social Media Manager, Enterprise Content Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. In addition to your application, please submit a resume, cover letter, contact information for at least three professional references, and a copy of your portfolio or a link to your online portfolio. If uploading a copy of your portfolio, please select “Other Document 1” as the document type. Posting Details Job Posting Information Posting Number PG195202SP Internal Recruitment No Working Title Social Media Manager, Enterprise Content Anticipated Hiring Range $58,000 - $60,000 Work Schedule Monday to Friday, 8 a.m. to 5 p.m. The typical schedule will be four days per week in the office, one day remote. Some evening and weekend work required. Job Location Raleigh, North Carolina Department University Communications and Marketing About the Department University Communications and Marketing is the central agency responsible for shaping and sharing the story of NC State University. As the stewards of the NC State brand, we drive the university’s reputation and visibility through integrated marketing, strategic communications, and digital engagement. We are a team of creators, strategists, and problem-solvers dedicated to the “Think and Do” spirit. We collaborate across the university to elevate NC State’s profile as a premier public research institution, supporting enrollment, research, alumni engagement, and institutional prestige. Research is central to that story. NC State is a top public research university with a sponsored research portfolio exceeding $460 million, and the way we translate that work into public understanding shapes how the university is funded, trusted, and understood. This role sits at the center of that effort, partnering closely with the Office of Research and Innovation to bring the impact of NC State’s discovery and innovation to local, national, and global audiences. Wolfpack Perks and Benefits As a Pack member, you belong here, and can enjoy exclusive perks designed to enhance your personal and professional well-being. As you consider this opportunity, we encourage you to review our Employee Value Proposition and learn more about what makes NC State the best place to learn and work for everyone. What we offer: Medical , Dental , and Vision Flexible Spending Account Retirement Programs Disability Plans Life Insurance Accident Plan Paid Time Off and Other Leave Programs 12 Holidays Each Year Tuition and Academic Assistance And so much more! Attain Work-life balance with our Childcare benefits, Wellness & Recreation Membership , and Wellness Programs that aim to build a thriving wolfpack community. Disclaimer: Perks and Benefit eligibility is based on Part-Time or Full-Time Employment status. Eligibility and Employer Sponsored Plans can be found within each of the links offered. Essential Job Duties The Social Media Manager for Enterprise Content helps shape how NC State connects with its audiences across the university’s official social media channels. As a member of the Social Media Hub within University Communications and Marketing, this role manages the day-to-day creation, publishing and community engagement that bring the university’s stories to life. From faculty research and student experiences to major university events, the Social Media Manager turns complex ideas and moments into timely, engaging digital content. In this hands-on role you will be a part of shaping the @NCState social presence, combining digital storytelling, short-form video production and community management to connect people with the university and with one another. You’ll have the opportunity to be where the action is through conceptualizing and capturing content, covering events in real time, collaborating with students, faculty, staff and alumni, and responding to the conversations happening across NC State’s social channels. The Wolfpack community and the university’s communication priorities will be strengthened through your efforts. These efforts will include these key impact areas and responsibilities: Manage daily social content and community engagement across official enterprise channels, including Facebook, Instagram, LinkedIn, X, Threads, Bluesky, YouTube and TikTok. Create social-first stories and short-form video from concept through filming and editing, translating university priorities, research, events and experiences into compelling content. Capture the university in the moment through live social coverage of events and timely content that keeps audiences connected to what’s happening across NC State. Build meaningful community connections by monitoring conversations, trends and emerging issues; responding thoughtfully to comments and interactions; and appropriately managing sensitive content. Collaborate across the university with students, faculty, staff, alumni and student content creators to develop authentic, audience-focused content aligned with enterprise social strategy. Use social insights and performance data to understand what resonates with audiences and inform future content and engagement strategies. If you’re a creative storyteller who thrives in a fast-paced environment, brings strong communication and collaboration skills, and enjoys finding new ways to connect people through social media, we encourage you to apply. Other Responsibilities In addition to the core responsibilities of this role, there may be occasional opportunities to take on additional duties. This offers an opportunity to build on your skills, explore new areas, and gain a deeper understanding of the department’s operations. Qualifications Minimum Experience/Education Bachelor’s degree in a discipline related to the area of assignment; or an equivalent combination of training and experience. All degrees must be received from appropriately accredited institutions. Preferred Qualifications 2+ years of professional social media management experience, including developing and managing content for multiple social platforms. 3+ years of professional multimedia content production experience, including short-form video, social graphics and platform-specific content such as Instagram Reels and TikTok. Advanced proficiency with Meta Business Suite and experience using social media scheduling, publishing and analytics platforms such as Hootsuite. Proficiency with Adobe Premiere Pro and Canva, with experience using mobile and professional audio/video equipment to produce social-first content. Strong command of AP Style and social media best practices, including platform-specific content development, audience engagement, and adapting content to emerging formats and trends. Required License or Certification N/A Valid NC Driver's License required No Commercial Driver's License Required? No Recruitment Dates and Special Instructions Job Open Date 09/03/2026 Earliest Close Date---- (Positions will be posted until 5:00 PM ET on this date. Positions remaining posted after this date are still accepting applications but may close at any time.) 09/11/2026 Notice to Applicants Please note that the work history on your resume, must also be included in your application. Special Instructions In addition to your application, please submit a resume, cover letter, contact information for at least three professional references, and a copy of your portfolio or a link to your online portfolio. If uploading a copy of your portfolio, please select “Other Document 1” as the document type. Position Details Position Number 00112284 Position Type SHRA Position Classification Band Title Public Communication Specialist Position Classification Band Level Journey Position Classification Salary Range $ 35,880  -  $ 96,560 Salary Grade Equivalency NC13 Alternate Option If no applicants apply who meet the required competency level and training & experience requirements, then management may consider other applicants. Salary would be determined based on competencies, equity, budget, and market considerations. Full Time Equivalent (FTE) (1.0 = 40 hours/week) 1.0 Appointment 12 Month Recurring Mandatory Designation - Adverse Weather Non Mandatory - Adverse Weather Mandatory Designation - Emergency Events Non Mandatory - Emergency Event Time Limited Position No Time-Limited Appointment Length (if applicable) Department Id 281001 - Payroll EEO NC State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal opportunities for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, and veteran status. The University encourages all qualified applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities, to apply. Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodations in the application and interview process are welcome to contact 919-513-0574 to speak with a representative of the Office of Equal Opportunity. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at (919) 515-2135 or workatncstate@ncsu.edu . Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. Degree(s) must be obtained prior to start date in order to meet qualifications and receive credit. NC State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn of this opportunity? NCSU Website Job Alert (automated email from our system) NCSU Executive Search Services Monster.com CareerBuilder.com InsideHigherEd.com Other Online Job Board Carolina Job Finder / Employment Guide Job / Career Fair The Chronicle of Higher Education Professional Journal Print Advertisement (Newspaper / Periodical) Professional Organization Direct Contact from NCSU HR Representative / Recruiter NCSU Employee Referral Social Media (LinkedIn, Twitter, Facebook, Other) Other If you learned about this vacancy from \"other source\" or \"other website\", please provide the source. (Open Ended Question) * Please select the response below that best describes your experience/education for the Public Communication Specialist position. Bachelor's, Master's, or Doctorate in a related field Associate's, Bachelor's, Master's, or Doctorate in an unrelated field and four years of related experience Associate's in a related and two years of related experience Combination of post-high school education and/or experience in a related field to equal at least 4 years (ex. 1 year towards a related degree and 3 years of related experience) Did not complete high school but have a combination of high school education and related experience to equal 8 years (ex. 1 year of high school and 7 years of related experience) None of the above Application Materials Required Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Other Document (1) Contact Information for References Optional Documents NC STATE UNIVERSITY RALEIGH, NC 27695 PHONE: (919) 515-2011 Privacy Accessibility Emergency Information Policies NC State Home © 2019 NC State University. All rights reserved To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/234203": {
      "title": "Research Technician",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | Research Technician - Olby Lab Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) Research Technician - Olby Lab Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please include a resume, cover letter and contact information for at least three professional references. Posting Details Job Posting Information Posting Number PG195185SP Internal Recruitment No Working Title Research Technician - Olby Lab Anticipated Hiring Range $40,000 to $45,000 Work Schedule Monday - Friday; 8:00 AM - 5:00 PM Job Location Raleigh, NC Department Department of Clinical Sciences About the Department The Department of Clinical Sciences has 60 faculty members, 59 residents, interns, and post-doctoral fellows, 23 graduate students, and 24 research technicians and 3 administrative staff. The department provides learning opportunities within the four-year veterinary curriculum (educational information) and through continuing education for practitioners. Within the Veterinary Health Complex, faculty and staff provide care for patients, teach veterinary students, and provide advanced training for interns and residents. Faculty are very active in research programs to improve the health and welfare of animals and people. The Comparative Biomedical Sciences graduate program allows graduate students to focus their research in the areas of cell biology, infectious diseases, pharmacology, pathology, and population medicine. Other graduate programs with which departmental faculty are affiliated include programs in immunology, physiology, toxicology and functional genomics. Faculty are also involved with the Fisheries, Wildlife and Conservation Biology graduate program. Wolfpack Perks and Benefits As a Pack member, you belong here, and can enjoy exclusive perks designed to enhance your personal and professional well-being. As you consider this opportunity, we encourage you to review our Employee Value Proposition and learn more about what makes NC State the best place to learn and work for everyone. What we offer: Medical , Dental , and Vision Flexible Spending Account Retirement Programs Disability Plans Life Insurance Accident Plan Paid Time Off and Other Leave Programs 12 Holidays Each Year Tuition and Academic Assistance And so much more! Attain Work-life balance with our Childcare benefits, Wellness & Recreation Membership , and Wellness Programs that aim to build a thriving wolfpack community. Disclaimer: Perks and Benefit eligibility is based on Part-Time or Full-Time Employment status. Eligibility and Employer Sponsored Plans can be found within each of the links offered. Essential Job Duties The Translational Research in Pain team is seeking a Research Technician who is passionate about advancing pain management through innovative clinical and basic research. This position offers the opportunity to contribute to meaningful studies that improve pain assessment and treatment approaches in veterinary medicine while working alongside an interdisciplinary research team in a collaborative laboratory environment. In this role, you will support scientifically rigorous research activities across the Gait Lab, Lascelles RB Lab, and the Lascelles/Mishra Rodent Behavior Suite while gaining hands-on experience in clinical research, laboratory techniques, patient care activities, and data analysis. Additionally, you get to work closely with an interdisciplinary research team to help advance translational pain research and contribute to studies focused on improving pain assessment and treatment approaches in veterinary medicine. Key Responsibilities: Support clinical and translational research studies focused on pain management and pain assessment. Assist with the organization and execution of clinical trials, including participant recruitment, screening, scheduling, and study coordination. Perform pain assessments and provide patient care support for clinical and laboratory research subjects. Collect, process, and analyze kinetic, behavioral, and laboratory research data in accordance with established protocols. Assist with tissue collection and processing activities to support ongoing research initiatives. Support data entry, data management, and data analysis activities to ensure accurate and reliable research outcomes. Assist with constructing, monitoring, and maintaining compliance with IACUC protocols and research procedures. Learn to operate and maintain specialized research equipment, including gait laboratory systems, pressure mats, force plates, QST equipment, rodent behavior systems, and laboratory benchtop equipment. Contribute to manuscript review and other research-related documentation activities. If you are excited by the opportunity to contribute to innovative pain research, enjoy working in a collaborative clinical and laboratory environment, and are eager to build hands-on experience in translational veterinary research, we encourage you to apply. Other Responsibilities In addition to the core responsibilities of this role, there will be additional duties to assist with listed below: Schedule visitors and coordinate laboratory meetings and room reservations. Help maintain organized, clean, and efficient laboratory and research environments. Provide general operational and administrative support to help ensure smooth day-to-day research activities. Assist with other laboratory support duties as assigned in support of the research team’s mission. Qualifications Minimum Experience/Education Demonstrated possession of the competencies necessary to perform the work. Preferred Qualifications Background working in a veterinary clinic or research environment, including customer service or client interaction responsibilities. Knowledge of animal anatomy, animal handling techniques, and the ability to assist with animal dissection or tissue collection activities. Familiarity with orthopedic pain research, gait analysis software, or related research technologies. Strong organizational, analytical, and computer skills with the ability to maintain accurate records and manage research data. Ability to demonstrate initiative, communicate effectively, and work proactively in a collaborative clinical and laboratory research environment. Required License or Certification N/A Valid NC Driver's License required No Commercial Driver's License Required? No Recruitment Dates and Special Instructions Job Open Date 08/24/2026 Earliest Close Date---- (Positions will be posted until 5:00 PM ET on this date. Positions remaining posted after this date are still accepting applications but may close at any time.) 08/31/2026 Notice to Applicants Please note that the work history on your resume, must also be included in your application. Special Instructions Please include a resume, cover letter and contact information for at least three professional references. Position Details Position Number 00111655 Position Type SHRA Position Classification Band Title Research Technician Position Classification Band Level Journey Position Classification Salary Range $ 34,320  -  $ 72,734 Salary Grade Equivalency MH04 Alternate Option If no applicants apply who meet the required competency level and training & experience requirements, then management may consider other applicants. Salary would be determined based on competencies, equity, budget, and market considerations. Full Time Equivalent (FTE) (1.0 = 40 hours/week) 1.0 Appointment 12 Month Recurring Mandatory Designation - Adverse Weather Non Mandatory - Adverse Weather Mandatory Designation - Emergency Events Mandatory - Medical Emergencies Time Limited Position No Time-Limited Appointment Length (if applicable) No Department Id 195001 - Department of Clinical Sciences EEO NC State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal opportunities for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, and veteran status. The University encourages all qualified applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities, to apply. Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodations in the application and interview process are welcome to contact 919-513-0574 to speak with a representative of the Office of Equal Opportunity. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at (919) 515-2135 or workatncstate@ncsu.edu . Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. Degree(s) must be obtained prior to start date in order to meet qualifications and receive credit. NC State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn of this opportunity? NCSU Website NCSU Executive Search Services Monster.com CareerBuilder.com InsideHigherEd.com Other Online Job Board Carolina Job Finder / Employment Guide Job / Career Fair The Chronicle of Higher Education HERC Professional Journal Print Advertisement (Newspaper / Periodical) Professional Organization Direct Contact from NCSU HR Representative / Recruiter NCSU Employee Referral Social Media (LinkedIn, Twitter, Facebook, Other) Other If you learned about this vacancy from \"other source\" or \"other website\", please provide the source. (Open Ended Question) * Do you have experience with laboratory testing and analysis? Yes No * Do you have experience with basic lab techniques and proper use of lab equipment? Yes No * Do you possess experience with orthopedic pain research?  If yes, please describe.  If you have no experience, please enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) Application Materials Required Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Contact Information for References Optional Documents NC STATE UNIVERSITY RALEIGH, NC 27695 PHONE: (919) 515-2011 Privacy Accessibility Emergency Information Policies NC State Home © 2019 NC State University. All rights reserved To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/228122": {
      "title": "Lecturer or Assistant Teaching Professor in Religious Studies",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | Lecturer or Assistant Teaching Professor in Religious Studies Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) Lecturer or Assistant Teaching Professor in Religious Studies Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Only online applications will be considered. These should be submitted online at https://jobs.ncsu.edu/. Please attach an application letter, your Curriculum Vitae, and evidence of teaching effectiveness (using the “Teaching Statement” option) to your online application and arrange to have three letters of reference sent by email attachment to Kathryn Zellmer at kkzellme@ncsu.edu Posting Details Posting Information Posting Number PG194521EP Internal Recruitment No Working Title Lecturer or Assistant Teaching Professor in Religious Studies Anticipated Hiring Range Commensurate with experience and credentials. Work Schedule Varies Based on Teaching Schedule Job Location Raleigh, NC Department Philosophy & Religious Studies About the Department The Department of Philosophy and Religious Studies at North Carolina State University is committed to offering a high quality undergraduate Philosophy curriculum, including a major and minor in Philosophy, that gives students an opportunity to confront through historical and contemporary resources a wide range of central philosophical issues, such as the relationship between the mind and brain, the ethical implications of scientific advances, the justification of moral, political, and legal institutions, the relationship between human knowledge and reality, and the nature of the logic that structures human language and thought; offering a high-quality undergraduate Religious Studies curriculum, including a major and a minor in Religious Studies, that provides students an extended opportunity to examine the multiple interpretations of the category “religion” – including religion as a social construction, as an element of psychological development, as a branch of metaphysics, and as a constellation of ritual practices – and the ways in which religious traditions have played a central role in human culture and history; developing the analytical abilities and expressive powers of our students; providing and expanding educational and research opportunities at the graduate level; and conducting research, teaching and scholarship that further knowledge and understanding in the disciplines of Philosophy and Religious Studies. Wolfpack Perks and Benefits As a Pack member, you belong here, and can enjoy exclusive perks designed to enhance your personal and professional well-being. As you consider this opportunity, we encourage you to review our Employee Value Proposition and learn more about what makes NC State the best place to learn and work for everyone. What we offer: Medical , Dental , and Vision Flexible Spending Account Retirement Programs Disability Plans Life Insurance Accident Plan Paid Time Off and Other Leave Programs 12 Holidays Each Year Tuition and Academic Assistance And so much more! Attain Work-life balance with our Childcare benefits, Wellness & Recreation Membership , and Wellness Programs that aim to build a thriving wolfpack community. Disclaimer: Perks and Benefit eligibility is based on Part-Time or Full-Time Employment status. Eligibility and Employer Sponsored Plans can be found within each of the links offered. Essential Job Duties The Department of Philosophy and Religious Studies at NC State University invites applications for potential short-term teaching positions in Religious Studies during the 2026-27 academic year. These positions may involve teaching one or more courses for a single semester or the full academic year, depending on departmental needs. Courses that may require instructors include Religious Traditions of the World, Asian Religions, Introduction to the Old Testament, Introduction to the New Testament, The Hindu Tradition, The Buddhist Traditions, Islam, and other Religious Studies ( REL ) courses listed in the NC State course catalog. We welcome applications from qualified candidates and will review submissions as teaching needs arise. Other Responsibilities Perform other duties as assigned by the department head. Qualifications Minimum Education and Experience Lecturer: Master’s Degree in Religious Studies or related field, an equivalent degree or equivalent professional experience is required. If teaching graduate level courses, a Doctor’s Degree, an equivalent degree, or equivalent professional experience is required. Assistant Teaching Professor: Doctor’s Degree in Religious Studies or related field, an equivalent degree, or equivalent professional experience is required. Ability to direct activities and participate in departmental activities. Rank is dependent upon qualifications. All degrees must be received from appropriately accredited institutions. Other Required Qualifications Strong commitment to excellence in teaching is expected. Excellent communication skills. Preferred Qualifications Ph.D. strongly preferred Required License(s) or Certification(s) n/a Valid NC Driver's License required No Commercial Driver's License required No Recruitment Dates and Special Instructions Job Open Date 03/05/2026 Anticipated Close Date 3/19/2026; if posting is still active we are still accepting and reviewing applications Special Instructions to Applicants Only online applications will be considered. These should be submitted online at https://jobs.ncsu.edu/. Please attach an application letter, your Curriculum Vitae, and evidence of teaching effectiveness (using the “Teaching Statement” option) to your online application and arrange to have three letters of reference sent by email attachment to Kathryn Zellmer at kkzellme@ncsu.edu Position Details Position Number 00104561 Position Type Non-Tenure-Track Faculty Full Time Equivalent (FTE) (1.0 = 40 hours/week) 0.225 - 1.0, depending on department needs Appointment 9 Month Recurring Mandatory Designation - Adverse Weather Non Mandatory - Adverse Weather Mandatory Designation - Emergency Events Non Mandatory - Emergency Event Department ID 160501 - Philosophy & Religious Studies EEO NC State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal opportunities for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, and veteran status. The University encourages all qualified applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities, to apply. Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodations in the application and interview process are welcome to contact 919-513-0574 to speak with a representative of the Office of Equal Opportunity. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at (919) 515-2135 or workatncstate@ncsu.edu . Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. Degree(s) must be obtained prior to start date in order to meet qualifications and receive credit. NC State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn of this opportunity? NCSU Website Job Alert (automated email from our system) NCSU Executive Search Services Monster.com CareerBuilder.com InsideHigherEd.com HigherEdJobs.com Other Online Job Board Carolina Job Finder / Employment Guide Job / Career Fair The Chronicle of Higher Education Professional Journal Print Advertisement (Newspaper / Periodical) Radio / Television Advertisement Professional Organization Higher Education Recruitment Consortium (HERC) Direct Contact from NCSU HR Representative / Recruiter NCSU Employee Referral Social Media (LinkedIn, Twitter, Facebook, Other) Other If you learned about this vacancy from \"other source\" or \"other website\", please provide the source. (Open Ended Question) * What is your highest level of education completed? Did not complete high school High School (or equivalency) Associate's degree (or equivalency) Bachelor's degree (or equivalency) Master's degree (or equivalency) Doctorate (or equivalency) Application Materials Required Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Contact Information for References Teaching Statement Optional Documents Other Document (1) NC STATE UNIVERSITY RALEIGH, NC 27695 PHONE: (919) 515-2011 Privacy Accessibility Emergency Information Policies NC State Home © 2019 NC State University. All rights reserved To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
