    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/225839": {
      "title": "Temporary Outdoor Education Instructor",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | Temporary Outdoor Education Instructor - Reidsville, NC Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) Temporary Outdoor Education Instructor - Reidsville, NC Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Attach: Resume Contact information for 3 references Posting Details Position Information Posting Number PG195628TM Position Number 11ASO3605 Position Type Temporary Essential Job Duties Primary Purpose of Position (Includes the day to day duties of the position) – NC State University’s Betsy-Jeff Penn 4-H Center is seeking Outdoor Education Instructors for our Spring program season beginning March 2, 2026 and ending May 22, 2026. Staff with an interest may continue employment for summer camp (June-August) and Fall programming (August- November). The Penn 4-H Center provides day and overnight programs to elementary, middle, and high school students on our 220 acres in Reidsville, NC. Program staff Provide instruction for nearly 20 programs in environmental science and cultural history to elementary school students in the Environmental Education Program. Topics include aquatic ecology, forest measurements, predator/prey relationships, wildlife habitats, pioneer living history, canoeing and much more. Staff also facilitate team challenges and Low and High Ropes course elements with students in the Soaring Thru Spaces program. A 2 week paid staff training is provided at the beginning of the season (March 2-6 / 9 – 13) and as part of that there will also be a 3 day high ropes course training provided that staff are required to attend. Instructors do NOT need to be comfortable working at heights to safely facilitate our high ropes course. Please check us out at bjpenn4h.org to learn more about us. Internships may also be available.Questions regarding the position should be directed to Kyle Shillinglaw at 336-349-9445 ext.305 or by email to kyle_shillinglaw@ncsu.edu Work Schedule: Varies, but generally 5 day work weeks, some weekend work required. Long work days (8am-9pm) are sometimes required but no overnight supervisory duties in the cabins is required during our fall/spring school programming. This is a seasonal position that ends in late May with opportunities for continued employment during our summer and fall programs. A Private room in our staff house and meals when working are included during the duration of spring employment. Internships may also be available. Questions regarding the position should be directed to Kyle Shillinglaw at 336-349-9445 ext.303 or by email to kyle_shillinglaw@ncsu.edu Please Email Kyle at kyle_shillinglaw@ncsu.edu after applying to confirm your application has been received in the NCSU jobs system Is Time Limited No If Yes, Appointment Length Wolfpack Perks and Benefits As a Pack member, you belong here, and can enjoy exclusive perks designed to enhance your personal and professional well-being. What we offer: Health Insurance for Temporary Employees Enhance your career with LEAD courses Attend non-revenue generating sporting events for free. Attain Work-life balance with our Childcare discounts , Wellness & Recreation Membership , and Wellness Programs that aim to build a thriving wolfpack community. Disclaimer: Perks and Benefit eligibility is based on Part-Time or Full-Time Employment status. Eligibility and Employer Sponsored Plans can be found within each of the links offered. Department Information Job City & State Reidsville, NC Department 4-H Youth Development/Betsy Jeff Penn 4-H Center System Information Classification Title Temporary-Technical/Paraprofessional Working Title Temporary Outdoor Education Instructor - Reidsville, NC Position Information Requirements and Preferences Work Schedule 40+ Other Work/Responsibilities n/a Minimum Experience/Education High School Diploma or equivalent Department Required Skills Must have a love for working with kids, an interest in experiential education, enthusiasm for hard work, and a ton of patience Preferred Years Experience, Skills, Training, Education Degree in a related field or 2 years experience working with youth Previous work in a camp setting Required License or Certification n/a Valid NC Driver's License required? No Commercial Driver's License Required? No Recruitment Recruitment Details Anticipated Hiring Range $425-$450/wk Recruitment Dates Job Open Date 12/08/2025 Applicant Information Quick Link https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/225570 EEO NC State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal opportunities for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, and veteran status. The University encourages all qualified applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities, to apply. Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodations in the application and interview process are welcome to contact 919-513-0574 to speak with a representative of the Office of Equal Opportunity. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at (919) 515-2135 or workatncstate@ncsu.edu. Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. Degree(s) must be obtained prior to start date in order to meet qualifications and receive credit. NC State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). How did you learn of this opportunity? NCSU Website Job Alert (automated email from our system) NCSU Executive Search Services Monster.com CareerBuilder.com InsideHigherEd.com HigherEdJobs.com Other Online Job Board Carolina Job Finder / Employment Guide Job / Career Fair The Chronicle of Higher Education Professional Journal Print Advertisement (Newspaper / Periodical) Radio / Television Advertisement Professional Organization Higher Education Recruitment Consortium (HERC) Direct Contact from NCSU HR Representative / Recruiter NCSU Employee Referral Social Media (LinkedIn, Twitter, Facebook, Other) Other If you learned about this vacancy from \"other source\" or \"other website\", please provide the source. (Open Ended Question) * Do you have a High School Diploma or Equivalent? Yes No * Do you possess a love for working with kids, an interest in experiential education, enthusiasm for hard work, and a ton of patience? Yes No Do you have previous experience in a camp setting? Yes No Do you have a degree in a related field or 2 years experience working with youth? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Contact Information for References Optional Documents NC STATE UNIVERSITY RALEIGH, NC 27695 PHONE: (919) 515-2011 Privacy Accessibility Emergency Information Policies NC State Home © 2019 NC State University. All rights reserved To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
