    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/234546": {
      "title": "Director of Research Communications",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | Director of Research Communications Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) Director of Research Communications Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please include a cover letter, resume and contact information for at least three professional references. Posting Details Posting Information Posting Number PG194854EP Internal Recruitment Yes Working Title Director of Research Communications Anticipated Hiring Range Commensurate with education and experience Work Schedule Core Business Hours: Monday - Friday, 8:00 am - 5:00 pm; hours will vary based on business need. Job Location Raleigh, NC Department University Communications and Marketing About the Department University Communications and Marketing is the central agency responsible for shaping and sharing the story of NC State University. As the stewards of the NC State brand, we drive the university’s reputation and visibility through integrated marketing, strategic communications, and digital engagement. We are a team of creators, strategists, and problem-solvers dedicated to the “Think and Do” spirit. We collaborate across the university to elevate NC State’s profile as a premier public research institution, supporting enrollment, research, alumni engagement, and institutional prestige. Research is central to that story. NC State is a top public research university with a sponsored research portfolio exceeding $460 million, and the way we translate that work into public understanding shapes how the university is funded, trusted, and understood. This role sits at the center of that effort, partnering closely with the Office of Research and Innovation to bring the impact of NC State’s discovery and innovation to local, national, and global audiences. Wolfpack Perks and Benefits As a Pack member, you belong here, and can enjoy exclusive perks designed to enhance your personal and professional well-being. As you consider this opportunity, we encourage you to review our Employee Value Proposition and learn more about what makes NC State the best place to learn and work for everyone. What we offer: Medical , Dental , and Vision Flexible Spending Account Retirement Programs Disability Plans Life Insurance Accident Plan Paid Time Off and Other Leave Programs 12 Holidays Each Year Tuition and Academic Assistance And so much more! Attain Work-life balance with our Childcare benefits, Wellness & Recreation Membership , and Wellness Programs that aim to build a thriving wolfpack community. Disclaimer: Perks and Benefit eligibility is based on Part-Time or Full-Time Employment status. Eligibility and Employer Sponsored Plans can be found within each of the links offered. Essential Job Duties This is an internal posting for current NC State permanent and temporary employees, and candidates with RIF priority. The University Communications team is seeking a skilled research communicator and collaborative leader to shape how the university’s research and innovation enterprise is understood, valued, and shared. This position leads enterprise-wide research communications that translate complex discoveries, expertise, and innovation into clear, compelling narratives for the audiences who influence NC State’s reputation, resources, and impact—including news media, policymakers, peer institutions, donors, partners, prospective students, faculty, and the public. In this role, you will serve as the university’s strategic communications partner to the research enterprise, working across University Communications and Marketing and closely with the Vice Chancellor for Communications and Marketing and the Vice Chancellor for Research and Innovation. You will shape research storytelling and national and trade media visibility, connect research communicators across the university, and help position NC State’s discoveries and expertise in conversations that matter beyond campus. Your ability to move comfortably between the laboratory and the newsroom will be essential—you will build trust with researchers, identify the stories behind their work, and make complex research meaningful to audiences who may never read the original paper. Key responsibilities fall within the following functional areas: Research Storytelling and Content Strategy: Shape the university’s research narrative and content strategy, identifying and elevating compelling stories across fundamental discovery, translational science, interdisciplinary research, and community-engaged scholarship for audiences and platforms that extend NC State’s reach and influence. Translate complex scientific and technical work into compelling, accessible narratives that maintain research rigor while connecting discovery to the people, questions, and real-world impact behind the work. Develop enterprise research communications strategy in alignment with the division’s integrated communications strategy and NC State’s “Think and Do” brand, message pillars, and visual standards. Earned Media and National Visibility for Research: Expand NC State’s national and industry visibility as a research and innovation leader through proactive media strategy and outreach that increases share of voice and positions faculty as trusted experts on issues of consequence. Orchestrate communications around high-impact research moments, including major discoveries, awards, rankings, funding, and other milestones, in partnership with the division’s media relations function. Cultivate relationships with science, research, trade, and industry journalists while strengthening faculty readiness to serve as credible, compelling expert sources. Campus Research Communications Network: Lead and strengthen a university-wide research communications network spanning colleges, centers, institutes, and the Office of Research and Innovation, creating greater alignment, visibility, and strategic value while respecting decentralized ownership. Connect communicators, research leadership, faculty, and University Communications and Marketing around shared priorities, creating coordinated pathways for identifying, developing, and amplifying research stories across university channels. Establish shared standards, story pipelines, and collaborative practices that increase the consistency, efficiency, and reach of research communications across the enterprise. Issues and Sensitive Research Communications Provide strategic counsel on emerging and sensitive research-related issues, helping ensure accurate, timely, and coordinated communications in partnership with university leadership and the division’s issues and crisis communications function. Navigate and translate an evolving federal research funding and policy environment, helping internal and external audiences understand implications for NC State’s research enterprise in coordination with the Office of Research and Innovation, legal counsel, and divisional partners. Guide coordinated research communications during periods of disruption or heightened scrutiny, including funding changes, policy transitions, leadership changes, and other issues affecting the university’s research mission and reputation. Collaboration, Culture, and Operations Leverage the division’s existing digital, editorial, marketing, and communications infrastructure to strengthen the reach and effectiveness of research storytelling across web, marketing, and other strategic channels. Lead and develop assigned communications staff, fostering a high-performing, collaborative culture grounded in professional growth, strong execution, and shared accountability. Use audience insight, analytics, and performance measures to strengthen communications strategy, continuously refining storytelling, channels, and engagement based on what advances organizational goals. Oversee external partners, vendors, and project delivery for research communications initiatives, ensuring resources and timelines support strategic priorities. If you are a strategic communicator who can move seamlessly between scientific discovery, institutional strategy, and compelling storytelling, we encourage you to apply and help shape how NC State’s research and innovation are understood, valued, and shared with the world. Other Responsibilities In addition to the core responsibilities of this role, there will be opportunities to represent the division through engagement with internal and external constituents, including university and research leadership, faculty, communicators across the university, representatives from peer institutions, media, partners, and members of the public. These opportunities will be assigned in collaboration with the Associate Vice Chancellor for Integrated Strategic Communications and Vice Chancellor in support of evolving departmental and institutional priorities. Qualifications Minimum Education and Experience Post-baccalaureate degree in Journalism, Communications, Public Relations, a scientific or technical discipline, or a related field; or a Bachelor’s degree with equivalent broad-based independent experience in research, science, or strategic communications. An equivalent combination of education and experience may be substituted for the advanced degree. All degrees must be received from appropriately accredited institutions. Other Required Qualifications Six or more years of progressively responsible experience in communications, public relations, science or research communications, or a related field, including translating complex or technical subject matter for non-specialist audiences. Advanced research storytelling, writing, editing, and multimedia skills, with the ability to translate complex scientific or technical information into clear, accurate, compelling narratives tailored to varied audiences and channels. Media relations and earned media skills, including cultivating journalist relationships and securing high-impact coverage that elevates research, institutional expertise, or organizational priorities. Senior-level advising and collaborative leadership skills, including building trust with leaders and subject-matter experts and aligning cross-functional teams or decentralized stakeholders around shared communications goals. Sound judgment and discretion in high-stakes communications, with experience assessing sensitive or emerging issues and developing timely, accurate, and coordinated communications. Preferred Qualifications Experience communicating within a research-intensive environment, such as an R1 university, academic medical center, federal agency, or science- or technology-focused organization. Knowledge of the higher education research ecosystem, including federal research funding agencies, academic research processes, and the research lifecycle. People leadership and talent development skills, with experience supervising professional staff and/or student employees and developing communications talent. Master’s degree in Journalism, Communications, Public Relations, a scientific or technical discipline, or a related field. Accreditation in Public Relations ( APR ) or an equivalent professional credential. Media monitoring and analytics skills, with the ability to interpret media and audience data to inform communications strategy and assess impact. Required License(s) or Certification(s) N/A Valid NC Driver's License required No Commercial Driver's License required No Recruitment Dates and Special Instructions Job Open Date 09/02/2026 Anticipated Close Date 9/15/2026, if posting is active we are still accepting and reviewing applications Special Instructions to Applicants Please include a cover letter, resume and contact information for at least three professional references. Position Details Position Number 00112286 Position Type EPS/SAAO Full Time Equivalent (FTE) (1.0 = 40 hours/week) 1.0 Appointment 12 Month Recurring Mandatory Designation - Adverse Weather Non Mandatory - Adverse Weather Mandatory Designation - Emergency Events Non Mandatory - Emergency Event Department ID 281001 - Payroll EEO NC State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal opportunities for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, and veteran status. The University encourages all qualified applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities, to apply. Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodations in the application and interview process are welcome to contact 919-513-0574 to speak with a representative of the Office of Equal Opportunity. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at (919) 515-2135 or workatncstate@ncsu.edu . Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. Degree(s) must be obtained prior to start date in order to meet qualifications and receive credit. NC State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn of this opportunity? NCSU website Craigslist Indeed.com Carolina Job Finder/Employment Guide NC Works Dress for Success Technical/Trade School Program Job Fair (Identify Job Fair in question #2 below) Direct Contact from NSCU Representative (identify person in question #2 below) Other Monster.com Other online job board NCSU employee referral Social Media (LinkedIn, Twitter, Facebook, Ohter) If you learned about this vacancy from \"other source\" or \"other website\", please provide the source. (Open Ended Question) * Are you a current NC State permanent employee, temporary employee, or candidates with RIF priority? Yes No Application Materials Required Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Contact Information for References Optional Documents NC STATE UNIVERSITY RALEIGH, NC 27695 PHONE: (919) 515-2011 Privacy Accessibility Emergency Information Policies NC State Home © 2019 NC State University. All rights reserved To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/234060": {
      "title": "Shipping & Receiving Assistant",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | Shipping &amp; Receiving Assistant Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) Shipping & Receiving Assistant Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please include as attachments a resume/CV and contact information for at least 3 professional references. Posting Details Job Posting Information Posting Number PG195179SP Internal Recruitment No Working Title Shipping & Receiving Assistant Anticipated Hiring Range $40,000 - $42,000 Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 8:00 am - 5:00 pm; with occasional overtime Job Location Raleigh, NC Department Materials Management Unit About the Department The Materials Management Unit of the College of Veterinary Medicine provides all materials management and supply support for the college. It is one of two units for the receipt and distribution of all materials, shipments, and any equipment and resource deliveries. The unit is responsible for the daily flow of supplies and materials needed for daily operations. North Carolina State University’s College of Veterinary Medicine ( CVM ) is a dynamic community whose members are dedicated to preparing veterinarians and veterinarian scientists while advancing animal and human health from the cellular level through entire ecosystems. Wolfpack Perks and Benefits As a Pack member, you belong here, and can enjoy exclusive perks designed to enhance your personal and professional well-being. As you consider this opportunity, we encourage you to review our Employee Value Proposition and learn more about what makes NC State the best place to learn and work for everyone. What we offer: Medical , Dental , and Vision Flexible Spending Account Retirement Programs Disability Plans Life Insurance Accident Plan Paid Time Off and Other Leave Programs 12 Holidays Each Year Tuition and Academic Assistance And so much more! Attain Work-life balance with our Childcare benefits, Wellness & Recreation Membership , and Wellness Programs that aim to build a thriving wolfpack community. Disclaimer: Perks and Benefit eligibility is based on Part-Time or Full-Time Employment status. Eligibility and Employer Sponsored Plans can be found within each of the links offered. Essential Job Duties Join our team as a Shipping and Receiving Assistant , a vital role supporting faculty, staff, and students across the Centennial Biomedical Campus. In this hands-on position, you will support daily receiving, asset tracking, mail runs, event setup, fleet care, and heavy equipment operation. You will also safely handle specialized items, including refrigerated supplies, controlled substances, anatomy specimens, and hazardous diagnostic samples. Key Responsibilities: This position plays a crucial role in supporting the sponsored activities of faculty, staff, and students within the College by performing a variety of tasks and responsibilities across different areas: Sign for and inventory all packages received daily from delivery trucks, confirming their accuracy against delivery manifests, including perishable, infectious, controlled substances, and valuable items. Conduct detailed inventories of all packages delivered to the Centennial Biomedical Campus, including various buildings and units within the college. Deliver packages to designated locations within the college campus, obtaining recipient signatures and recording delivery dates, especially for perishable items requiring refrigerated storage. Assist with the annual inventory of assets spread across multiple campuses and locations, including locating items, recording their details, and updating the university asset management system. Assist the Mail Room Manager with mail operations, including operation of the mail machine, deliveries and pickups from the local post office, courier runs, and retrieving pathology samples from the NC Department of Agriculture Veterinary Diagnostic Laboratory. Transport veterinary diagnostic samples to and from diagnostic laboratories, ensuring proper handling of infectious materials. Handle formaldehyde-preserved large and small animal cadavers for the Anatomy Lab, including transportation and use of protective equipment. Receive, document, and transport infectious disease samples for the Vector Born Laboratory to avoid public health risks. Locate and tag new purchases made by the college, documenting their details and entering them into the inventory database. Assist in documenting, tagging, and removing surplus items for disposal, adhering to safety procedures, and maintaining accurate inventory records. Assist with setting up and logistics for special events at the college, including deliveries, setup, and furniture rearrangement. Operate heavy equipment such as forklifts, pallet jacks, backhoes, dump trucks, and box trucks, ensuring proper safety training and certification. Assist with light maintenance on departmental vehicles, including fueling, cleaning, and scheduling maintenance and repairs. Assist with various moves within the college, including office and laboratory moves, and transporting heavy or delicate equipment. Provide customer service throughout the college and the College of Engineering Biomedical Engineering department, assisting customers with their needs. Demonstrate knowledge of various programs administered by Shipping and Receiving and explain them to others. Address various requests from customers across campus, ensuring policies and procedures are communicated and followed. Abilities Necessary to Perform Job Duties: Must be able to lift up to 50 pounds, with or without reasonable accommodations, on a frequent basis. Other Responsibilities Any physical assistance involving heavy items or multiple items to be moved as requested by supervisor. Other tasks and responsibilities may be assigned based on the needs of the organization and evolving priorities. Qualifications Minimum Experience/Education High school diploma or equivalency. Preferred Qualifications Previous experience operating a forklift, hand cart, hand truck, and dollies. Ability to operate Mail Sorting and Metering Machine is desired. Excellent oral and written communication skills with an emphasis on providing outstanding customer service. Strong computer skills with particular emphasis on Microsoft Excel or similar software, and the ability to learn and use on-line computer applications to track inventory and surplus. Detail oriented with strong organizational skills. Required License or Certification Valid driver’s license is required for this position. NC driver’s license within 60 days of hire. Valid NC Driver's License required Yes Commercial Driver's License Required? No Recruitment Dates and Special Instructions Job Open Date 08/21/2026 Earliest Close Date---- (Positions will be posted until 5:00 PM ET on this date. Positions remaining posted after this date are still accepting applications but may close at any time.) 08/28/2026 Notice to Applicants Please make sure that the work history you list on your application is identical to the work history listed on your resume. The application must be filled out completely, do not use the phrase “see resume”. Special Instructions Please include as attachments a resume/CV and contact information for at least 3 professional references. Position Details Position Number 00065085 Position Type SHRA Position Classification Band Title Support Services Associate Position Classification Band Level Journey Position Classification Salary Range $ 33,540  -  $ 58,335 Salary Grade Equivalency NC02 Alternate Option If no applicants apply who meet the required competency level and training & experience requirements, then management may consider other applicants. Salary would be determined based on competencies, equity, budget, and market considerations. Full Time Equivalent (FTE) (1.0 = 40 hours/week) 1.0 Appointment 12 Month Recurring Mandatory Designation - Adverse Weather Mandatory - Adverse Weather Mandatory Designation - Emergency Events Mandatory - Medical Emergencies Time Limited Position No Time-Limited Appointment Length (if applicable) Department Id 190701 - Property Management EEO NC State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal opportunities for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, and veteran status. The University encourages all qualified applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities, to apply. Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodations in the application and interview process are welcome to contact 919-513-0574 to speak with a representative of the Office of Equal Opportunity. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at (919) 515-2135 or workatncstate@ncsu.edu . Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. Degree(s) must be obtained prior to start date in order to meet qualifications and receive credit. NC State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn of this opportunity? NCSU Website Job Alert (automated email from our system) NCSU Executive Search Services Monster.com CareerBuilder.com InsideHigherEd.com HigherEdJobs.com Other Online Job Board Carolina Job Finder / Employment Guide Job / Career Fair The Chronicle of Higher Education Professional Journal Print Advertisement (Newspaper / Periodical) Radio / Television Advertisement Professional Organization Higher Education Recruitment Consortium (HERC) Direct Contact from NCSU HR Representative / Recruiter NCSU Employee Referral Social Media (LinkedIn, Twitter, Facebook, Other) Other If you learned about this vacancy from \"other source\" or \"other website\", please provide the source. (Open Ended Question) * Please select the response below that best describes your experience/education for the Support Services Associate position. High school diploma/GED Associate's, Bachelor's, Master's, and/or Doctorate in any field Did not complete high school but have a combination of high school education and office support experience to equal 4 years (ex. 1 year of high school and 3 years of experience) None of the above * Do you have previous experience operating a forklift? Yes No * Do you have Forklift Certification? Yes No * A valid driver's license (DL) is required and a North Carolina Driver's License (NCDL) must be obtained within 60 days of hire and maintained as a condition of employment. Do you have a valid driver's license or the ability to obtain one prior to start date, and the ability to obtain a North Carolina Driver's License within 60 days of hire? Yes, I have a valid NCDL and will maintain it as a condition of employment. Yes, I have a valid DL from another state and will obtain a NCDL within 60 days of hire and maintain it as a condition of employment. Yes, I have a valid DL from another state but cannot or will not obtain a NCDL within 60 days of hire. No, I do not have a valid DL from any state, but I will obtain a it within 60 days of hire and maintain it as a condition of employment. No, I do not have a valid DL from any state and cannot or will not obtain it. Application Materials Required Required Documents Resume Contact Information for References Optional Documents Cover Letter NC STATE UNIVERSITY RALEIGH, NC 27695 PHONE: (919) 515-2011 Privacy Accessibility Emergency Information Policies NC State Home © 2019 NC State University. All rights reserved To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
