    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/227271": {
      "title": "Position Information",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | Temporary Summer Camp Nurse - Ellerbe, NC Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) Temporary Summer Camp Nurse - Ellerbe, NC Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Attach: Contact information for 3 references Posting Details Position Information Posting Number PG195765TM Position Number 11ASO3655 Position Type Temporary Essential Job Duties Millstone 4H Educational Center is seeking licensed RNs to join our team for the 2026 Summer Camp season! The Camp Nurse serves as a vital member of the Camp Healthcare Team, and oversees all health care operations for approximately 120 residential campers each week. The ideal candidate will enjoy working with youth of all ages, have the ability to work in unpredictable outdoor conditions, and thrive in a fast-paced dynamic environment outside of the clinical setting. Due to the on-call nature of this position, applicants must be able to reside on-site (housing provided) or within a half-hour commute of camp for the duration of the summer season. If you want to apply your nursing skills to a residential camp setting and work with a team like no other, apply today! Primary Responsibilities: Ability to follow all health care policies/procedures as described in facility standing orders, treatment procedures, and Staff Manual On call to respond to medical emergencies at all times campers are on-site, including overnight Perform basic assessment and first aid for conditions including but not limited to: minor soft tissue and musculoskeletal injuries, insect bites/stings, dehydration, sunburns, general illness; providing follow-up checks as needed Facilitate proper medication administration, for both routine prescription and over the counter medications, during all administration periods throughout the day Maintain written medical records for all medications and treatments administered according to state and American Camp Association Standards Prepare and record insurance and accident report forms Oversee Sunday check-in and Friday check-out of all camper medications each week, discussing any medical concerns with parent/guardian as needed Review all camper health forms and communicate medical needs to counselors as necessary Manage a team of 1-2 Health Care Coordinators who may assist with primary and secondary responsibilities Prepare and distribute camper’s medication schedule list to all counselors before dinner on Sundays Secondary Responsibilities: Attend all relevant staff trainings Keep camp Infirmary and medical supply storage space clean and organized Prepare and distribute all campus first aid kits, conducting routine checks and restocks as necessary Perform medical supply/equipment inventory and place restock orders Work Schedule: The summer season runs from May 29th – August 7th, 2026. Workdays will begin at noon on Sunday of each week and end at noon on Friday. These positions demand a high level of responsibility and attention to detail. You will be on call 24/7 including overnight, meal times and during activities to ensure overall health of campers and staff. Lodging (7 days a week, if needed) and Meals (5 days a week) provided. Potential to modify to a part-time role based on applicant’s needs and experience, please contact us directly to discuss options. Child discount for camp is negotiable Is Time Limited No If Yes, Appointment Length Wolfpack Perks and Benefits As a Pack member, you belong here, and can enjoy exclusive perks designed to enhance your personal and professional well-being. As you consider this opportunity, we encourage you to review our Employee Value Proposition and learn more about what makes NC State the best place to learn and work for everyone. What we offer: Health Insurance for Temporary Employees Enhance your career with LEAD courses Attend non-revenue generating sporting events for free. Attain Work-life balance with our Childcare discounts , Wellness & Recreation Membership , and Wellness Programs that aim to build a thriving wolfpack community. Disclaimer: Perks and Benefit eligibility is based on Part-Time or Full-Time Employment status. Eligibility and Employer Sponsored Plans can be found within each of the links offered. Department Information Job City & State Ellerbe, NC Department Millstone 4H Center - Ellerbe, NC System Information Classification Title Temporary-Technical/Paraprofessional Working Title Temporary Summer Camp Nurse - Ellerbe, NC Position Information Requirements and Preferences Work Schedule 40 hours per week Other Work/Responsibilities n/a Minimum Experience/Education Currently licensed to practice as a LPN , RN, or APRN within the state of North Carolina Department Required Skills Must possess a positive attitude and professionalism Experience in nursing or medical field Ability to administer medication Ability to work independently & follow directions. Enjoy working with youth in an outdoor environment Ability to work in extreme weather conditions including high temperatures and inclement weather situations Ability to communicate effectively with camp staff, parents/guardians, and campers Ability to utilize critical thinking in emergency situations outside of the clinical environment and determine when a higher level of care is appropriate Preferred Years Experience, Skills, Training, Education First Aid/ CPR / AED certified Required License or Certification LPN , RN, or APRN Valid driver’s license Valid NC Driver's License required? Yes Commercial Driver's License Required? No Recruitment Recruitment Details Anticipated Hiring Range $28-$35/hr Recruitment Dates Job Open Date 02/09/2026 Applicant Information Quick Link https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/227268 EEO NC State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal opportunities for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, and veteran status. The University encourages all qualified applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities, to apply. Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodations in the application and interview process are welcome to contact 919-513-0574 to speak with a representative of the Office of Equal Opportunity. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at (919) 515-2135 or workatncstate@ncsu.edu . Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. Degree(s) must be obtained prior to start date in order to meet qualifications and receive credit. NC State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). How did you learn of this opportunity? NCSU Website Job Alert (automated email from our system) NCSU Executive Search Services Monster.com CareerBuilder.com InsideHigherEd.com HigherEdJobs.com Other Online Job Board Carolina Job Finder / Employment Guide Job / Career Fair The Chronicle of Higher Education Professional Journal Print Advertisement (Newspaper / Periodical) Radio / Television Advertisement Professional Organization Higher Education Recruitment Consortium (HERC) Direct Contact from NCSU HR Representative / Recruiter NCSU Employee Referral Social Media (LinkedIn, Twitter, Facebook, Other) Other If you learned about this vacancy from \"other source\" or \"other website\", please provide the source. (Open Ended Question) * Are you a currently licensed in North Carolina as a LPN, RN or APRN? Yes No * Describe your experience in the nursing/medical field. (Open Ended Question) * Do you possess the ability to administer medication? Yes No * Do you enjoy working with youth in an outdoor environment? Yes No * Are you able to communicate effectively with camp staff, parents/guardians, and campers? Yes No * Describe how you would handle an emergency situation outside of a clinical environment. How you would determine when higher level care is required. (Open Ended Question) * Do you have a valid driver’s license? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Contact Information for References Optional Documents NC STATE UNIVERSITY RALEIGH, NC 27695 PHONE: (919) 515-2011 Privacy Accessibility Emergency Information Policies NC State Home © 2019 NC State University. All rights reserved To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
