    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/234719": {
      "title": "Position Information",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | Cybersecurity Program Operations Analyst Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) Cybersecurity Program Operations Analyst Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number PG196182TM Position Number 13CAT3 Position Type Temporary Essential Job Duties The Friday Institute for Educational Innovation is a large, multi-faceted Institute housed in a 33,000 square foot state-of-the-art facility on NC State University’s Centennial Campus in Raleigh. Our work encompasses educational research, professional development, policy and program evaluation, and direct services to schools, districts, state departments of education and public- and private sector organizations. We are deeply involved in work throughout North Carolina, leading some of the major statewide K-12 education initiatives and working closely with the Department of Public Instruction, the State Board of Education, and the majority of school districts in the State on the transition to digital teaching and learning. Since opening in 2005, the Friday Institute has developed a strong national presence, working with organizations throughout the country, and is increasingly developing international connections. More information is available at http://www.fi.ncsu.edu . The Friday Institute supports the North Carolina Department of Public Instruction ( NCDPI ) K-12 Cybersecurity Program , which organizes and aligns business and technical functions across the state so that the Public School Unit ( PSU ) will have greater visibility into the people, processes, and technologies deployed for cybersecurity. The goal of the program is to help PSUs achieve Strong Cyber Hygiene and this position will be entirely focused on supporting this program. The K-12 Cybersecurity Program has expanded significantly, and the core team requires additional project and operational support. Friday Institute seeks a K-12 Cybersecurity Program Operations Analyst to assist with program communications and reporting, outreach, knowledge management, data utilization and metrics, dashboard development, project coordination, and other routine but critical activities that keep the program organized and efficient. This is a time-limited contract-based position that will provide services in support of the K-12 Cybersecurity Program under the terms, scope, and period of performance established in the applicable contract. Continuation of the position is contingent upon contract requirements, funding availability, satisfactory performance, and any applicable renewal or extension of the contract. Work in a North Carolina PSU is ideal, but not required. Familiarity with general K-12 IT practices and cybersecurity are essential. Due to access to security-sensitive information, only U.S. citizens living in the state of North Carolina should apply. All work must be completed on a university provided and managed Macbook. Is Time Limited Yes If Yes, Appointment Length Time limited to June 30, 2027 Wolfpack Perks and Benefits As a Pack member, you belong here, and can enjoy exclusive perks designed to enhance your personal and professional well-being.  As you consider this opportunity, we encourage you to review our Employee Value Proposition and learn more about what makes NC State the best place to learn and work for everyone. What we offer: Health Insurance for Temporary Employees Enhance your career with LEAD courses Attend non-revenue generating sporting events for free. Attain Work-life balance with our Childcare discounts , Wellness & Recreation Membership , and Wellness Programs that aim to build a thriving wolfpack community. Disclaimer: Perks and Benefit eligibility is based on Part-Time or Full-Time Employment status. Eligibility and Employer Sponsored Plans can be found within each of the links offered. Department Information Job City & State Raleigh, NC Department Friday Institute System Information Classification Title Temporary-Professional NonFaculty Working Title Cybersecurity Program Operations Analyst Position Information Requirements and Preferences Work Schedule Monday - Wednesday, 9:00 am - 5:00 pm Other Work/Responsibilities Outreach to PSUs to help support better cyber hygiene. Minimum Experience/Education B.S. in Computer Engineering, or B.S. in Computer Science or CISSP , or 6 years of relevant cybersecurity engineering. Department Required Skills Working knowledge of cybersecurity principles, NIST 800 framework, and CIS controls Preferred Years Experience, Skills, Training, Education Knowledge and experience in project management that can help manage and track program projects and initiative deliverables. Knowledge and experience in technical writing to support process improvement efforts by: Generating templates to streamline communications and external program information materials Ensure program internal and external documentation remain updated, consistent, and organized Leverage common GenAI platforms to support, enhance, and improve existing and future documentation and other program materials Knowledge and experience performing data analysis, reporting, and dashboard generation that helps the program team provide utilization, impact, and ROI metrics (macro & micro) for program services and resources to key stakeholdersWorking knowledge of IT infrastructure, cybersecurity concepts/governance, and cybersecurity and privacy frameworks Required License or Certification n/a Valid NC Driver's License required? Yes Commercial Driver's License Required? No Recruitment Recruitment Details Anticipated Hiring Range $45,000 - $60,000 Recruitment Dates Job Open Date 09/02/2026 Applicant Information Quick Link https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/234424 EEO NC State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal opportunities for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, and veteran status. The University encourages all qualified applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities, to apply. Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodations in the application and interview process are welcome to contact 919-513-0574 to speak with a representative of the Office of Equal Opportunity. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at (919) 515-2135 or workatncstate@ncsu.edu. Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. Degree(s) must be obtained prior to start date in order to meet qualifications and receive credit. NC State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). How did you learn of this opportunity? NCSU Website Job Alert (automated email from our system) NCSU Executive Search Services Monster.com CareerBuilder.com InsideHigherEd.com HigherEdJobs.com Other Online Job Board Carolina Job Finder / Employment Guide Job / Career Fair The Chronicle of Higher Education Professional Journal Print Advertisement (Newspaper / Periodical) Radio / Television Advertisement Professional Organization Higher Education Recruitment Consortium (HERC) Direct Contact from NCSU HR Representative / Recruiter NCSU Employee Referral Social Media (LinkedIn, Twitter, Facebook, Other) Other If you learned about this vacancy from \"other source\" or \"other website\", please provide the source. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Contact Information for References Optional Documents NC STATE UNIVERSITY RALEIGH, NC 27695 PHONE: (919) 515-2011 Privacy Accessibility Emergency Information Policies NC State Home © 2019 NC State University. All rights reserved To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
