    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/234261": {
      "title": "Alumni Coordinator",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | Alumni Coordinator Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) Alumni Coordinator Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please include as attachments a resume, cover letter, and contact information for at least 3 professional references. This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Applicants must be authorized to work in the United States without the need for current or future sponsorship. This position is open for current NC State Employees only, permanent or temporary. Posting Details Posting Information Posting Number PG194835EP Internal Recruitment Yes Working Title Alumni Coordinator Anticipated Hiring Range $40,000 - $45,000 @ .75FTE Work Schedule Mon-Fri 9am - 3 pm with occasional weekend events required. Job Location Raleigh, NC Department College Of Education About the Department About the NC State College of Education As one of the nation’s top-ranked colleges of education, NC State’s College of Education leads the way in North Carolina in preparing extraordinary educators, conducting transformational research, and engaging communities where they are to improve the educational outcomes of all learners and advance the greater good. The college’s faculty are widely-recognized thought leaders who use their research to transform the practice of teaching, learning, and leading. They have particular strengths in improving technology-enhanced learning and teaching; fostering community-based learning and PK-16 partnerships; and innovating leadership and workforce development, educational policy, and evaluation. About two-thirds of the faculty are grant active. They are engaged in over 225 active projects totaling $151 million, making them the most productive in terms of research activity compared with other colleges of education in North Carolina and among the Top 5% in the nation. The college has over 1,600 students studying across five graduate certificates, seven undergraduate majors, two undergraduate minors, 13 master’s degrees, three Ph.D., and two Ed.D. programs housed in three academic departments: Educational Leadership, Policy, and Human Development; Science, Technology, Engineering, and Mathematics Education; and Teacher Education and Learning Sciences, with approximately 130 tenure-track and professional-track faculty, 110 support and professional staff, and about 160 graduate and teaching assistants. The College of Education is also home to the Belk Center for Community College Leadership and Research, the Friday Institute for Educational Innovation, and Elevate, NC State’s inclusive postsecondary education program for students with intellectual and developmental disabilities. The college has over 18,000 living alumni, with over 6,000 working in public schools in every county in North Carolina. Those who are teachers rate among the highest in effectiveness on surveys of school employers in North Carolina. NC State promotes an integrated approach to problem solving that transforms lives and provides leadership for social, economic, and technological development across North Carolina and around the world. NC State’s land grant mission of teaching, research and service is dedicated to the service of North Carolina and its people. Applicants are encouraged to review the institution’s mission, vision and strategic plan, and consider how their background, interest and experience would enable them to support the university. Wolfpack Perks and Benefits As a Pack member, you belong here, and can enjoy exclusive perks designed to enhance your personal and professional well-being. As you consider this opportunity, we encourage you to review our Employee Value Proposition and learn more about what makes NC State the best place to learn and work for everyone. What we offer: Medical , Dental , and Vision Flexible Spending Account Retirement Programs Disability Plans Life Insurance Accident Plan Paid Time Off and Other Leave Programs 12 Holidays Each Year Tuition and Academic Assistance And so much more! Attain Work-life balance with our Childcare benefits, Wellness & Recreation Membership , and Wellness Programs that aim to build a thriving wolfpack community. Disclaimer: Perks and Benefit eligibility is based on Part-Time or Full-Time Employment status. Eligibility and Employer Sponsored Plans can be found within each of the links offered. Essential Job Duties The Alumni Coordinator serves as a key relationship-builder and ambassador for the College of Education by developing, strengthening, and sustaining meaningful connections with alumni, students, faculty, staff, donors, and community partners. This position is responsible for advancing alumni engagement initiatives that foster lifelong relationships with the college and promote a strong sense of community, pride, and philanthropic support. Through strategic outreach, impactful programming, stewardship activities, communications, and events, the Alumni Coordinator plays an essential role in enhancing alumni participation, volunteerism, mentorship opportunities, and advancement efforts in support of the college’s mission and long-term strategic priorities. This position works collaboratively across the college to cultivate a vibrant alumni network that supports student success, professional development, career exploration, community engagement, and institutional advancement. This role requires a highly relational, organized, and proactive professional who is passionate about higher education, engagement, and building authentic relationships across populations and generations of alumni. Key Responsibilities Alumni Communications & Engagement Develop and support alumni engagement communication initiatives designed to strengthen alumni connection, participation, and affinity with the College of Education. Assist in the creation and coordination of alumni-focused content including digital newsletters, email campaigns, donor stewardship messaging, alumni spotlights, event promotions, social media collaboration, and engagement materials. Serve as a liaison and collaborative partner with university advancement and annual giving initiatives related to alumni outreach and engagement communications. Support strategic communication efforts that promote alumni networking, mentoring, volunteer engagement, continuing education opportunities, and professional development initiatives. Maintain and support accurate alumni records, contact information, engagement tracking, and participation data to strengthen outreach efforts and long-term relationship management. Analyze engagement trends and assist in identifying opportunities to increase alumni participation and connectivity across programs and initiatives. Relationship Development & Volunteer Engagement Cultivate, develop, and steward meaningful relationships with alumni across a broad range of backgrounds, professions, career stages, and geographic regions. Recruit and support alumni volunteers for mentorship programs, speaking engagements, networking initiatives, advisory opportunities, student engagement activities, and college events. Develop strategies to increase alumni involvement and strengthen connections between alumni, current students, faculty, and the broader college community. Conduct proactive outreach to alumni to preserve institutional relationships, strengthen long-term engagement, and enhance continuity of institutional knowledge and community connection. Identify and support opportunities for alumni leadership, advocacy, and volunteer participation in support of college initiatives and strategic priorities. Performs other duties as assigned in support of alumni programming, engagement events, continuing education initiatives, and the overall mission and strategic goals of the College of Education and Advancement Office. Alumni Programming, Events & Continuing Education Partner with alumni leadership groups and advisory boards to support the development and achievement of strategic alumni engagement goals and initiatives. Coordinate, plan, and facilitate alumni events and engagement activities including networking events, mentoring opportunities, reunions, continuing education initiatives, recognition programs, annual celebrations, tailgates, and special college events. Support the development of innovative programming that fosters professional growth, career connection, lifelong learning, and community engagement among alumni. Collaborate with internal and external partners to ensure successful execution of alumni engagement initiatives and programs. Assist with event logistics, communications, registration management, volunteer coordination, budgeting support, and post-event assessment activities. Other duties as assigned that support the mission, goals, and strategic priorities of the Alumni Coordinator role and the College of Education Advancement Office. Advancement & Philanthropic Engagement Support Partner with advancement and development staff to strengthen alumni engagement as it relates to philanthropy, donor cultivation, volunteerism, and institutional support. Support donor stewardship initiatives by assisting with gratitude communications, alumni recognition efforts, engagement tracking, and relationship-building activities. Assist with Day of Giving and other fundraising initiatives by coordinating student philanthropy activities, increasing alumni participation, and supporting donor engagement efforts. Help cultivate a culture of philanthropy and alumni investment within the College of Education community. This position is open for current NC State Employees only, permanent or temporary. Other Responsibilities Other duties as assigned that support the mission, goals, and strategic priorities of the Alumni Coordinator role and the College of Education Advancement Office Qualifications Minimum Education and Experience Bachelor’s degree and at least 1 year of professional experience in alumni relations, higher education, advancement, communications, student engagement, event coordination, nonprofit engagement, community outreach, or a related field; or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Other Required Qualifications Demonstrated ability to build authentic relationships and foster meaningful engagement with varied populations and stakeholders. Strong interpersonal, written, and verbal communication skills with the ability to engage effectively across multiple audiences and generations. Experience coordinating events, programs, outreach initiatives, or engagement activities with strong attention to detail and organizational effectiveness. Ability to work collaboratively in a team-oriented environment while also managing projects and responsibilities independently. Strong organizational, planning, and project coordination skills with the ability to manage multiple priorities simultaneously. Commitment to customer service, relationship management, and creating welcoming experiences for alumni, students, donors, and community members. Demonstrated professionalism, initiative, adaptability, and sound judgment in a fast-paced and evolving environment. Ability to maintain confidentiality and appropriately handle sensitive information. Preferred Qualifications Experience working in higher education, alumni relations, advancement, nonprofit engagement, constituent relations, or donor engagement environments. Knowledge of alumni engagement strategies, volunteer management practices, donor stewardship principles, and relationship cultivation approaches. Experience supporting mentorship initiatives, networking programs, leadership engagement, or community-building activities. Demonstrated experience planning and executing events, programs, or engagement initiatives with multiple stakeholders. Strong digital fluency and comfort utilizing web-based systems, constituent relationship management platforms, event registration systems, collaboration tools, databases, and content management systems. Experience utilizing data and engagement metrics to support outreach, relationship-building, and program improvement efforts. Ability to work occasional evenings and weekends in support of alumni events and engagement activities. Required License(s) or Certification(s) N/A Valid NC Driver's License required No Commercial Driver's License required No Recruitment Dates and Special Instructions Job Open Date 08/27/2026 Anticipated Close Date Open until filled Special Instructions to Applicants Please include as attachments a resume, cover letter, and contact information for at least 3 professional references. This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Applicants must be authorized to work in the United States without the need for current or future sponsorship. This position is open for current NC State Employees only, permanent or temporary. Position Details Position Number 00112229 Position Type EPS/SAAO Full Time Equivalent (FTE) (1.0 = 40 hours/week) .75 Appointment 12 Month Recurring Mandatory Designation - Adverse Weather Non Mandatory - Adverse Weather Mandatory Designation - Emergency Events Non Mandatory - Emergency Event Department ID 130101 - College Of Education EEO NC State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal opportunities for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, and veteran status. The University encourages all qualified applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities, to apply. Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodations in the application and interview process are welcome to contact 919-513-0574 to speak with a representative of the Office of Equal Opportunity. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at (919) 515-2135 or workatncstate@ncsu.edu . Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. Degree(s) must be obtained prior to start date in order to meet qualifications and receive credit. NC State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn of this opportunity? NCSU Website NCSU Executive Search Services Monster.com CareerBuilder.com InsideHigherEd.com Other Online Job Board Carolina Job Finder / Employment Guide Job / Career Fair The Chronicle of Higher Education HERC Professional Journal Print Advertisement (Newspaper / Periodical) Professional Organization Direct Contact from NCSU HR Representative / Recruiter NCSU Employee Referral Social Media (LinkedIn, Twitter, Facebook, Other) Other If you learned about this vacancy from \"other source\" or \"other website\", please provide the source. (Open Ended Question) * Are you CURRENTLY a PERMANENT or TEMPORARY employee of NC State University? Yes No Application Materials Required Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Contact Information for References Optional Documents NC STATE UNIVERSITY RALEIGH, NC 27695 PHONE: (919) 515-2011 Privacy Accessibility Emergency Information Policies NC State Home © 2019 NC State University. All rights reserved To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/228340": {
      "title": "Open Rank Lecturer or Teaching Assistant Professor",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | Open Rank Lecturer or Teaching Assistant Professor Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) Open Rank Lecturer or Teaching Assistant Professor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. In addition to your application please submit a cover letter explaining your interest in the position, CV, and a separate document containing contact information for three professional references. Posting Details Posting Information Posting Number PG194529EP Internal Recruitment No Working Title Open Rank Lecturer or Teaching Assistant Professor Anticipated Hiring Range Commensurate with Education and Experience Work Schedule Varies according to need Job Location Raleigh, NC Department World Languages and Cultures About the Department The Department of World Languages & Cultures at NC State provides students with a broad and intimate understanding of the rich and varied cultures of our globe—understanding that is built on solid competence of spoken and written skills in the language(s) you choose. At the undergraduate level, the Department offers students the opportunity to major in the following concentrations leading to the B.A. degree: Arabic, Asian Languages (Chinese, Japanese & Hindi/Urdu), French, German Studies, and Spanish. Students who are eager to make teaching their career can pursue the B.A. Degree in French, German, Spanish or Chinese Education. We also offer minors in the following: Arabic (through Middle Eastern Studies), Chinese, Classics (Greek and Latin), French, German Studies, Hindi/Urdu, Italian, Japanese, Portuguese, Russian, Spanish and World Literacy. In addition, we teach classes in Persian and English as a Second Language. At the graduate level, we have an M.A. program in World Languages & Cultures with two separate concentrations: one in French, and one in Spanish. Each of the concentrations incorporates literature, linguistics, and culture courses. We also have an M.A. program in TESOL . To provide students with more possibilities for languages or levels that may not be taught at NC State, we have developed an inter-institutional collaboration with other schools in the UNC System through a system-wide Language Exchange, so that we may provide greater language opportunities for our students. Wolfpack Perks and Benefits As a Pack member, you belong here, and can enjoy exclusive perks designed to enhance your personal and professional well-being. As you consider this opportunity, we encourage you to review our Employee Value Proposition and learn more about what makes NC State the best place to learn and work for everyone. What we offer: Medical , Dental , and Vision Flexible Spending Account Retirement Programs Disability Plans Life Insurance Accident Plan Paid Time Off and Other Leave Programs 12 Holidays Each Year Tuition and Academic Assistance And so much more! Attain Work-life balance with our Childcare benefits, Wellness & Recreation Membership , and Wellness Programs that aim to build a thriving wolfpack community. Disclaimer: Perks and Benefit eligibility is based on Part-Time or Full-Time Employment status. Eligibility and Employer Sponsored Plans can be found within each of the links offered. Essential Job Duties The successful candidate (s) will teach undergraduate courses in a specific discipline in World Languages & Cultures according to departmental need and employee knowledge, skills and ability. Courses may be taught in any of the languages for the classes that we offer. Appointments may be available part time for Summer 2026 and/or 2026-2027 Academic Year, all with the possibility of renewal. Other Responsibilities Other tasks and responsibilities may be assigned based on the needs of the organization and evolving priorities. Qualifications Minimum Education and Experience Master’s degree, an equivalent degree, or equivalent education and/or professional experience, for Lecturer. Bachelor’s degree plus 18 graduate credit hours will also be considered for Lecturer. PhD is necessary for rank of Assistant Teaching Professor. Degrees/credits must be received by start date . Other Required Qualifications Must demonstrate strong communication and interpersonal communication skills. Must demonstrate a commitment to excellence in teaching. Preferred Qualifications Instruction experience and proof of excellence in teaching at the undergraduate level are preferred. Required License(s) or Certification(s) N/A Valid NC Driver's License required No Commercial Driver's License required No Recruitment Dates and Special Instructions Job Open Date 03/12/2026 Anticipated Close Date Open Until Filled Special Instructions to Applicants In addition to your application please submit a cover letter explaining your interest in the position, CV, and a separate document containing contact information for three professional references. Position Details Position Number 00102362 Position Type Non-Tenure-Track Faculty Full Time Equivalent (FTE) (1.0 = 40 hours/week) up to 1.0 Appointment 9 Month Recurring Mandatory Designation - Adverse Weather Non Mandatory - Adverse Weather Mandatory Designation - Emergency Events Non Mandatory - Emergency Event Department ID 160401 - World Languages and Cultures EEO NC State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal opportunities for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, and veteran status. The University encourages all qualified applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities, to apply. Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodations in the application and interview process are welcome to contact 919-513-0574 to speak with a representative of the Office of Equal Opportunity. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at (919) 515-2135 or workatncstate@ncsu.edu . Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. Degree(s) must be obtained prior to start date in order to meet qualifications and receive credit. NC State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn of this opportunity? NCSU website Craigslist Indeed.com Carolina Job Finder/Employment Guide NC Works Dress for Success Technical/Trade School Program Job Fair (Identify Job Fair in question #2 below) Direct Contact from NSCU Representative (identify person in question #2 below) Other Monster.com Other online job board NCSU employee referral Social Media (LinkedIn, Twitter, Facebook, Ohter) If you learned about this vacancy from \"other source\" or \"other website\", please provide the source. (Open Ended Question) Application Materials Required Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Contact Information for References Optional Documents NC STATE UNIVERSITY RALEIGH, NC 27695 PHONE: (919) 515-2011 Privacy Accessibility Emergency Information Policies NC State Home © 2019 NC State University. All rights reserved To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
