    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/234485": {
      "title": "Director of Creative Media & Content Strategy",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | Director of Creative Media &amp; Content Strategy Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) Director of Creative Media & Content Strategy Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please attach resume and separate document containing contact information for 3 professional references. This posting is for current permanent NC State University employees only. Posting Details Posting Information Posting Number PG194850EP Internal Recruitment Yes Working Title Director of Creative Media & Content Strategy Anticipated Hiring Range Commensurate with experience Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 8am - 5pm; with nights, weekends and holidays as needed Job Location Raleigh, NC Department Athletics - Football About the Department The mission of the NC State University Department of Athletics is to prepare student-athletes to compete at the highest level and to inspire them to be leaders now and for the future by providing the best environment to achieve their athletic, academic, and personal aspirations as well as providing support for the professional development of our coaches and staff, all within the role of the greater institutional relationships to the University. The NC State Football program is a Division 1A FBS program in the Atlantic Coast Conference ( ACC ) within the National Collegiate Athletic Association ( NCAA ). Wolfpack Perks and Benefits As a Pack member, you belong here, and can enjoy exclusive perks designed to enhance your personal and professional well-being. As you consider this opportunity, we encourage you to review our Employee Value Proposition and learn more about what makes NC State the best place to learn and work for everyone. What we offer: Medical , Dental , and Vision Flexible Spending Account Retirement Programs Disability Plans Life Insurance Accident Plan Paid Time Off and Other Leave Programs 12 Holidays Each Year Tuition and Academic Assistance And so much more! Attain Work-life balance with our Childcare benefits, Wellness & Recreation Membership , and Wellness Programs that aim to build a thriving wolfpack community. Disclaimer: Perks and Benefit eligibility is based on Part-Time or Full-Time Employment status. Eligibility and Employer Sponsored Plans can be found within each of the links offered. Essential Job Duties Serve as the primary creative director responsible for overseeing all creative content (video, photography, graphic design, social media) ideation, creation, and delivery strategies for the football program. Responsibilities and duties include but are not limited to: Coordinates the creative direction, ideation, plans, estimates and timetables for football content Creation and distribution on social media channels, website, video boards and other external facing channels In collaboration with other athletic external units, help direct and guide messaging strategy and storytelling for the football program Coordinates the main creative content calendar for football, including sponsored content Oversight of all football day to day and game day creative operations and content collection – including but not limited to practices, workouts, team travel, in-game, pre-game & post-game Collaborate with coaching staff to produce internal highlight and motivational content Collaborate with recruiting staff to produce intentional and innovative content for the player acquisition process Coordinates the organization and archiving of all yearly creative content into athletic department storage platforms Oversight of the student creative intern program to include selection and onboarding expectations and compliance mentoring, training and development Oversee the forecasting, creating and tracking the football creative budget Purchasing and inventory of all equipment, technology, materials, and supplies Any other duties assigned by the General Manager and Head Coach Follow all compliance related rules of NC State University, NCAA & ACC This posting is for current permanent NC State University employees only. Other Responsibilities Other duties as assigned. This posting is for current permanent NC State University employees only. Qualifications Minimum Education and Experience Bachelor’s degree and minimum of two years of video production experience related to area of assignment or an equivalent combination of training and experience. All degrees must be received from appropriately accredited institutions. Other Required Qualifications Two years of experience capturing and editing football video content at the collegiate or professional level. Knowledge and experience with Adobe Creative Suite. Knowledge and experience with professional camera equipment. Knowledge and experience archiving creative content (photo, video, graphic) using ShareBrowser or similar software. Understanding of NCAA rules and regulations. Preferred Qualifications Proven success producing creative and innovative multi-media content. Experience in a wide range of multi-media production platforms (web sites, social media, animation, video and graphic design). Knowledge of a collegiate athletics department and the NCAA structure. Required License(s) or Certification(s) N/A Valid NC Driver's License required No Commercial Driver's License required No Recruitment Dates and Special Instructions Job Open Date 09/01/2026 Anticipated Close Date 09/15/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants Please attach resume and separate document containing contact information for 3 professional references. This posting is for current permanent NC State University employees only. Position Details Position Number 00107258 Position Type EPS/SAAO Full Time Equivalent (FTE) (1.0 = 40 hours/week) 1.0 Appointment 12 Month Recurring Mandatory Designation - Adverse Weather Mandatory - Adverse Weather Mandatory Designation - Emergency Events Non Mandatory - Emergency Event Department ID 101012 - Football EEO NC State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal opportunities for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, and veteran status. The University encourages all qualified applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities, to apply. Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodations in the application and interview process are welcome to contact 919-513-0574 to speak with a representative of the Office of Equal Opportunity. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at (919) 515-2135 or workatncstate@ncsu.edu . Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. Degree(s) must be obtained prior to start date in order to meet qualifications and receive credit. NC State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn of this opportunity? NCSU website Craigslist Indeed.com Carolina Job Finder/Employment Guide NC Works Dress for Success Technical/Trade School Program Job Fair (Identify Job Fair in question #2 below) Direct Contact from NSCU Representative (identify person in question #2 below) Other Monster.com Other online job board NCSU employee referral Social Media (LinkedIn, Twitter, Facebook, Ohter) If you learned about this vacancy from \"other source\" or \"other website\", please provide the source. (Open Ended Question) * Do you have (or will you have by date of hire) a bachelor's degree or higher? Yes No * Are you CURRENTLY a PERMANENT employee of NC State University? Yes No * Do you have a minimum of two years of experience capturing and editing football video content at the collegiate or professional level? Yes No * If yes, in 2-3 sentences please describe your relevant experience. (Open Ended Question) Application Materials Required Required Documents Resume Contact Information for References Optional Documents Cover Letter NC STATE UNIVERSITY RALEIGH, NC 27695 PHONE: (919) 515-2011 Privacy Accessibility Emergency Information Policies NC State Home © 2019 NC State University. All rights reserved To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
