    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/233521": {
      "title": "Position Information",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | Market Supervisor Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) Market Supervisor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Complete all required fields. Include 2 positions that are relevant to the posted position. **Important**If you are required to be registered by the Selective Service, please certify your compliance by your initials. If this question is not applicable to you, please type \"N/A\" along with your initials. Posting Details Position Information Posting Number PG196130TM Position Number 47MarketSupervisor0726 Position Type Temporary Essential Job Duties Are you a natural leader with a passion for hospitality, team building, and great food? Step up as a Temporary Market Supervisor with NC State Dining! In this role, you’ll do more than manage day-to-day market operations—you’ll set the tone for exceptional campus service, coach a dynamic crew, and gain valuable management experience with one of North Carolina’s premier university dining programs. Whether you are looking to build your resume or take the next step toward a permanent career in hospitality, our experienced leadership team is here to support your growth every step of the way. What You’ll Do Lead & Train: Supervise daily store operations, coach student and temporary staff, and foster a welcoming, high-energy environment. Deliver Hospitality: Serve as a champion for outstanding customer service, ensuring every guest leaves satisfied. Manage Operations & Inventory: Oversee point-of-sale (Micros POS ) transactions, maintain accurate financial paperwork, track inventory, and ensure smooth purchasing/selling workflows. Craft Quality Products: Safely prepare drinks and food to recipe standards—from pulling espresso shots and scooping ice cream to baking fresh cookies and making waffle cones. Maintain High Standards: Execute daily cleaning protocols to uphold our proud Grade “A” Sanitation rating. Adapt & Support: Pitch in across other dining locations as needed to keep campus running seamlessly. Why Join NC State Dining? Flexible Scheduling: Work-life balance built around your availability. Real Career Growth: Gain hands-on leadership experience with on-the-job training from dedicated industry professionals. A Pathway to More: Outstanding performance opens doors for contract renewal and potential advancement into benefits-eligible, permanent staff positions. Vibrant Campus Impact: Be part of a massive, energetic operation serving thousands of students, faculty, and staff daily across 25+ campus locations. Position Details Type: Hourly / Temporary Location: On-Campus (NC State University) Term Limit: Per State policy, temporary roles include a mandatory 31-day break after 24 months of continuous service. Superior performance offers opportunities to re-hire or transition to permanent roles. About NC State Dining NC State Dining is the heart of campus nourishment, operating 10 cafes, 3 food courts, 6 dining halls, 4 markets, a full-service restaurant, catering, vending, and nutritional counseling. Powered by a dedicated team of 1,000+ student and temporary staff alongside 190 permanent professionals, we are committed to service, quality, and community. Ready to lead on campus? Apply today and Join our Pack! If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at (919) 515-2135 or workatncstate@ncsu.edu . Is Time Limited No If Yes, Appointment Length Wolfpack Perks and Benefits As a Pack member, you belong here, and can enjoy exclusive perks designed to enhance your personal and professional well-being. What we offer: Health Insurance for Temporary Employees Enhance your career with LEAD courses Attend non-revenue generating sporting events for free. Attain Work-life balance with our Childcare discounts , Wellness & Recreation Membership , and Wellness Programs that aim to build a thriving wolfpack community. Disclaimer: Perks and Benefit eligibility is based on Part-Time or Full-Time Employment status. Eligibility and Employer Sponsored Plans can be found within each of the links offered. Department Information Job City & State Raleigh, NC Department NC State Dining System Information Classification Title Temporary-Skilled Trades Working Title Market Supervisor Position Information Requirements and Preferences Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 12 pm - 8:30 pm with rotating weekends Other Work/Responsibilities Be an ambassador for NC State Dining and the university as a whole and enrich the quality of life for the campus community and support student success. Work as a cohesive team member and play an integral part in creating a positive work environment. Minimum Experience/Education High School Diploma or equivalency Demonstrated possession of the competencies necessary to perform the work will also be considered. Department Required Skills Customer Service & Leadership Provide exemplary, courteous service to all guests, maintaining professionalism and composure during high-volume periods or difficult situations. Work collaboratively as an active, supportive member of a team. Communicate clearly and effectively with customers, peers, and management. Operational Skills & Execution Thrives in a fast-paced environment; adapts quickly to shifting customer volume with a strong sense of urgency. Accurately processes financial transactions using credit card and NC State One Card POS systems. Strong attention to detail with a proven track record of following written/verbal instructions and completing tasks efficiently. Intermediate computer literacy with the ability to quickly learn custom department software. Physical Demands & Environment: To succeed in this role, you must be comfortable standing, walking, bending, pushing, and pulling for extended periods, as well as lifting up to 30 lbs (with or without reasonable accommodation). Roles take place in active kitchen and dining settings, requiring adaptability to both hot and cold working conditions. Preferred Years Experience, Skills, Training, Education Previous experience working in a similar capacity. Supervising or purchasing experience. Experience on a college or university campus if helpful. Required License or Certification • ServSafe certificate a plus Valid NC Driver's License required? No Commercial Driver's License Required? No Recruitment Recruitment Details Anticipated Hiring Range $17.00 Recruitment Dates Job Open Date 08/05/2026 Applicant Information Quick Link https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/232150 EEO NC State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal opportunities for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, and veteran status. The University encourages all qualified applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities, to apply. Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodations in the application and interview process are welcome to contact 919-513-0574 to speak with a representative of the Office of Equal Opportunity. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at (919) 515-2135 or workatncstate@ncsu.edu . Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. Degree(s) must be obtained prior to start date in order to meet qualifications and receive credit. NC State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn of this opportunity? NCSU website Craigslist Indeed.com Carolina Job Finder/Employment Guide NC Works Dress for Success Technical/Trade School Program Job Fair (Identify Job Fair in question #2 below) Direct Contact from NSCU Representative (identify person in question #2 below) Other Monster.com Other online job board NCSU employee referral Social Media (LinkedIn, Twitter, Facebook, Ohter) If you learned about this vacancy from \"other source\" or \"other website\", please provide the source. (Open Ended Question) * Please briefly describe any previous cashier, stock clerk, or ordering experience you have had. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter NC STATE UNIVERSITY RALEIGH, NC 27695 PHONE: (919) 515-2011 Privacy Accessibility Emergency Information Policies NC State Home © 2019 NC State University. All rights reserved To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
