    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/231240": {
      "title": "Position Information",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | UTS -Temporary Environmental Services at NC State (4:00 AM – 12:30 PM) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) UTS -Temporary Environmental Services at NC State (4:00 AM – 12:30 PM) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number PG195864TM Position Number 48SM49 Position Type Temporary Essential Job Duties Thank you for applying with University Temporary Services! Please note, this application is the first step in the process of being considered for Environmental Services roles at NC State. This is not a specific position but rather, an application showing your skillset and interest in becoming a candidate for consideration with UTS . Main responsibilities: • Performing routine manual housekeeping work while cleaning various areas across campus. • Cleaning, mopping, scrubbing, sweeping, and vacuuming floors, as well as stairwells and hallways. • Cleaning of lavatories, washing windows, moving furniture to thoroughly clean areas, and collecting and removing trash. This is an ongoing recruitment. Is Time Limited Yes If Yes, Appointment Length 11 months Wolfpack Perks and Benefits As a Pack member, you belong here , and can enjoy exclusive perks designed to enhance your personal and professional well-being. As you consider this opportunity, we encourage you to review our Employee Value Proposition and learn more about what makes NC State the best place to learn and work for everyone. What we offer: Health Insurance for Temporary Employees Enhance your career with LEAD courses Attend non-revenue generating sporting events for free. Attain Work-life balance with our Childcare discounts , Wellness & Recreation Membership , and Wellness Programs that aim to build a thriving wolfpack community. Disclaimer: Perks and Benefit eligibility is based on Part-Time or Full-Time Employment status. Eligibility and Employer Sponsored Plans can be found within each of the links offered. Department Information Job City & State Raleigh, NC Department System Information Classification Title Temporary-Service Maintenance Working Title UTS -Temporary Environmental Services at NC State (4:00 AM – 12:30 PM) Position Information Requirements and Preferences Work Schedule A variety of shifts are available, 40 hours per week Other Work/Responsibilities Shifts Available: 4 AM – 12:30 PM, M – F Minimum Experience/Education 6 months of experience in Housekeeping- Knowledge of cleaning procedures, ability to follow instructions and to perform medium to heavy physical work (with or without reasonable accommodation); or an equivalent combination of training and experience. Special certification may be required for some of these positions. Department Required Skills Candidates: • Must have working knowledge of housekeeping and cleaning procedures including the proper utilization of cleaning chemicals and supplies. • Must be able to read, write and follow written and oral instructions in English • Must be able to visually inspect work area to assure it has been cleaned. • Physical requirements include walking, bending, stooping and lifting up to 50 lbs with or without accommodation Preferred Years Experience, Skills, Training, Education • 6+ months of professional cleaning experience strongly preferred. Required License or Certification N/A Valid NC Driver's License required? No Commercial Driver's License Required? No Recruitment Recruitment Details Anticipated Hiring Range $18.00 per hour Recruitment Dates Job Open Date 03/26/2026 Applicant Information Quick Link https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/228774 EEO NC State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal opportunities for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, and veteran status. The University encourages all qualified applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities, to apply. Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodations in the application and interview process are welcome to contact 919-513-0574 to speak with a representative of the Office of Equal Opportunity. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at (919) 515-2135 or workatncstate@ncsu.edu. Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. Degree(s) must be obtained prior to start date in order to meet qualifications and receive credit. NC State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What housekeeping shift are you interested in working? (Open Ended Question) * Do you have a minimum of 6 months of professional housekeeping experience? Yes No * Are you able to lift up to 50 lbs with or without reasonable accommodation? Yes No * Stooping, bending, climbing, lifting, pulling and walking are all routinely involved in conducting activities of this position.  Will you be able to perform these activities? Yes No * How did you hear about University Temporary Services? (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Contact Information for References NC STATE UNIVERSITY RALEIGH, NC 27695 PHONE: (919) 515-2011 Privacy Accessibility Emergency Information Policies NC State Home © 2019 NC State University. All rights reserved To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
