    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/231807": {
      "title": "Research Assistant",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | Research Assistant Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) Research Assistant Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please include a cover letter, resume, and contact information for at least three professional references. Posting Details Posting Information Posting Number PG194723EP Internal Recruitment No Working Title Research Assistant Anticipated Hiring Range $55,000 - $58,000 Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 8 am - 5 pm. . As the project involves working with live insects it may be necessary to work outside regular hours as needed. Job Location Raleigh, NC Department Entomology and Plant Pathology About the Department As part of the Land Grant University, the Department of Entomology and Plant Pathology in the College of Agriculture and Life Sciences at North Carolina State University is composed of over 40 faculty that direct a varied portfolio of programs in teaching, research, and extension. Collectively, these strengths not only serve our clientele and our science but also provide a rich environment for graduate education and training that can be tailored to the specific career interests of the student, irrespective of whether they prefer training in the basic sciences or are preparing for a career in extension. Our education and research programs provide graduate and undergraduate students with unique hands-on learning opportunities using the latest technologies. Entomology and Plant Pathology houses the Plant Disease and Insect Clinic, the Larry Grand Mycological Herbarium, Micropropagation and Repository Unit, Structural Pest Management Training Facility, an Insect Museum with 1.9 million vouchered insects, and the Center for Integrated Fungal Research. The College of Agriculture and Life Sciences houses 12 Academic departments with 294faculty, 2,891 undergraduate students and 899 graduate students. The College is home to 18 research stations strategically located across the state that enhances our interactions with our farmers, stakeholders, and industry partners. Wolfpack Perks and Benefits As a Pack member, you belong here, and can enjoy exclusive perks designed to enhance your personal and professional well-being. As you consider this opportunity, we encourage you to review our Employee Value Proposition and learn more about what makes NC State the best place to learn and work for everyone. What we offer: Medical , Dental , and Vision Flexible Spending Account Retirement Programs Disability Plans Life Insurance Accident Plan Paid Time Off and Other Leave Programs 12 Holidays Each Year Tuition and Academic Assistance And so much more! Attain Work-life balance with our Childcare benefits, Wellness & Recreation Membership , and Wellness Programs that aim to build a thriving wolfpack community. Disclaimer: Perks and Benefit eligibility is based on Part-Time or Full-Time Employment status. Eligibility and Employer Sponsored Plans can be found within each of the links offered. Essential Job Duties The Research Assistant will support a multidisciplinary research program focused on the development of CRISPR -based genetic control technologies for the New World screwworm and related blowfly species. This includes work on gene drive systems and precision-guided sterile insect techniques (pgSIT). The position integrates laboratory operations, insect colony management, biosafety compliance, and hands-on experimental support for genetic and molecular studies. Duties Include: Maintain fly stocks and provide staff with biological material at different stages of development when requested. Support postdoctoral fellows by performing blow fly crosses, examining the progeny and setting additional crosses with selected offspring. Purchase supplies. Autoclaving insect waste. Supervise undergraduate students who support insect rearing. Other Responsibilities Responsible for ensuring that all safety/biosafety requirements are met. Update safety plan and SOP for BUA as needed. Qualifications Minimum Education and Experience Relevant Master’s degree OR Relevant Bachelor’s degree and 3 or more years of relevant experience, or relevant independent experience and education Other Required Qualifications Ability to: Operate microscopes Use pipette man Work with live insects in cages Operate autoclave Preferred Qualifications MS in entomology or related discipline Required License(s) or Certification(s) Valid NC Driver’s License Valid NC Driver's License required Yes Commercial Driver's License required No Recruitment Dates and Special Instructions Job Open Date 06/17/2026 Anticipated Close Date Open Until Filled Special Instructions to Applicants Please include a cover letter, resume, and contact information for at least three professional references. Position Details Position Number 00112139 Position Type EPS/SAAO Full Time Equivalent (FTE) (1.0 = 40 hours/week) 1.00 Appointment 12 Month Recurring Mandatory Designation - Adverse Weather Non Mandatory - Adverse Weather Mandatory Designation - Emergency Events Non Mandatory - Emergency Event Department ID 111801 - Entomology and Plant Pathology EEO NC State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal opportunities for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, and veteran status. The University encourages all qualified applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities, to apply. Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodations in the application and interview process are welcome to contact 919-513-0574 to speak with a representative of the Office of Equal Opportunity. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at (919) 515-2135 or workatncstate@ncsu.edu . Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. Degree(s) must be obtained prior to start date in order to meet qualifications and receive credit. NC State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn of this opportunity? NCSU Website Job Alert (automated email from our system) NCSU Executive Search Services Monster.com CareerBuilder.com InsideHigherEd.com Other Online Job Board Carolina Job Finder / Employment Guide Job / Career Fair The Chronicle of Higher Education Professional Journal Print Advertisement (Newspaper / Periodical) Professional Organization Direct Contact from NCSU HR Representative / Recruiter NCSU Employee Referral Social Media (LinkedIn, Twitter, Facebook, Other) Other If you learned about this vacancy from \"other source\" or \"other website\", please provide the source. (Open Ended Question) * Which of the following best describes your education and experience? Relevant Master’s degree Relevant Bachelor’s and 3 or more years of relevant experience, or relevant independent experience and education Neither of the above Application Materials Required Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Contact Information for References Optional Documents NC STATE UNIVERSITY RALEIGH, NC 27695 PHONE: (919) 515-2011 Privacy Accessibility Emergency Information Policies NC State Home © 2019 NC State University. All rights reserved To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/233290": {
      "title": "Position Information",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | Equine and Farm Animal Attendant Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) Equine and Farm Animal Attendant Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number PG195768TM Position Number 19PLS05708 Position Type Temporary Essential Job Duties This temporary position will be responsible for maintaining a clean and sanitary hospital through routine stall/cage maintenance, hospital cleaning and disinfection, and waste removal. Restrain and provide basic husbandry for equine and farm animal patients. Small animal hospital backup, same duties. Is Time Limited No If Yes, Appointment Length Wolfpack Perks and Benefits As a Pack member, you belong here , and can enjoy exclusive perks designed to enhance your personal and professional well-being. As you consider this opportunity, we encourage you to review our Employee Value Proposition and learn more about what makes NC State the best place to learn and work for everyone. What we offer: Health Insurance for Temporary Employees Enhance your career with LEAD courses Attend non-revenue generating sporting events for free. Attain Work-life balance with our Childcare discounts , Wellness & Recreation Membership , and Wellness Programs that aim to build a thriving wolfpack community. Disclaimer: Perks and Benefit eligibility is based on Part-Time or Full-Time Employment status. Eligibility and Employer Sponsored Plans can be found within each of the links offered. Department Information Job City & State Raleigh, NC Department System Information Classification Title Temporary-Skilled Trades Working Title Equine and Farm Animal Attendant Position Information Requirements and Preferences Work Schedule Sat - Tues, 1:00 PM - 12 am,  varies with occasional holiday coverage as needed. Other Work/Responsibilities N/A Minimum Experience/Education High School diploma or equivalent. Demonstrated experience in the handling and restraint of equine patients, including mares with foals, pregnant mares, and stallions, as well as othr farm animals. Proficiency in animal husbandry practices, cleaning and disinfection protocols, and basic facility maintneance skills are also required. Department Required Skills Must be able to lift up to 70 pounds. Ability to operate equipment such as forklifts, pressure washers, and basic power tools. Responsible for inventory management and accurately measuring and diluting chemicals according to established guidelines. Demonstrates safe, humane handling of all patients at all times. Must communicate effectively, work collaboratively within a team, and comply with all institutional policies and procedures, including safety requirements. Ability to commute to Reedy Creek Equine Farm to provide care. Preferred Years Experience, Skills, Training, Education Experience in restraining and providing husbandry care for equine and Farm Animal species is required. Preferred qualifications include prior experience working in a veterinary setting, working knowledge of infectious disease control programs, and familiarity with established safety programs. Candidates should demonstrate compliance with OSHA standards and awareness of veterinary accreditation and certification guidelines such as AAHA , AVMA , and related regulatory bodies. Required License or Certification Must have a valid NC driver’s license Valid NC Driver's License required? Yes Commercial Driver's License Required? No Recruitment Recruitment Details Anticipated Hiring Range $15.00 - $18.75 Recruitment Dates Job Open Date 02/10/2026 Applicant Information Quick Link https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/227277 EEO NC State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal opportunities for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, and veteran status. The University encourages all qualified applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities, to apply. Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodations in the application and interview process are welcome to contact 919-513-0574 to speak with a representative of the Office of Equal Opportunity. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at (919) 515-2135 or workatncstate@ncsu.edu. Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. Degree(s) must be obtained prior to start date in order to meet qualifications and receive credit. NC State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have experience handling and caring for horses? Yes No * Please describe any experience you have with equine and/or large animal care/animal husbandry you have. (Open Ended Question) Do you have experience operating a forklift, pressure washer and other basic power tools? (Open Ended Question) Do you have a valid NC driver's license or the ability to obtain one within 30 days of start date? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Contact Information for References Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter NC STATE UNIVERSITY RALEIGH, NC 27695 PHONE: (919) 515-2011 Privacy Accessibility Emergency Information Policies NC State Home © 2019 NC State University. All rights reserved To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
