    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/234603": {
      "title": "Director of Philanthropic Strategy & Prospect Management",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | Director of Philanthropic Strategy &amp; Prospect Management Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) Director of Philanthropic Strategy & Prospect Management Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please include as attachments a resume, cover letter, and contact information for at least 3 professional references. Posting Details Posting Information Posting Number PG194851EP Internal Recruitment No Working Title Director of Philanthropic Strategy & Prospect Management Anticipated Hiring Range Commensurate with experience and education Work Schedule 8:00 am - 5:00 pm Job Location Raleigh, NC Department Engineering Advancement About the Department About NC State: North Carolina State University (NC State) was founded in 1887 with the purpose of creating economic, societal and intellectual prosperity for the people of North Carolina. Today it is the largest university in North Carolina with more than 34,000 high-performing students, 8,000 pre-eminent faculty and staff and over 230,000 living alumni. NC State is known for its leadership in research, education and service and as a research extensive university, is recognized for its strengths in science, engineering and technology. The University consistently ranks among the top public universities and is one of the best values in higher education. In 2016, NC State launched the Think & Do the Extraordinary Campaign, the most ambitious fundraising effort in the history of the university with a $1.6 billion goal. Priorities include dramatically increasing endowment to benefit students and faculty, enhancing facilities and strengthening support for current operations. Primary Function of Organization: NC State is home to one of the world’s finest colleges of engineering and computer sciences. For the second year in a row the College ranked 25th overall in the US News and 12th among public institutions. In 2018-19, research expenditures in the College reached nearly $198 million which ranked 6th among public engineering colleges. NC State Engineering also serves as the lead institution on two National Science Foundation Engineering Research Centers. More than 10,000 students attend the College of Engineering involved in one of the 18 bachelors’, 21 master’s and 13 doctoral degree programs offered. There are nine academic departments including: Biomedical Engineering, Chemical and Biomolecular Engineering, Civil, Construction and Environmental Engineering, Computer Science, Electrical and Computer Engineering, Industrial and Systems Engineering, Materials Science Engineering, Mechanical and Aerospace Engineering and Nuclear Engineering. The College’s commitment to excellence is evidenced by the success of our faculty and students. Each year, both faculty and students receive numerous scholarly and professional awards for their teaching and technological achievements, and our graduates find top-notch careers in research and development, design, production, and management. Many of our 65,000 alumni hold leadership positions in government and both private and public sector institutions around the world. Chartered in 1944, the NC State Engineering Foundation, Inc. ( NCSEF ) is a private 501c3 non-profit organization which raises funds from alumni, friends, industry-related foundations and other sources to support the College of Engineering at NC State. Current fundraising initiatives include scholarships, fellowships, professorships, study abroad funds, and capital projects like Fitts-Woolard Hall (the fourth Engineering building to be built on Centennial Campus). Wolfpack Perks and Benefits As a Pack member, you belong here, and can enjoy exclusive perks designed to enhance your personal and professional well-being. As you consider this opportunity, we encourage you to review our Employee Value Proposition and learn more about what makes NC State the best place to learn and work for everyone. What we offer: Medical , Dental , and Vision Flexible Spending Account Retirement Programs Disability Plans Life Insurance Accident Plan Paid Time Off and Other Leave Programs 12 Holidays Each Year Tuition and Academic Assistance And so much more! Attain Work-life balance with our Childcare benefits, Wellness & Recreation Membership , and Wellness Programs that aim to build a thriving wolfpack community. Disclaimer: Perks and Benefit eligibility is based on Part-Time or Full-Time Employment status. Eligibility and Employer Sponsored Plans can be found within each of the links offered. Essential Job Duties The Director of Philanthropic Strategy & Prospect Management serves as the College of Engineering’s strategic advisor on fundraising performance, portfolio optimization, campaign readiness, and prospect strategy. This position partners closely with the Assistant Dean for Philanthropy and frontline fundraisers to maximize philanthropic results through data-informed decision making, fundraising analytics, CRM leadership, and strategic portfolio management. Rather than serving solely as a prospect manager, this role functions as a strategic partner to fundraising leadership by helping ensure gift officers are focused on the highest-impact opportunities and equipped with the information, systems, and strategy necessary to maximize fundraising success. Core Responsibilities 1. Philanthropic Strategy Provide strategic guidance that strengthens fundraising performance across the College. Key Responsibilities Serve as strategic advisor to the Assistant Dean and Executive Director on fundraising priorities and campaign readiness. Lead portfolio optimization and prospect assignment strategies. Facilitate prospect strategy meetings with frontline fundraisers. Identify opportunities, risks, and trends within all levels of the major gift fundraising pipeline – focusing on the continuum from major gift discovery to major gifts to principal giving. Develop recommendations to maximize fundraising productivity and philanthropic outcomes. Support campaign planning and principal gift pipeline development. 2. Prospect Management Lead the strategic management of prospect portfolios to maximize fundraiser effectiveness. Key Responsibilities Oversee portfolio management and assignment processes. Monitor prospect movement through the donor pipeline. Ensure portfolio health and accountability. Conduct regular portfolio reviews with gift officers. Coordinate closely with University Advancement Prospect Development on prospect management and research, working closely with analysts on research projects to fill fundraiser portfolios & gaps. Develop recommendations for prospect assignment and portfolio balancing. 3. CRM Strategy & Salesforce (Lobo) Leadership Serve as the College’s functional expert for Salesforce (Lobo), ensuring the CRM effectively supports fundraising strategy and frontline success. Key Responsibilities Serve as the College of Engineering’s primary functional lead for Salesforce (Lobo). Partner with University Advancement on CRM implementation, enhancements, testing, and user adoption. Develop best practices, workflows, and business processes within Salesforce. Train and support frontline fundraisers in the effective use of the CRM . Ensure data quality and consistency across fundraising operations. Translate fundraising needs into CRM solutions that improve efficiency and effectiveness. Identify opportunities to leverage Salesforce to improve fundraising performance and reporting. 4. Fundraising Analytics & Performance Provide meaningful data and analysis that informs leadership decisions and drives fundraising success. Key Responsibilities Develop executive dashboards and performance reports in Salesforce that track activity, strategy and pipeline health. Monitor fundraising KPIs and portfolio metrics. Analyze pipeline health and fundraising trends. Forecast fundraising performance and campaign progress. Track proposal activity and donor movement. Produce regular reports that support strategic decision making by the Assistant Dean and fundraising leadership. Other Responsibilities Other duties as assigned. Qualifications Minimum Education and Experience Requires a relevant post-baccalaureate degree with a minimum of three (3) years or greater of related professional experience, or a relevant undergraduate degree and a minimum of five (5) years or greater of relevant experience may be substituted for the advanced degree. Other Required Qualifications Strong communication (written and verbal) and organizational skills. Enthusiasm for fund-raising in a public university. Effective ability to multi-task. Ability to work with multiple and varied constituencies. Collegiality; ability to work as part of a team in a goal-oriented environment. Preferred Qualifications Ability to learn database applications. Required License(s) or Certification(s) Driver’s license required to make visits and attend events. Valid NC Driver's License required Yes Commercial Driver's License required No Recruitment Dates and Special Instructions Job Open Date 09/03/2026 Anticipated Close Date Open until filled Special Instructions to Applicants Please include as attachments a resume, cover letter, and contact information for at least 3 professional references. Position Details Position Number 00103158 Position Type EPS/SAAO Full Time Equivalent (FTE) (1.0 = 40 hours/week) 1.00 Appointment 12 Month Recurring Mandatory Designation - Adverse Weather Non Mandatory - Adverse Weather Mandatory Designation - Emergency Events Non Mandatory - Emergency Event Department ID 143801 - Engineering Advancement EEO NC State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal opportunities for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, and veteran status. The University encourages all qualified applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities, to apply. Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodations in the application and interview process are welcome to contact 919-513-0574 to speak with a representative of the Office of Equal Opportunity. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at (919) 515-2135 or workatncstate@ncsu.edu . Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. Degree(s) must be obtained prior to start date in order to meet qualifications and receive credit. NC State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn of this opportunity? NCSU Website Job Alert (automated email from our system) NCSU Executive Search Services Monster.com CareerBuilder.com InsideHigherEd.com HigherEdJobs.com Other Online Job Board Carolina Job Finder / Employment Guide Job / Career Fair The Chronicle of Higher Education Professional Journal Print Advertisement (Newspaper / Periodical) Radio / Television Advertisement Professional Organization Higher Education Recruitment Consortium (HERC) Direct Contact from NCSU HR Representative / Recruiter NCSU Employee Referral Social Media (LinkedIn, Twitter, Facebook, Other) Other If you learned about this vacancy from \"other source\" or \"other website\", please provide the source. (Open Ended Question) * Do you have (or will you have by date of hire) a bachelor's degree or higher? Yes No * Do you have experience (professional, student, and/or volunteer) in development or alumni relations? Yes No * Describe your relevant experience as it relates to this position. Highlight the knowledge, skills, and accomplishments that have prepared you to be successful in this role. (300 words or less) (Open Ended Question) Application Materials Required Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Contact Information for References Optional Documents NC STATE UNIVERSITY RALEIGH, NC 27695 PHONE: (919) 515-2011 Privacy Accessibility Emergency Information Policies NC State Home © 2019 NC State University. All rights reserved To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/234113": {
      "title": "Position Information",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | Postdoctoral Research Scholar Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) Postdoctoral Research Scholar Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please attach a Cover Letter, resume/CV, and contact information for three (3) professional references. Please make sure that the information entered on the application matches what is on your resume. Posting Details Position Information Posting Number PG191578PD Position Number 00111692 Position Type Post Doc FLSA Exempt Departmental Information Department ID 110901 - Crop and Soil Sciences Department 110901 - Crop and Soil Sciences Job City & State Raleigh, NC Position Information Position Overview Essential Job Duties The Department of Crop and Soil Sciences encompasses varied disciplines in research, extension, and teaching. The department’s mission is to develop future leaders in crop, soil, and environmental sciences, improve crop plants and products, devise effective and sustainable crop production systems, devise effective and sustainable soil management techniques in both agriculture and urban settings; and disseminate crop, soil, and environmental science knowledge for the benefit of users and producers of food, feed turf, biofuels and fiber in North Carolina, the nation and the world. The successful candidate will conduct independent and collaborative research to develop and elucidate bio-physical-chemical mechanisms that regulate soil carbon sequestration, nitrogen retention, and greenhouse gas ( GHG ) emissions mitigation in agricultural systems. The primary focus will be on understanding how soil amendments derived from bioenergy production byproducts influence soil processes and ecosystem sustainability. Key responsibilities include: Collect soil samples and set up microcosm experiments. Measure soil fluxes of carbon dioxide and nitrous oxide. Conduct metagenomic DNA extraction and shotgun sequencing. Perform bioinformatics and statistical data analyses. Prepare manuscripts and present research findings in professional meetings. Work closely with team members and help train graduate students. Other Work/Responsibilities Design experiments, collect and analyze data, and prepare manuscripts Wolfpack Perks and Benefits As a Pack member, you belong here , and can enjoy exclusive perks designed to enhance your personal and professional well-being. As you consider this opportunity, we encourage you to review our Employee Value Proposition and learn more about what makes NC State the best place to learn and work for everyone. What we offer: Medical, Dental, Vision, Retirement and Leave Faculty and Staff Assistance Program Enhance your career with LEAD courses Attend non-revenue generating sporting events for free. Attain Work-life balance with our Childcare benefits, Wellness & Recreation Membership , and Wellness Programs that aim to build a thriving wolfpack community. Disclaimer: Perks and Benefit eligibility is based on Part-Time or Full-Time Employment status. Eligibility and Employer Sponsored Plans can be found within each of the links offered. Requirements and Preferences Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 8 am - 5 pm Department Required Skills n/a Preferred Years Experience, Skills, Training, Education Ph.D. in a discipline relevant to soil carbon and nitrogen dynamics (e.g., biogeochemistry, microbiology, ecology). Experience with contemporary techniques in soil physics, chemistry, and microbiology. Excellent writing and communication skills in English Required License or Certification n/a Valid NC Driver's License required? No Commercial Driver's License Required? No Recruitment Recruitment Details Anticipated Hiring Range commensurate with experience ($58,656 – $60,000) If you anticipate multiple hires from this search, please indicate how many Recruitment Dates Job Open Date 08/24/2026 Applicant Information Quick Link https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/224616 EEO NC State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal opportunities for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, and veteran status. The University encourages all qualified applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities, to apply. Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodations in the application and interview process are welcome to contact 919-513-0574 to speak with a representative of the Office of Equal Opportunity. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at (919) 515-2135 or workatncstate@ncsu.edu . Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. Degree(s) must be obtained prior to start date in order to meet qualifications and receive credit. NC State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn of this opportunity? NCSU Website NCSU Executive Search Services Monster.com CareerBuilder.com InsideHigherEd.com Other Online Job Board Carolina Job Finder / Employment Guide Job / Career Fair The Chronicle of Higher Education HERC Professional Journal Print Advertisement (Newspaper / Periodical) Professional Organization Direct Contact from NCSU HR Representative / Recruiter NCSU Employee Referral Social Media (LinkedIn, Twitter, Facebook, Other) Other If you learned about this vacancy from \"other source\" or \"other website\", please provide the source. (Open Ended Question) * According to our university's regulations, a postdoctoral scholar needs to have successfully completed their terminal degree no more than 5 years from the start date of their appointment.  Given this, please provide the date (MM/DD/YYYY) your terminal degree has been or will be confirmed. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Contact Information for References Resume/CV Optional Documents NC STATE UNIVERSITY RALEIGH, NC 27695 PHONE: (919) 515-2011 Privacy Accessibility Emergency Information Policies NC State Home © 2019 NC State University. All rights reserved To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/227722": {
      "title": "Lecturer",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | Lecturer Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) Lecturer Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please include as attachments a resume/CV, cover letter, and contact information for at least 3 professional references. Posting Details Posting Information Posting Number PG194504EP Internal Recruitment No Working Title Lecturer Anticipated Hiring Range $5,063 - $5,500 per course (depending on degree attained) Work Schedule Varies based on teaching schedule Job Location Raleigh, NC Department Department of Communication About the Department The Department of Communication is one of the largest departments in the College of Humanities and Social Sciences at NC State, with over 700 undergraduate majors and about 70 full- or part-time graduate students (M.S. and Ph.D.). We have two graduate programs: a Masters of Science in Communication and an interdisciplinary PhD program in Communication, Rhetoric and Digital Media in partnership with the Department of English. The Department of Communication at NC State is an accomplished community of students, staff members, teachers, and researchers with varied intellectual interests in the communication arts and sciences. Through our teaching, research and service, we cultivate responsible, caring and collaborative communication practices for our students, our community partners and the global citizenry. We do this because communication is central to addressing the significant challenges and opportunities of the 21st Century and we are committed to enabling people, organizations and communities to thrive. Wolfpack Perks and Benefits As a Pack member, you belong here, and can enjoy exclusive perks designed to enhance your personal and professional well-being. As you consider this opportunity, we encourage you to review our Employee Value Proposition and learn more about what makes NC State the best place to learn and work for everyone. What we offer: Medical , Dental , and Vision Flexible Spending Account Retirement Programs Disability Plans Life Insurance Accident Plan Paid Time Off and Other Leave Programs 12 Holidays Each Year Tuition and Academic Assistance And so much more! Attain Work-life balance with our Childcare benefits, Wellness & Recreation Membership , and Wellness Programs that aim to build a thriving wolfpack community. Disclaimer: Perks and Benefit eligibility is based on Part-Time or Full-Time Employment status. Eligibility and Employer Sponsored Plans can be found within each of the links offered. Essential Job Duties The Department of Communication at North Carolina State University (NC State) invites applications for part-time Lecturer positions. Multiple hires may be made from this posting, with most positions being part-time and requiring in-person instruction. The position(s) are one-semester or one-year, non-tenure-track appointments with the possibility of renewal. Primary responsibilities include teaching undergraduate courses in communication as well as coordinating, planning, preparing, delivering, and evaluating classroom instruction and related activities. Other duties may be negotiated with the department head. Other Responsibilities Other tasks and responsibilities may be assigned based on the needs of the organization and evolving priorities. Qualifications Minimum Education and Experience Requires master’s degree, an equivalent degree, or equivalent professional experience. Other Required Qualifications Commitment to teaching excellence. Excellent communication skills. Preferred Qualifications Teaching experience in communication at the college level and demonstrated teaching excellence. Required License(s) or Certification(s) N/A Valid NC Driver's License required No Commercial Driver's License required No Recruitment Dates and Special Instructions Job Open Date 02/23/2026 Anticipated Close Date Open Until Filled Special Instructions to Applicants Please include as attachments a resume/CV, cover letter, and contact information for at least 3 professional references. Position Details Position Number 00005037 Position Type Non-Tenure-Track Faculty Full Time Equivalent (FTE) (1.0 = 40 hours/week) 0.225 - 1.0, depending on department needs Appointment 9 Month Recurring Mandatory Designation - Adverse Weather Non Mandatory - Adverse Weather Mandatory Designation - Emergency Events Non Mandatory - Emergency Event Department ID 160701 - Communication EEO NC State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal opportunities for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, and veteran status. The University encourages all qualified applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities, to apply. Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodations in the application and interview process are welcome to contact 919-513-0574 to speak with a representative of the Office of Equal Opportunity. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at (919) 515-2135 or workatncstate@ncsu.edu . Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. Degree(s) must be obtained prior to start date in order to meet qualifications and receive credit. NC State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn of this opportunity? NCSU website Craigslist Indeed.com Carolina Job Finder/Employment Guide NC Works Dress for Success Technical/Trade School Program Job Fair (Identify Job Fair in question #2 below) Direct Contact from NSCU Representative (identify person in question #2 below) Other Monster.com Other online job board NCSU employee referral Social Media (LinkedIn, Twitter, Facebook, Ohter) If you learned about this vacancy from \"other source\" or \"other website\", please provide the source. (Open Ended Question) Application Materials Required Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Contact Information for References Optional Documents NC STATE UNIVERSITY RALEIGH, NC 27695 PHONE: (919) 515-2011 Privacy Accessibility Emergency Information Policies NC State Home © 2019 NC State University. All rights reserved To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
