    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/233988": {
      "title": "Position Information",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | UTS - Temporary Recycling Collections Operator at NC State Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) UTS - Temporary Recycling Collections Operator at NC State Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number PG196166TM Position Number 48TT02 Position Type Temporary Essential Job Duties Bulk Waste and Electronics Collections – scheduled route collections average of 180 sites per week for materials and electronics not accepted in the automated or recycling collection system. Related transport and sorting into appropriate materials bins at the Dearstyne Rolloff Site. Bulk material collections include items such as pallets, crates, discarded furniture, scrap metal, electronics, etc. Recycling and Reuse Collections – customer requested collections of reuse, recycling and unwanted building items and hauling to Dearstyne for recycling or disposal. This is on demand service for campus customers and response time is offered within 1-2 business days of the initial request. Common requests include delivery and pick up of carts for office clean outs, pick up and signature collections of confidential recycling, preparing and distributing materials for reuse in other areas or departments. Events and Projects – Field support to provide special waste/recycling/compost service for campus events and support major activities on campus such as residence hall move in and move out where additional services, monitoring and staff support are needed for collections. Repair, Maintenance, Safety – provide inspection and maintenance of containers related to the collection of waste and recycling on campus. Includes cleaning, proper labeling, delivery, distribution and placement of containers inside and outside of buildings. Inspection and maintenance of assigned trucks and equipment used daily to complete duties and assignments. Perform all work assignments and duties in compliance with established safe work practices. Follow safety and health regulations, policies and procedures. Identifies and resolves potential safety concerns or violations. Is Time Limited No If Yes, Appointment Length 24 months (potential to be extended) Wolfpack Perks and Benefits As a Pack member, you belong here, and can enjoy exclusive perks designed to enhance your personal and professional well-being. What we offer: Health Insurance for Temporary Employees Enhance your career with LEAD courses Attend non-revenue generating sporting events for free. Attain Work-life balance with our Childcare discounts , Wellness & Recreation Membership , and Wellness Programs that aim to build a thriving wolfpack community. Disclaimer: Perks and Benefit eligibility is based on Part-Time or Full-Time Employment status. Eligibility and Employer Sponsored Plans can be found within each of the links offered. Department Information Job City & State Raleigh, NC Department System Information Classification Title Temporary-Service Maintenance Working Title UTS - Temporary Recycling Collections Operator at NC State Position Information Requirements and Preferences Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 40 hours a week, 6:00 AM - 2:30 PM Other Work/Responsibilities Minimum Experience/Education High school or General Educational Development ( GED ) diploma Department Required Skills Assist the recycling collections team with Routes and Projects; Bulk Waste and Electronics Collections; Recycling and Reuse Collections Events and Projects – Support special waste/recycling/compost service for campus events and major activities on campus such as residence hall move in and move out. Customer service and communication – Share important information with a diverse work group. Communicate and implement operational procedures, standards or changes. Repair, Maintenance, Safety – maintenance of containers related to the collection of waste, recycling, and compost on campus. Must be able to move and lift up to 50 pounds with or without reasonable accommodation. Safe driving skills Preferred Years Experience, Skills, Training, Education Experience with collection of waste and recycling. Experience with cleaning, proper labeling, delivery, distribution, and maintenance inspection. Required License or Certification Valid driver’s license required. North Carolina driver’s license required within 60 days of hire and must be maintained. Valid NC Driver's License required? Yes Commercial Driver's License Required? No Recruitment Recruitment Details Anticipated Hiring Range $20.00 per hour Recruitment Dates Job Open Date 08/19/2026 Applicant Information Quick Link https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/233983 EEO NC State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal opportunities for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, and veteran status. The University encourages all qualified applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities, to apply. Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodations in the application and interview process are welcome to contact 919-513-0574 to speak with a representative of the Office of Equal Opportunity. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at (919) 515-2135 or workatncstate@ncsu.edu. Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. Degree(s) must be obtained prior to start date in order to meet qualifications and receive credit. NC State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about University Temporary Services? (Open Ended Question) * Are you able to move and lift up to 50 pounds with or without reasonable accommodation? Yes No * A valid driver's license (DL) is required for this position. Do you have a valid DL or the ability to obtain one if selected for hire? Yes, I have a valid DL and will maintain it as a condition of employment. No, I do not have a valid DL, but I will obtain a DL if selected for hire and maintain it as a condition of employment. No, I do not have a valid DL and cannot or will not obtain it. * Do you have any experience with collection of waste and recycling? Yes No * Please describe your customer service experience. (Open Ended Question) * Are you able to work from 6 am-2:30pm M-F? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Contact Information for References NC STATE UNIVERSITY RALEIGH, NC 27695 PHONE: (919) 515-2011 Privacy Accessibility Emergency Information Policies NC State Home © 2019 NC State University. All rights reserved To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
