    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/234409": {
      "title": "HR Project Manager",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | HR Project Manager Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) HR Project Manager Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please include a resume, cover letter and contact information for at least three professional references. This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Applicants must be authorized to work in the United States without the need for current or future sponsorship. Posting Details Posting Information Posting Number PG194838EP Internal Recruitment No Working Title HR Project Manager Anticipated Hiring Range $85,000 - $93,000 Work Schedule Core Business Hours: Monday - Friday, 8:00 am - 5:00 pm; flexible schedule and hybrid work environment are available. Job Location Raleigh, North Carolina Department UHR - Information Management & Analytics About the Department The Human Resources Information Management and Analytics ( HRIMA ) unit serves as the central information center for University HR, operating as a consultative, technology-adjacent partner to the campus community. The unit prioritizes process-first design, structured governance through a centralized Project Management Office ( PMO ), and collaborative data stewardship to ensure employee data is accurate, secure, and reliable throughout its lifecycle. Through active project facilitation and strategic alignment, HRIMA focuses on evaluating and optimizing business workflows, building campus data literacy, and providing practical, actionable insights. By turning complex operational processes into smart, dynamic business rules, the unit ensures that technology effectively serves our people, breaks down operational silos, and supports the broader talent strategies of the university. Wolfpack Perks and Benefits As a Pack member, you belong here, and can enjoy exclusive perks designed to enhance your personal and professional well-being. As you consider this opportunity, we encourage you to review our Employee Value Proposition and learn more about what makes NC State the best place to learn and work for everyone. What we offer: Medical , Dental , and Vision Flexible Spending Account Retirement Programs Disability Plans Life Insurance Accident Plan Paid Time Off and Other Leave Programs 12 Holidays Each Year Tuition and Academic Assistance And so much more! Attain Work-life balance with our Childcare benefits, Wellness & Recreation Membership , and Wellness Programs that aim to build a thriving wolfpack community. Disclaimer: Perks and Benefit eligibility is based on Part-Time or Full-Time Employment status. Eligibility and Employer Sponsored Plans can be found within each of the links offered. Essential Job Duties The HR Project Manager, housed within the HR Information Management & Analytics ( HRIMA ) unit, serves as a consultative advisor and facilitator for cross-functional HR projects, supporting the planning, scoping, and implementation of technical and non-technical initiatives. This role connects HR, campus partners, and the Office of Information Technology to clarify business needs, establish project goals and timelines, and advance projects from concept to completion. You will bring people, processes, and technology together to make HR operations more efficient and effective. By evaluating workflows, identifying opportunities for improvement, and translating policy and regulatory changes into clear business requirements, you will help teams navigate complexity and turn ideas into practical solutions. Your ability to build relationships, communicate clearly, and remove roadblocks will be key to delivering HR processes and technology that meet university needs and support compliance. Key responsibilities fall within the following functional areas. Project Facilitation & Consultative Advising Facilitate cross-functional process and project teams by providing consultative guidance that helps campus partners navigate process improvements, technical enhancements, and system configurations. Connect UHR , campus divisions, and Enterprise Application System/Office of Information Technology partners to identify systemic and technical barriers, coordinate resolution, and maintain momentum on shared priorities. Guide discovery and alignment sessions with campus partners to understand current-state workflows, assess institutional and localized business needs, and establish clear direction for cross-functional project delivery. Strategic Insight & Workflow Optimization Translate complex legislative changes, Federal and State requirements, and UNC System Office mandates into functional requirements and automated system logic that support accurate, sustainable technical solutions. Partner with university leadership and process teams to evaluate and improve business processes and technology, increasing efficiency, strengthening service delivery, and reducing unnecessary rework across the organization. Employee Data Governance & Quality Assurance Provide leadership and guidance for HR technology business rules, security parameters, and data definition standards to promote consistent, reliable, and well-governed employee data. Serve as a subject matter expert on the alignment of HR technology functionality with university policies, regulations, rules, and applicable regulatory requirements, helping ensure system behavior supports institutional standards. Operational Excellence & Support Oversee complex operational troubleshooting and system optimization for core HR processes. Act as the point of escalation for complex functional issues before they are moved to OIT . Partner with OIT / EAS throughout User Acceptance Testing ( UAT ) and post-implementation reviews to validate business requirements, assess system functionality, and ensure technology solutions deliver the intended operational outcomes. We are looking for someone who can build relationships, navigate complexity, and turn ideas into practical solutions that move HR initiatives forward. If you are a collaborative problem-solver who enjoys bringing people, processes, and technology together to make complex work more manageable, we invite you to apply. Other Responsibilities In addition to the core responsibilities of this role, there may be occasional opportunities to take on additional duties. This offers an opportunity to build on your skills, explore new areas, and gain a deeper understanding of the department’s operations. Qualifications Minimum Education and Experience This position requires a relevant post-Baccalaureate degree with a minimum of three (3) years of relevant Human Resource, Business Operations, or Information Technology experience , or a relevant undergraduate degree with a minimum of five (5) years of relevant experience as a substitute for the advanced degree (All degrees must be from appropriately accredited institutions) Other Required Qualifications Proven ability to navigate decentralized institutional structures, build consensus, and drive project accountability across diverse stakeholder groups. Demonstrated proficiency in business process mapping, requirements elicitation, and project lifecycle management frameworks. Exceptional ability to pivot standard “technical support” conversations toward high-level business logic and end-user experience discussions. Preferred Qualifications Experience working with ServiceNow HR Service Delivery ( HRSD ) or similar HR service management platforms. 4-5 years experience leading or coordinating projects using Agile, Scrum, or other structured project management methodologies. 2-3 yrs. experience in process improvement & change management Proven ability to manage competing priorities, coordinate multiple initiatives, and maintain attention to detail and quality in a fast-paced, dynamic environment. Demonstrated ability to provide clear guidance, facilitate collaboration, and communicate effectively with diverse stakeholders. Project Management, Process Improvement, Change Management, or related professional certifications. Required License(s) or Certification(s) N/A Valid NC Driver's License required No Commercial Driver's License required No Recruitment Dates and Special Instructions Job Open Date 08/31/2026 Anticipated Close Date 9/15/2026; if posting is still active we are accepting and reviewing applications. Special Instructions to Applicants Please include a resume, cover letter and contact information for at least three professional references. This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Applicants must be authorized to work in the United States without the need for current or future sponsorship. Position Details Position Number 00109647 Position Type EPS/SAAO Full Time Equivalent (FTE) (1.0 = 40 hours/week) 1.00 Appointment 12 Month Recurring Mandatory Designation - Adverse Weather Non Mandatory - Adverse Weather Mandatory Designation - Emergency Events Non Mandatory - Emergency Event Department ID 480201 - UHR - Information Management & Analytics EEO NC State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal opportunities for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, and veteran status. The University encourages all qualified applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities, to apply. Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodations in the application and interview process are welcome to contact 919-513-0574 to speak with a representative of the Office of Equal Opportunity. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at (919) 515-2135 or workatncstate@ncsu.edu . Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. Degree(s) must be obtained prior to start date in order to meet qualifications and receive credit. NC State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn of this opportunity? NCSU Website NCSU Executive Search Services Monster.com CareerBuilder.com InsideHigherEd.com Other Online Job Board Carolina Job Finder / Employment Guide Job / Career Fair The Chronicle of Higher Education HERC Professional Journal Print Advertisement (Newspaper / Periodical) Professional Organization Direct Contact from NCSU HR Representative / Recruiter NCSU Employee Referral Social Media (LinkedIn, Twitter, Facebook, Other) Other If you learned about this vacancy from \"other source\" or \"other website\", please provide the source. (Open Ended Question) * Please describe your experience with ServiceNow. Do you have experience with ServiceNow HRSD? Please describe your knowledge of any ServiceNow modules. (Open Ended Question) * Detail a project where a stakeholder, leadership, or the policy owners had directly conflicting priorities for a technical or process rollout. What specific facilitation approach did you take to build consensus, and what hard compromise did you convince both parties to accept? (Open Ended Question) * Tell us about a time a project was stalling due to systemic bottlenecks. What root cause did you identify, and what specific action did you take to clear the bottleneck without taking on clerical/administrative documentation tasks yourself? (Open Ended Question) * Describe a process you audited. Differentiate between how you improved its efficiency (removing waste/steps) and how you ensured its effectiveness (meeting core policy or organizational goals). How did you prevent yourself from simply automating an ineffective workflow? (Open Ended Question) Application Materials Required Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Contact Information for References Optional Documents NC STATE UNIVERSITY RALEIGH, NC 27695 PHONE: (919) 515-2011 Privacy Accessibility Emergency Information Policies NC State Home © 2019 NC State University. All rights reserved To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
