    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/233409": {
      "title": "Position Information",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | Postdoctoral Research Scholar Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) Postdoctoral Research Scholar Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please include a cover letter, resume/CV, and contact information for professional references. Posting Details Position Information Posting Number PG191746PD Position Number 00112237 Position Type Post Doc FLSA Exempt Departmental Information Department ID 111801 - Entomology and Plant Pathology Department 111801 - Entomology and Plant Pathology Job City & State Raleigh, NC Position Information Position Overview Essential Job Duties The Department of Entomology and Plant Pathology at NC State University is seeking a highly motivated Postdoctoral Research Scholar to conduct research focused on the isolation, characterization, genomics, and virulence of Orientia spp. bacteria associated with free-living chiggers. The successful candidate will work as part of a collaborative research team investigating Orientia spp. through a combination of bacterial culture, cell-based assays, next-generation sequencing, and genomic bioinformatics. The position will involve laboratory research conducted in a BSL -3 facility, as well as computational analysis of bacterial genomes. Collaborating researchers will collect wild-caught, free-living chiggers in the United States and provide specimens for laboratory analysis. The Postdoctoral Research Scholar will contribute to the culture and characterization of Orientia spp., genomic sequencing and analysis, assessment of bacterial virulence, and preparation of research findings for publication and presentation. Key Responsibilities: Culture Orientia spp. bacteria from specimens collected by collaborating researchers and establish and maintain pure bacterial cultures. Conduct laboratory studies to characterize Orientia spp. and assess bacterial virulence using appropriate human or animal cell lines. Perform bacterial culture and related laboratory research in a BSL -3 facility in accordance with established biosafety and laboratory protocols. Prepare purified bacterial DNA for next-generation sequencing and coordinate genomic sequencing with external sequencing service providers. Use probe-directed genome sequencing approaches, as appropriate, to obtain genomic data from Orientia spp. present in crude bacterial mixtures. Assemble, annotate, and analyze Orientia spp. genome sequences using bioinformatic approaches. Compare newly generated genome sequences with known Orientia spp. genomes to determine species identity and characterize genetic relationships. Conduct genomic analyses to investigate genetic factors associated with bacterial virulence and other relevant biological characteristics. Integrate laboratory and genomic findings to support research objectives. Prepare manuscripts, abstracts, presentations, and other scholarly products for dissemination of research findings. Present research findings at scientific meetings and conferences. Contribute to collaborative research activities, grant proposals, and other scholarly activities as appropriate. Maintain accurate records of laboratory experiments, genomic analyses, and research findings. Other Duties and Responsibilities: 1. Culture and characterize Orientia spp. bacteria – 50% Culture Orientia spp. bacteria from wild-caught, free-living chiggers collected in the United States by collaborating researchers. Establish and maintain pure cultures of Orientia spp. bacteria and conduct laboratory studies to characterize bacterial growth and virulence. Perform bacterial culture and related experimental work in a BSL -3 laboratory using established biosafety protocols. Culture Orientia spp. in appropriate animal cell lines and assess the virulence and biological characteristics of isolated bacterial cultures using human or other animal cell lines. Chiggers will be collected and provided by collaborating researchers in culture media and will not be provided as live specimens. 2. Obtain genomic sequence data for Orientia spp. – 10% Obtain genome sequence data from Orientia spp. bacteria using next-generation sequencing approaches. Prepare purified DNA obtained from bacterial cultures for submission to an external DNA sequencing service. As an alternative approach, collaborate with private sequencing service providers to use probe-directed genome sequencing to obtain genomic data from Orientia spp. present in crude bacterial mixtures derived from free-living chiggers. 3. Assemble and analyze Orientia spp. genomes – 30% Assemble and analyze genomic sequence data from Orientia spp. bacteria. Compare newly sequenced genomes with publicly available genomes from known Orientia spp. to determine species identity and characterize genetic relationships. Use genomic and bioinformatic analyses to identify genetic factors associated with bacterial virulence and other relevant biological characteristics. Interpret and integrate genomic findings with laboratory data to support research objectives and prepare results for publication in scientific journals. 4. Research communication and scholarly activities – 10% Analyze, interpret, and document research findings; prepare manuscripts, abstracts, presentations, and other scholarly materials; contribute to research proposals and grant applications as appropriate; and present research findings at scientific meetings and conferences. Maintain accurate records of experimental procedures, results, and genomic analyses and contribute to collaborative research activities with internal and external research partners. Other Work/Responsibilities Wolfpack Perks and Benefits As a Pack member, you belong here, and can enjoy exclusive perks designed to enhance your personal and professional well-being. As you consider this opportunity, we encourage you to review our Employee Value Proposition and learn more about what makes NC State the best place to learn and work for everyone. What we offer: Medical, Dental, Vision, Retirement and Leave Faculty and Staff Assistance Program Enhance your career with LEAD courses Attend non-revenue generating sporting events for free. Attain Work-life balance with our Childcare benefits, Wellness & Recreation Membership , and Wellness Programs that aim to build a thriving wolfpack community. Disclaimer: Perks and Benefit eligibility is based on Part-Time or Full-Time Employment status. Eligibility and Employer Sponsored Plans can be found within each of the links offered. Requirements and Preferences Work Schedule Monday-Friday, 8 am-5 pm Department Required Skills Ph.D. in Microbiology, Molecular Biology, Genomics, or a related field. Experience with mammalian and/or microbial cell culture and standard molecular biology techniques, including DNA extraction, PCR , and next-generation sequencing ( NGS ). Knowledge of microbial genomics, including genome assembly, annotation, and genomic data analysis using bioinformatics tools. Preferred Years Experience, Skills, Training, Education Ability to prepare manuscripts and work effectively in a collaborative research environment Required License or Certification Valid NC Driver’s License required Valid NC Driver's License required? Yes Commercial Driver's License Required? No Recruitment Recruitment Details Anticipated Hiring Range $58,656 If you anticipate multiple hires from this search, please indicate how many Recruitment Dates Job Open Date 07/31/2026 Applicant Information Quick Link https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/233408 EEO NC State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal opportunities for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, and veteran status. The University encourages all qualified applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities, to apply. Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodations in the application and interview process are welcome to contact 919-513-0574 to speak with a representative of the Office of Equal Opportunity. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at (919) 515-2135 or workatncstate@ncsu.edu . Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. Degree(s) must be obtained prior to start date in order to meet qualifications and receive credit. NC State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn of this opportunity? NCSU Website NCSU Executive Search Services Monster.com CareerBuilder.com InsideHigherEd.com Other Online Job Board Carolina Job Finder / Employment Guide Job / Career Fair The Chronicle of Higher Education HERC Professional Journal Print Advertisement (Newspaper / Periodical) Professional Organization Direct Contact from NCSU HR Representative / Recruiter NCSU Employee Referral Social Media (LinkedIn, Twitter, Facebook, Other) Other If you learned about this vacancy from \"other source\" or \"other website\", please provide the source. (Open Ended Question) * According to our university's regulations, a postdoctoral scholar needs to have successfully completed their terminal degree no more than 5 years from the start date of their appointment. Given this, please provide the date (MM/DD/YYYY) your terminal degree has been or will be confirmed. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Contact Information for References Optional Documents NC STATE UNIVERSITY RALEIGH, NC 27695 PHONE: (919) 515-2011 Privacy Accessibility Emergency Information Policies NC State Home © 2019 NC State University. All rights reserved To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/223258": {
      "title": "Position Information",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | Postdoctoral Research Scholar Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) Postdoctoral Research Scholar Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number PG191104PD Position Number 00110484 Position Type Post Doc FLSA Exempt Departmental Information Department ID 140301 - Civil Construction & Environmental Engineering Department 140301 - Civil Const & Environ Engineer Job City & State Raleigh, NC Position Information Position Overview Essential Job Duties NC State Department of Civil, Construction, and Environmental Engineering ( CCEE ), seeks a postdoctoral researcher in the transportation area related to human-Autonomous Vehicle (AV) interactions. For questions regarding the position please contact Professor Danjue Chen (dchen33@ncsu.edu). The postdoc training and mentoring will be in: 1. Helping to advance research in human-automation interaction. 2. Helping to establish in the professional community. 3. Helping to get familiar with writing proposals. 4. Helping & supervising in graduate & undergraduate students advising. The research project will study how human users (as a driver or AV user) interact with AVs on the road to investigate a set of problems like (1) how human drivers decide whether to cooperate with AVs (e.g., to yield or not) and (2) how AV users decide whether to accept the cooperation from the algorithmic design? We are interested in learning the influential factors in such human-AV interactions, the decision-making process from the cognitive and/or behavioral economics perspective, and how to develop strategies to promote human-AV cooperation (e.g., via improved communication design, or nudging). We expect to utilize a simulator network consisting of multiple connected driving simulators (i.e., with embedded connectivity). Responsibilities include (1) designing and implementing research experiments, (2) conducting data analysis, and (3) paper writing. Other Work/Responsibilities Other responsibilities include (1) supervising graduate students in research, and (2) developing research proposals. Wolfpack Perks and Benefits As a Pack member, you belong here, and can enjoy exclusive perks designed to enhance your personal and professional well-being. What we offer: Medical, Dental, Vision, Retirement and Leave Faculty and Staff Assistance Program Enhance your career with LEAD courses Attend non-revenue generating sporting events for free. Attain Work-life balance with our Childcare benefits, Wellness & Recreation Membership , and Wellness Programs that aim to build a thriving wolfpack community. Disclaimer: Perks and Benefit eligibility is based on Part-Time or Full-Time Employment status. Eligibility and Employer Sponsored Plans can be found within each of the links offered. Requirements and Preferences Work Schedule M-F, 8 AM-5PM unless noted otherwise Department Required Skills PhD degree in transportation, economics, industrial engineering, psychology, or a related field. Excellent communication skills. Self-motivated with professional work ethics. Highly desired experience in one or more of these areas: behavioral economics, human factors, statistics, and experimental design. Preferred Years Experience, Skills, Training, Education Experience in one or more of these areas: multi-agent interaction, driving simulators, game theory, and human-computer interaction Required License or Certification N/A Valid NC Driver's License required? No Commercial Driver's License Required? No Recruitment Recruitment Details Anticipated Hiring Range $58,656-$60,000 If you anticipate multiple hires from this search, please indicate how many Recruitment Dates Job Open Date 11/13/2023 Applicant Information Quick Link https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/193023 EEO NC State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal opportunities for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, and veteran status. The University encourages all qualified applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities, to apply. Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodations in the application and interview process are welcome to contact 919-513-0574 to speak with a representative of the Office of Equal Opportunity. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at (919) 515-2135 or workatncstate@ncsu.edu . Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. Degree(s) must be obtained prior to start date in order to meet qualifications and receive credit. NC State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn of this opportunity? NCSU Website NCSU Executive Search Services Monster.com CareerBuilder.com InsideHigherEd.com Other Online Job Board Carolina Job Finder / Employment Guide Job / Career Fair The Chronicle of Higher Education HERC Professional Journal Print Advertisement (Newspaper / Periodical) Professional Organization Direct Contact from NCSU HR Representative / Recruiter NCSU Employee Referral Social Media (LinkedIn, Twitter, Facebook, Other) Other If you learned about this vacancy from \"other source\" or \"other website\", please provide the source. (Open Ended Question) * Do you have, or will you have by the start date, a relevant PhD awarded no more than five (5) years from initial date of postdoctoral appointment? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Contact Information for References Optional Documents NC STATE UNIVERSITY RALEIGH, NC 27695 PHONE: (919) 515-2011 Privacy Accessibility Emergency Information Policies NC State Home © 2019 NC State University. All rights reserved To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/234635": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | Assistant Professor Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) Assistant Professor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Any questions can be addressed to the search committee chair, Vanessa V. Volpe atvvvolpe@ncsu.edu. Review of applications will begin on October 15th and will continue until a suitable candidate is identified. Please include the following documents as part of your online application: 1. Cover Letter 2.CV 2. Research statement 4. Teaching statement 5. Contact information for references. *Additional information or application materials may be requested.* Posting Details Posting Information Posting Number PG194842EP Internal Recruitment No Working Title Assistant Professor Anticipated Hiring Range Commensurate with education and credentials ($85,000 - $95,000) Work Schedule Core Business Hours: Monday - Friday; 8:00 am - 5:00 pm; schedule will vary based on research and teaching needs. Job Location Raleigh, NC Department Psychology About the Department NC State is a research extensive land grant institution serving more than 34,000 students and is located in Raleigh, NC, the state capital (http://www.ncsu.edu/about-nc-state/). This geographical location offers access to major intellectual and cultural resources, including the Research Triangle Park, Duke University, University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill, and the National Humanities Center. The School Psychology is an AP A-accredited and NASP -approved Ph.D. program. Additional information about the university (http://www.ncsu.edu/) or the department (https://psychology.chass.ncsu.edu/) may be accessed on the web. The Department of Psychology consists of 31 faculty members, the staff of the advising center, the staff of the Psychoeducational Clinic, and the four members of our office staff, as well as over 750 undergraduate majors and 120 graduate students pursuing their doctoral degrees. The faculty are outstanding scholars, many of whom have won awards for teaching and research and/or are fellows in the major professional societies in Psychology. Faculty have received research grants and training grants from the National Science Foundation, the National Institutes for Health, the National Institute on Aging, the Army Research Laboratory, the Army Research Institute, the Department of Education, and numerous companies. Wolfpack Perks and Benefits As a Pack member, you belong here, and can enjoy exclusive perks designed to enhance your personal and professional well-being. As you consider this opportunity, we encourage you to review our Employee Value Proposition and learn more about what makes NC State the best place to learn and work for everyone. What we offer: Medical , Dental , and Vision Flexible Spending Account Retirement Programs Disability Plans Life Insurance Accident Plan Paid Time Off and Other Leave Programs 12 Holidays Each Year Tuition and Academic Assistance And so much more! Attain Work-life balance with our Childcare benefits, Wellness & Recreation Membership , and Wellness Programs that aim to build a thriving wolfpack community. Disclaimer: Perks and Benefit eligibility is based on Part-Time or Full-Time Employment status. Eligibility and Employer Sponsored Plans can be found within each of the links offered. Essential Job Duties The Department of Psychology is seeking an Assistant Professor to advance research, teaching, and service in applied social psychology. This position requires the establishment of an independent research program with demonstrated or potential for external funding, dissemination of scholarship through scholarly outlets, teaching and mentorship of undergraduate and graduate students, and service to the Applied Social Psychology program area, department, college, university, and broader field. As an Assistant Professor, you will conduct a productive program of research that contributes meaningful scholarship to the discipline and strengthens the department’s research profile. You will teach and mentor undergraduate and graduate students, helping them develop as scholars and professionals, while contributing your expertise to the continued growth of the program and the broader discipline. Key Responsibilities: Develop and sustain an independent, externally funded research program. Disseminate research through scholarly publications, presentations, and other professional outlets. Teach courses that support undergraduate and graduate education in psychology. Mentor undergraduate and graduate students in their academics, research, and professional development. Contribute service and professional leadership within the Applied Social Psychology program area, department, college, university, and broader field. If you are an emerging scholar in applied social psychology who is excited to build a meaningful research program, engage students through teaching and mentorship, and contribute to a collaborative academic community, we encourage you to apply. Other Responsibilities In addition to the core responsibilities of this role, there will be occasional opportunities to take on additional duties. This offers an opportunity to build on your skills, explore new areas, and gain a deeper understanding of the department’s operations. Qualifications Minimum Education and Experience PhD in psychology or relevant discipline by August 16, 2027. Other Required Qualifications Collaborative approach to interdisciplinary research or scholarly projects with colleagues within and beyond the university. Record of scholarly productivity, including peer-reviewed research and other scholarly publications. Commitment to meaningful service that contributes to an academic program, department, university, or professional field. Teaching proficiency at both the undergraduate and graduate levels, with a focus on supporting students with varied academic and professional goals. Demonstrated mentorship of doctoral students, postdoctoral fellows, or other emerging scholars. Preferred Qualifications Success or promise in securing external research funding, including competitive federal, foundation, or other sponsored funding. Alignment with the core values of our applied social psychology program: conducting high-quality research, considering the multilevel social and cultural contexts in which individuals are embedded, practical application of psychological theory to real-world challenges, and leveraging the value of interdisciplinary collaboration. Success or promise in research that emphasizes applied and basic research approaches to inform social change from multiple disciplinary perspectives. Required License(s) or Certification(s) N/A Valid NC Driver's License required No Commercial Driver's License required No Recruitment Dates and Special Instructions Job Open Date 09/01/2026 Anticipated Close Date 10/15/2026; if posting is still active, we are accepting and reviewing applications Special Instructions to Applicants Any questions can be addressed to the search committee chair, Vanessa V. Volpe atvvvolpe@ncsu.edu. Review of applications will begin on October 15th and will continue until a suitable candidate is identified. Please include the following documents as part of your online application: 1. Cover Letter 2.CV 2. Research statement 4. Teaching statement 5. Contact information for references. Additional information or application materials may be requested. Position Details Position Number 00112290 Position Type Tenured/Tenure-Track Faculty Full Time Equivalent (FTE) (1.0 = 40 hours/week) 1.0 Appointment 9 Month Recurring Mandatory Designation - Adverse Weather Non Mandatory - Adverse Weather Mandatory Designation - Emergency Events Non Mandatory - Emergency Event Department ID 164501 - Psychology EEO NC State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal opportunities for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, and veteran status. The University encourages all qualified applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities, to apply. Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodations in the application and interview process are welcome to contact 919-513-0574 to speak with a representative of the Office of Equal Opportunity. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at (919) 515-2135 or workatncstate@ncsu.edu . Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. Degree(s) must be obtained prior to start date in order to meet qualifications and receive credit. NC State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn of this opportunity? NCSU Website Job Alert (automated email from our system) NCSU Executive Search Services Monster.com CareerBuilder.com InsideHigherEd.com Other Online Job Board Carolina Job Finder / Employment Guide Job / Career Fair The Chronicle of Higher Education Professional Journal Print Advertisement (Newspaper / Periodical) Professional Organization Direct Contact from NCSU HR Representative / Recruiter NCSU Employee Referral Social Media (LinkedIn, Twitter, Facebook, Other) Other If you learned about this vacancy from \"other source\" or \"other website\", please provide the source. (Open Ended Question) Application Materials Required Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Contact Information for References Research Statement Teaching Statement Optional Documents NC STATE UNIVERSITY RALEIGH, NC 27695 PHONE: (919) 515-2011 Privacy Accessibility Emergency Information Policies NC State Home © 2019 NC State University. All rights reserved To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/234124": {
      "title": "IT Technical Support Analyst",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | IT Technical Support Analyst Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) IT Technical Support Analyst Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please include as attachments a resume, cover letter, and contact information for at least 3 professional references. This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Applicants must be authorized to work in the United States without the need for current or future sponsorship. Posting Details Posting Information Posting Number PG194831EP Internal Recruitment No Working Title IT Technical Support Analyst Anticipated Hiring Range $60,000 - $65,000 Work Schedule 8:00am - 5:00pm, Monday - Friday Job Location Raleigh, NC Department CVM - Dean's Office About the Department CVM IT is dedicated to meeting the evolving and varied information technology needs of the College of Veterinary Medicine. We provide comprehensive support to faculty, staff, students, researchers, administrators, and Veterinary Hospital clinicians. Our team is committed to integrating innovative computing technologies, maintaining and enhancing existing systems, and ensuring the confidentiality, integrity, and availability of CVM IT assets and data. Wolfpack Perks and Benefits As a Pack member, you belong here, and can enjoy exclusive perks designed to enhance your personal and professional well-being. As you consider this opportunity, we encourage you to review our Employee Value Proposition and learn more about what makes NC State the best place to learn and work for everyone. What we offer: Medical , Dental , and Vision Flexible Spending Account Retirement Programs Disability Plans Life Insurance Accident Plan Paid Time Off and Other Leave Programs 12 Holidays Each Year Tuition and Academic Assistance And so much more! Attain Work-life balance with our Childcare benefits, Wellness & Recreation Membership , and Wellness Programs that aim to build a thriving wolfpack community. Disclaimer: Perks and Benefit eligibility is based on Part-Time or Full-Time Employment status. Eligibility and Employer Sponsored Plans can be found within each of the links offered. Essential Job Duties The IT Technical Support Analyst plays a critical role in delivering advanced IT desktop support and technology solutions to the College of Veterinary Medicine’s faculty, staff, and students. This position requires strong technical expertise, excellent problem-solving abilities, and a high level of customer service in a fast-paced academic and clinical environment. As a Tier 2 support position within CVM IT, this role is responsible for resolving complex technical issues, supporting enterprise endpoint management, assisting with infrastructure and technology projects, and serving as an escalation point for Tier 1 staff and student workers. In addition to desktop support responsibilities, the IT Technical Support Analyst assists with Audio/Visual (A/V) support, classroom technologies, and other specialized technology initiatives across the college and veterinary hospital. Key Responsibilities : Advanced IT Desktop Support: Provide advanced hands-on and remote technical support for faculty, staff, and students, troubleshooting complex hardware, software, operating system, and network-related issues. Serve as an escalation point for Tier 1 support staff and student IT workers, assisting with advanced troubleshooting and issue resolution. Deploy, configure, maintain, and troubleshoot Windows and Mac OS devices, printers, mobile devices, and specialized peripherals. Utilize enterprise management tools such as SCCM , Jamf, Active Directory, and Group Policy to manage endpoint configurations, software deployments, updates, and security compliance. Diagnose and resolve complex endpoint management, authentication, profile, software, and connectivity issues. Support and maintain university-supported software, departmental applications, and specialized veterinary and research technologies. Document technical issues, resolutions, procedures, and knowledge base articles within the IT ticketing system (ServiceNow). Participate in endpoint lifecycle management processes, including imaging, deployments, refresh programs, surplus processing, and asset tracking. Collaborate with Systems Administration, Clinical Informatics Support ( CIS ), Application Development, OIT , vendors, and other stakeholders to resolve technical issues and implement solutions. Assist with technology planning, testing, standardization, and implementation of new hardware and software solutions. Provide mentorship, guidance, and technical training to Tier 1 staff and student workers. Serve as a technical lead for desktop-related networking and telephony support, including troubleshooting endpoint connectivity issues, coordinating network jack activations and moves, supporting VoIP phone deployments and relocations, assisting with switch and wireless troubleshooting, and working closely with NC State OIT /ComTech and vendors to resolve infrastructure-related issues affecting CVM users. Audio/Visual (A/V) and Technology Project Support: Assist with the setup, maintenance, troubleshooting, and support of A/V systems in classrooms, conference rooms, teaching spaces, and event areas. Support the A/V Coordinator in implementing classroom technology upgrades, conference room enhancements, and other A/V projects. Provide technical assistance for meetings, presentations, live events, and video conferencing systems as needed. Assist with diagnosing and resolving classroom and conference room technology issues to minimize disruption to teaching and meetings. Participate in technology deployment projects, office moves, Windows upgrades, hardware refresh initiatives, and other departmental IT projects. Other Responsibilities Other tasks and responsibilities may be assigned based on the needs of the organization and evolving priorities. Qualifications Minimum Education and Experience Minimum Education/Experience Bachelor’s degree with 1-2 years of relevant IT experience or an equivalent combination of education, training, and experience. Other Required Qualifications Strong troubleshooting skills for Windows and Mac OS environments. Experience with IT system management tools such as SCCM and Jamf. Excellent verbal and written communication skills. Ability to work collaboratively with various stakeholders, including faculty, staff, and IT partners. Experience w/ A/V classroom support is desirable. Preferred Qualifications Advanced knowledge of Windows and macOS operating systems in an enterprise environment. Experience supporting Linux operating systems and Linux-based applications in research, academic, or enterprise environments. Experience with endpoint management platforms such as SCCM , Jamf, Intune, or similar tools; Familiarity with Active Directory, Group Policy, enterprise networking concepts, and endpoint security practices. Ability to manage multiple priorities and work independently in a fast-paced support environment. Experience with ServiceNow or similar enterprise ticketing systems. Experience supporting classroom technology, video conferencing platforms, and A/V systems. Required License(s) or Certification(s) N/A Valid NC Driver's License required No Commercial Driver's License required No Recruitment Dates and Special Instructions Job Open Date 08/25/2026 Anticipated Close Date Open Until Filled Special Instructions to Applicants Please include as attachments a resume, cover letter, and contact information for at least 3 professional references. This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Applicants must be authorized to work in the United States without the need for current or future sponsorship. Position Details Position Number 00112252 Position Type EPS/SAAO Full Time Equivalent (FTE) (1.0 = 40 hours/week) 1.0 Appointment 12 Month Recurring Mandatory Designation - Adverse Weather Non Mandatory - Adverse Weather Mandatory Designation - Emergency Events Non Mandatory - Emergency Event Department ID 190104 - CVM - Dean's Office EEO NC State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal opportunities for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, and veteran status. The University encourages all qualified applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities, to apply. Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodations in the application and interview process are welcome to contact 919-513-0574 to speak with a representative of the Office of Equal Opportunity. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at (919) 515-2135 or workatncstate@ncsu.edu . Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. Degree(s) must be obtained prior to start date in order to meet qualifications and receive credit. NC State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn of this opportunity? NCSU Website NCSU Executive Search Services Monster.com CareerBuilder.com InsideHigherEd.com Other Online Job Board Carolina Job Finder / Employment Guide Job / Career Fair The Chronicle of Higher Education HERC Professional Journal Print Advertisement (Newspaper / Periodical) Professional Organization Direct Contact from NCSU HR Representative / Recruiter NCSU Employee Referral Social Media (LinkedIn, Twitter, Facebook, Other) Other If you learned about this vacancy from \"other source\" or \"other website\", please provide the source. (Open Ended Question) * Do you have professional IT experience in an institute of higher education? Yes No Application Materials Required Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Contact Information for References Optional Documents NC STATE UNIVERSITY RALEIGH, NC 27695 PHONE: (919) 515-2011 Privacy Accessibility Emergency Information Policies NC State Home © 2019 NC State University. All rights reserved To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/227960": {
      "title": "Position Information",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | Temporary Camp Cook - Ellerbe, NC Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) Temporary Camp Cook - Ellerbe, NC Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Attach: Contact information for three references Posting Details Position Information Posting Number PG195736TM Position Number 11ASO3643 Position Type Temporary Essential Job Duties Assist in the preparation of meals for summer camp. Interact with camp leadership in providing a positive experience for participants. Work Schedule: Spring March 27. 2026 – May 25, 2026 as needed. During summer camp Sunday – Friday. Approximately, May 31 – August 7. Hours may vary from week to week. Is Time Limited No If Yes, Appointment Length Wolfpack Perks and Benefits As a Pack member, you belong here, and can enjoy exclusive perks designed to enhance your personal and professional well-being. What we offer: Health Insurance for Temporary Employees Enhance your career with LEAD courses Attend non-revenue generating sporting events for free. Attain Work-life balance with our Childcare discounts , Wellness & Recreation Membership , and Wellness Programs that aim to build a thriving wolfpack community. Disclaimer: Perks and Benefit eligibility is based on Part-Time or Full-Time Employment status. Eligibility and Employer Sponsored Plans can be found within each of the links offered. Department Information Job City & State Ellerbe, NC Department Millstone 4H Center - Ellerbe, NC System Information Classification Title Temporary-Service Maintenance Working Title Temporary Camp Cook - Ellerbe, NC Position Information Requirements and Preferences Work Schedule 40+ hours a week Other Work/Responsibilities n/a Minimum Experience/Educat