    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/234536": {
      "title": "Senior AI and Applications Developer",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | Senior AI and Applications Developer Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) Senior AI and Applications Developer Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please include a resume, cover letter and contact information for at least three professional references. This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Applicants must be authorized to work in the United States without the need for current or future sponsorship. Posting Details Posting Information Posting Number PG194843EP Internal Recruitment No Working Title Senior AI and Applications Developer Anticipated Hiring Range commensurate with education/experience Work Schedule Monday- Friday, 8am-5pm Some weekend and evening work required. Job Location Raleigh, NC Department Enterprise Application Services About the Department Enterprise Application Services ( EAS ) is in the Office of Information Technology ( OIT ) division at North Carolina State University. EAS is responsible for the design, implementation, operation, enhancement & maintenance of the University’s enterprise business applications. This includes: development, operation & maintenance of all enterprise administrative systems (Enterprise Document Mgmt, Financials, HR, Guest & Affiliate, MyPack Portal, Student Information, REPORTER , Enterprise Research Administration systems, etc.), configuration management, database administration and the maintenance, enhancement, and integration of these systems. Wolfpack Perks and Benefits As a Pack member, you belong here, and can enjoy exclusive perks designed to enhance your personal and professional well-being. As you consider this opportunity, we encourage you to review our Employee Value Proposition and learn more about what makes NC State the best place to learn and work for everyone. What we offer: Medical , Dental , and Vision Flexible Spending Account Retirement Programs Disability Plans Life Insurance Accident Plan Paid Time Off and Other Leave Programs 12 Holidays Each Year Tuition and Academic Assistance And so much more! Attain Work-life balance with our Childcare benefits, Wellness & Recreation Membership , and Wellness Programs that aim to build a thriving wolfpack community. Disclaimer: Perks and Benefit eligibility is based on Part-Time or Full-Time Employment status. Eligibility and Employer Sponsored Plans can be found within each of the links offered. Essential Job Duties As a member of the EAS Development team, this position will serve as a Mendix Sr. Enterprise Developer, as well as leading AI development and deployment initiatives within EAS . Mendix Development: Lead the design, build and/or implementation of practical, cost effective business solutions. Complete detailed analysis and solutions development, regression testing, performance testing and quality assurance testing of Mendix applications. Develop and maintain technical documentation. Assist customers with defining requirements, implementing solutions and testing. AI Development and Deployment: Evaluate emerging AI technologies and platforms to identify viable solutions for EAS and the broader NC State community; author and formalize a comprehensive strategic plan for embedding AI across software development, deployment, and support life cycles. Represent EAS / OIT on collaborative campus IT committees and working groups, aligning AI initiatives and practices across university departments. Provide guidance to other team members, across all EAS teams on the proper implementation of AI tools, workflow and security guidelines. Technical Solutions Development Interpret complex business processes and technological functions and provide input to management and customers on the appropriate resource and technology for automated solutions. Ensure that application development efforts align closely with business requirements, from design to delivery, and that applications are user friendly, scalable, secure, and can be efficiently maintained once deployed. Planning and Organizing Maintain a strong knowledge of the SDLC at NC State University combined with outstanding organization and communication skills. Maintain an understanding of software development project management methodologies and tools (Microsoft Project, QuickBase, SmartSheet, etc) and a thorough understanding of project expectations and procedures. Technical Support Act as a subject matter expert and direct advisor to senior OIT management regarding AI capabilities, risk management, and resource allocation. Apply knowledge and skills to troubleshoot complex problems and provide timely resolution. Customer Service Promote positive customer relationships to ensure customer satisfaction. Establish a positive and proactive relationship by demonstrating ownership and knowledge of customer business processes and issues. Technical Solutions Development Interpret complex business processes and technological functions and provide input to management and customers on the appropriate resource and technology for automated solutions. Ensure that application development efforts align closely with business requirements, from design to delivery, and that applications are user friendly, scalable, secure, and can be efficiently maintained once deployed. Planning and Organizing Maintain a strong knowledge of the SDLC at NC State University combined with outstanding organization and communication skills. Maintain an understanding of software development project management methodologies and tools (Microsoft Project, QuickBase, SmartSheet, etc) and a thorough understanding of project expectations and procedures. Technical Support Act as a subject matter expert and direct advisor to senior OIT management regarding AI capabilities, risk management, and resource allocation. Apply knowledge and skills to troubleshoot complex problems and provide timely resolution. Customer Service Promote positive customer relationships to ensure customer satisfaction. Establish a positive and proactive relationship by demonstrating ownership and knowledge of customer business processes and issues. Other Responsibilities Qualifications Minimum Education and Experience Master’s degree and at least one year of relevant experience; or Bachelor’s degree with at least two years’ of relevant experience; or an equivalent combination of education, training and relevant experience. Other Required Qualifications There or more years of developing applications using Mendix technologies. Understanding of Artificial Intelligence (AI) Agentic tool development within the SDLC process. Experience using AI tools such as Gemini or Claude in software development environments. Excellent verbal and written communication skills in both technical and non-technical subjects including the ability to communicate effectively at all levels of the organization. Strong project management, organizational and time management skills with the ability to manage project work and support tasks concurrently. Excellent problem-solving, analytical and evaluative skills with an ability to resolve complex, difficult technical issues at the macro level. Strong organizational and communication skills. Understanding of the project development life cycle, including but not limited to application analysis, development, testing, documentation, approval and post migration validation. Attention to detail and ability to form strong relationships between team members, customers, and management is essential. Preferred Qualifications Functional knowledge of, or experience using NC State’s Mendix applications. Experience developing deploying applications using PHP . Experience developing applications using shopping cart and catalog functions. Experience developing applications for billing, equipment scheduling and CRM functions. Knowledge of relevant technical standards such as OIT change management/source control, Section 508 (accessibility), NC Records Retention and Disposition Standards, NC IT audit standards and any applicable federal data protection standards ( FERPA , HIPAA , ISO 27002, NIST 800-53, etc.) . Required License(s) or Certification(s) N/A Valid NC Driver's License required No Commercial Driver's License required No Recruitment Dates and Special Instructions Job Open Date 09/01/2026 Anticipated Close Date 9/16/2026; if posting is still active we are accepting and reviewing applications. Special Instructions to Applicants Please include a resume, cover letter and contact information for at least three professional references. This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Applicants must be authorized to work in the United States without the need for current or future sponsorship. Position Details Position Number 00105636 Position Type EPS/SAAO Full Time Equivalent (FTE) (1.0 = 40 hours/week) 1.0 Appointment 12 Month Recurring Mandatory Designation - Adverse Weather Mandatory - Adverse Weather Mandatory Designation - Emergency Events Mandatory - Fire/Explosions, Mandatory - Medical Emergencies, Mandatory - Hazardous Material Incidents, Mandatory - Transportation Accidents, Mandatory - Evacuations/Natural Hazards, Mandatory - Utilities/Infrastructure Failure, Mandatory - Threats of Violence/Terrorism/Interpersonal Emergencies Department ID 515001 - Enterprise Application Services EEO NC State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal opportunities for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, and veteran status. The University encourages all qualified applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities, to apply. Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodations in the application and interview process are welcome to contact 919-513-0574 to speak with a representative of the Office of Equal Opportunity. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at (919) 515-2135 or workatncstate@ncsu.edu . Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. Degree(s) must be obtained prior to start date in order to meet qualifications and receive credit. NC State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn of this opportunity? NCSU Website NCSU Executive Search Services Monster.com CareerBuilder.com InsideHigherEd.com Other Online Job Board Carolina Job Finder / Employment Guide Job / Career Fair The Chronicle of Higher Education HERC Professional Journal Print Advertisement (Newspaper / Periodical) Professional Organization Direct Contact from NCSU HR Representative / Recruiter NCSU Employee Referral Social Media (LinkedIn, Twitter, Facebook, Other) Other If you learned about this vacancy from \"other source\" or \"other website\", please provide the source. (Open Ended Question) * Please describe any experience you may have with the development of artificial intelligence systems. (Open Ended Question) * Please describe your experiences with Java and/or Mendix application development. (Open Ended Question) Application Materials Required Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Contact Information for References Optional Documents NC STATE UNIVERSITY RALEIGH, NC 27695 PHONE: (919) 515-2011 Privacy Accessibility Emergency Information Policies NC State Home © 2019 NC State University. All rights reserved To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/234037": {
      "title": "Position Information",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | Postdoctoral Research Scholar Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) Postdoctoral Research Scholar Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Candidates should attach cover letter, CV/resume, contact information for three references to their application. Posting Details Position Information Posting Number PG191756PD Position Number 00111489 Position Type Post Doc FLSA Exempt Departmental Information Department ID 140301 - Civil Construction & Environmental Engineering Department 140301 - Civil Construction & Environmental Engineering Job City & State Raleigh, NC Position Information Position Overview Essential Job Duties This position will support an ongoing project with the NCDOT to evaluate road ripples and the position may generally involve supporting other short duration experimental mechanical evaluations of asphalt concrete mixtures. The position will also provide some laboratory and project management support. The main duties and responsibilities include: Conduct and synthesize literature and agency-practice reviews related to road ripples, including potential formation mechanisms, diagnostic methods, contributing factors, and pavement-performance implications. Coordinate and participate in field and forensic evaluations of North Carolina pavements exhibiting road ripples, including site selection, records and data compilation, field testing, sample collection, laboratory evaluation, and comparative analysis. Plan, conduct, and analyze laboratory and modeling studies to evaluate residual moisture in asphalt mixtures and the potential short- and long-term effects of road ripples on pavement performance. Draft quarterly reports and monthly reports to support the aforementioned research project and/or similar project. May be asked to participate in other research projects related to aforementioned topic as projects are awarded. Coordinate laboratory management activities in support of the asphalt mixture analysis group tasks. This may include coordinating graduate students for cleaning, ensuring PPE is appropriately worn, ensuring supplies are ordered, and coordinating on calibrations. Other Work/Responsibilities Wolfpack Perks and Benefits As a Pack member, you belong here, and can enjoy exclusive perks designed to enhance your personal and professional well-being. As you consider this opportunity, we encourage you to review our Employee Value Proposition and learn more about what makes NC State the best place to learn and work for everyone. What we offer: Medical, Dental, Vision, Retirement and Leave Faculty and Staff Assistance Program Enhance your career with LEAD courses Attend non-revenue generating sporting events for free. Attain Work-life balance with our Childcare benefits, Wellness & Recreation Membership , and Wellness Programs that aim to build a thriving wolfpack community. Disclaimer: Perks and Benefit eligibility is based on Part-Time or Full-Time Employment status. Eligibility and Employer Sponsored Plans can be found within each of the links offered. Requirements and Preferences Work Schedule Flexibility can be provided given the nature of research Department Required Skills Ability to work in a dynamic environment with people of varying backgrounds and good communication skills. Strong written and oral communication skills, be self-motivated, and possess leadership skills Preferred Years Experience, Skills, Training, Education Ph.D. in Civil or Environmental Engineering is preferred or closely related field (at the time of appointment). Knowledge of asphalt materials, pavement construction, and performance, particularly moisture-related distress, layer bonding, and pavement forensic evaluation. Experience conducting or supporting field and laboratory investigations of asphalt pavements, including pavement condition assessment, sample collection and handling, nondestructive testing, asphalt mixture testing, or pavement-performance analysis. Familiarity with statistical modeling approaches. Familiarity with state highway agency and/or federal agency research reporting requirements. Required License or Certification N/A Valid NC Driver's License required? Yes Commercial Driver's License Required? No Recruitment Recruitment Details Anticipated Hiring Range $60,000-$65,000 If you anticipate multiple hires from this search, please indicate how many Recruitment Dates Job Open Date 08/20/2026 Applicant Information Quick Link https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/234035 EEO NC State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal opportunities for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, and veteran status. The University encourages all qualified applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities, to apply. Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodations in the application and interview process are welcome to contact 919-513-0574 to speak with a representative of the Office of Equal Opportunity. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at (919) 515-2135 or workatncstate@ncsu.edu . Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. Degree(s) must be obtained prior to start date in order to meet qualifications and receive credit. NC State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn of this opportunity? NCSU Website NCSU Executive Search Services Monster.com CareerBuilder.com InsideHigherEd.com Other Online Job Board Carolina Job Finder / Employment Guide Job / Career Fair The Chronicle of Higher Education HERC Professional Journal Print Advertisement (Newspaper / Periodical) Professional Organization Direct Contact from NCSU HR Representative / Recruiter NCSU Employee Referral Social Media (LinkedIn, Twitter, Facebook, Other) Other If you learned about this vacancy from \"other source\" or \"other website\", please provide the source. (Open Ended Question) * According to our university's regulations, a postdoctoral scholar needs to have successfully completed their terminal degree no more than 5 years from the start date of their appointment. Given this, please provide the date (MM/DD/YYYY) your terminal degree has been or will be confirmed. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Contact Information for References Optional Documents NC STATE UNIVERSITY RALEIGH, NC 27695 PHONE: (919) 515-2011 Privacy Accessibility Emergency Information Policies NC State Home © 2019 NC State University. All rights reserved To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/227250": {
      "title": "Lecturer, Economics",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | Lecturer, Economics Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) Lecturer, Economics Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please note, you will be required to attach a letter of application, CV/resume, and contact information for three professional references to apply. Finalists may be required to submit three letters of recommendation. Posting Details Posting Information Posting Number PG194460EP Internal Recruitment No Working Title Lecturer, Economics Anticipated Hiring Range Dependent upon course load Work Schedule Varies based on course schedule Job Location Raleigh, NC Department Economics - Poole College of Management About the Department The Poole College of Management actively engages with industry and academia to create an innovative and collaborative intellectual environment that fosters learning, scholarship, and service. We’re deeply rooted in NC State’s history as a university that excels at science, technology, engineering, and math. Our college’s diverse student body — over 4,000 students — hails from across North Carolina, the United States, and the world. Our faculty are thought leaders and field-tested experts with enduring ties to the world of business. Poole College of Management has four academic departments: Accounting, Business Management, Economics, and Management, Innovation, and Entrepreneurship. We offer bachelor’s degrees in accounting, business administration, economics; master’s degrees in accounting, business administration ( MBA ), economics, management (including specialized degrees); as well as a doctoral degree in economics. Among our non-degree programs, we offer Executive Education and graduate certificates. The college houses six initiatives fostering research, learning, and corporate engagement: Business Analytics Initiative, Business Sustainability Collaborative, Enterprise Risk Management Initiative, Entrepreneurship Clinic, Entrepreneurship Collaborative, and Supply Chain Resource Cooperative. The college is fully accredited by the AACSB . To learn more about our College, visit: https://poole.ncsu.edu Wolfpack Perks and Benefits As a Pack member, you belong here, and can enjoy exclusive perks designed to enhance your personal and professional well-being. As you consider this opportunity, we encourage you to review our Employee Value Proposition and learn more about what makes NC State the best place to learn and work for everyone. What we offer: Medical , Dental , and Vision Flexible Spending Account Retirement Programs Disability Plans Life Insurance Accident Plan Paid Time Off and Other Leave Programs 12 Holidays Each Year Tuition and Academic Assistance And so much more! Attain Work-life balance with our Childcare benefits, Wellness & Recreation Membership , and Wellness Programs that aim to build a thriving wolfpack community. Disclaimer: Perks and Benefit eligibility is based on Part-Time or Full-Time Employment status. Eligibility and Employer Sponsored Plans can be found within each of the links offered. Essential Job Duties The Department of Economics invites applications for part-time, non-tenure-track Lecturer positions. These appointments are typically for one semester or one academic year, with the possibility of renewal based on departmental needs and performance. Lecturers may be asked to teach one to three courses per semester at the undergraduate and/or graduate level. Instructional needs may include courses in microeconomics, macroeconomics, labor economics, and/or law and economics. Specific teaching needs for the upcoming academic year will be determined as departmental scheduling and enrollment demands are finalized. Applications will remain on file for one year should openings arise in subsequent semesters. Other Responsibilities Contributing member of the department, college, and university. Qualifications Minimum Education and Experience Requires doctoral degree, an equivalent degree, or equivalent experience in the appropriate field of interest. Other Required Qualifications Excellent teaching ability. A commitment to the success of students and programs at the University. Preferred Qualifications College teaching experience. Required License(s) or Certification(s) N/A Valid NC Driver's License required No Commercial Driver's License required No Recruitment Dates and Special Instructions Job Open Date 02/09/2026 Anticipated Close Date This is a pooled position we are actively recruiting for therefore applications will remain on file for one year should openings arise in subsequent semesters. Special Instructions to Applicants Please note, you will be required to attach a letter of application, CV/resume, and contact information for three professional references to apply. Finalists may be required to submit three letters of recommendation. Position Details Position Number 00105702 Position Type Non-Tenure-Track Faculty Full Time Equivalent (FTE) (1.0 = 40 hours/week) 0.675 Appointment < 9 Months Recurring Mandatory Designation - Adverse Weather Non Mandatory - Adverse Weather Mandatory Designation - Emergency Events Non Mandatory - Emergency Event Department ID 203001 - Economics - Poole College of Management EEO NC State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal opportunities for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, and veteran status. The University encourages all qualified applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities, to apply. Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodations in the application and interview process are welcome to contact 919-513-0574 to speak with a representative of the Office of Equal Opportunity. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at (919) 515-2135 or workatncstate@ncsu.edu . Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. Degree(s) must be obtained prior to start date in order to meet qualifications and receive credit. NC State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn of this opportunity? NCSU Website Job Alert (automated email from our system) NCSU Executive Search Services Monster.com CareerBuilder.com InsideHigherEd.com Other Online Job Board Carolina Job Finder / Employment Guide Job / Career Fair The Chronicle of Higher Education Professional Journal Print Advertisement (Newspaper / Periodical) Professional Organization Direct Contact from NCSU HR Representative / Recruiter NCSU Employee Referral Social Media (LinkedIn, Twitter, Facebook, Other) Other If you learned about this vacancy from \"other source\" or \"other website\", please provide the source. (Open Ended Question) * Do you have previous professional experience teaching at the College/university level? Yes NO Application Materials Required Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Contact Information for References Optional Documents NC STATE UNIVERSITY RALEIGH, NC 27695 PHONE: (919) 515-2011 Privacy Accessibility Emergency Information Policies NC State Home © 2019 NC State University. All rights reserved To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/230459": {
      "title": "Crew Leader I",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | Crew Leader I - 46995 Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) Crew Leader I - 46995 Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please include a resume as an attachment. Posting Details Job Posting Information Posting Number PG194984SP Internal Recruitment No Working Title Crew Leader I - 46995 Anticipated Hiring Range $38,500 - $40,585 Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 8:00 AM - 4:30 PM Job Location Raleigh, NC Department Environmental Services - Housekeeping About the Department The NC State University Facilities Division is home to nearly 900 professionals who plan , build , and maintain the spaces that foster an environment where innovation, learning, and community thrive. Through this work, we help create spaces that empower students, faculty, and staff to reach their full potential. Operating year-round, we manage more than 16.7 million gross square feet of built space and oversee 4,733 acres of campus infrastructure through a series of core departments, each composed of multiple specialized units: Design & Construction Business Operations Campus Operations and Maintenance Campus Planning and Strategic Investment Whether responding to a maintenance request, shaping future facilities, or creating spaces that inspire discovery, our team is grounded in excellence, service, and stewardship. Join the pack and become part of one of the largest and most respected employers in the state, helping shape the future of our campus community. Take a look below to see what we offer! Wolfpack Perks and Benefits As a Pack member, you belong here, and can enjoy exclusive perks designed to enhance your personal and professional well-being. As you consider this opportunity, we encourage you to review our Employee Value Proposition and learn more about what makes NC State the best place to learn and work for everyone. What we offer: Medical , Dental , and Vision Flexible Spending Account Retirement Programs Disability Plans Life Insurance Accident Plan Paid Time Off and Other Leave Programs 12 Holidays Each Year Tuition and Academic Assistance And so much more! Attain Work-life balance with our Childcare benefits, Wellness & Recreation Membership , and Wellness Programs that aim to build a thriving wolfpack community. Disclaimer: Perks and Benefit eligibility is based on Part-Time or Full-Time Employment status. Eligibility and Employer Sponsored Plans can be found within each of the links offered. Essential Job Duties Join our dynamic Environmental Services team as a Crew Leader I , where you’ll take the lead on essential projects like power washing entrances, window washing, waxing floors, and more. In this hands-on leadership role, you’ll guide a dedicated team while helping maintain clean, safe, and welcoming campus spaces. You’ll coordinate daily operations, address maintenance needs, and deliver high-quality service that directly impacts the campus community. This is a great opportunity for someone who enjoys leading by example, takes pride in their work, and thrives in a fast-paced, team-oriented environment. If you’re ready to step into a leadership role and make a visible impact every day, we encourage you to apply today and be part of a team that keeps our campus running at its best. Working Hours: Monday-Friday, 8:00 AM to 4:30 PM Key responsibilities and duties include, but are not limited to: Lead projects, including power washing, window washing, floor waxing, and re-lamping fixtures and dispensers Inspect and verify maintenance discrepancies and ensure timely resolution Provide support to other zones as needed, filling in for vacant positions or absenteeism Collect and submit timesheets within established timelines Perform critical duties during adverse weather or emergencies as assigned Complete accident reports within 24 hours of an incident Assist with equipment inventory and maintain a monthly inventory of storage closet supplies Submit supply orders for manager approval to ensure adequate stock levels Train new employees, ensuring they understand tasks and safety protocols Transport employees to various locations for assignments Collaborate with maintenance staff inside and outside the unit to resolve issues efficiently Address and resolve customer requests via radio communications, work orders, and direct interactions Ability to lift a minimum of 60 pounds continuously and 90 pounds occasionally with or without reasonable accommodations Communicate effectively with supervisors, coworkers, and the general public, and follow verbal and written instructions related to work assignments and operational needs. Other Responsibilities This position has been designated as essential personnel for the University and may be required to report to work during adverse weather conditions, even though the University may be operating on an alternate schedule This position may assist with snow and ice removal under the direction of a supervisor Other tasks and responsibilities may be assigned based on the needs of the organization and evolving priorities. Qualifications Minimum Experience/Education Some knowledge of cleaning procedures, ability to follow instructions and to perform medium to heavy physical work; or an equivalent combination of training and experience. Special certification may be required for some of these positions. Preferred Qualifications Demonstrated experience performing housekeeping or facilities maintenance in a university or commercial environment Ability to operate and perform minor repairs on cleaning equipment such as auto-scrubbers, burnishers, and power washers Strong communication and leadership skills with the ability to direct, train, and motivate team members Experience with inventory management, supply ordering systems, and timesheet coordination Working knowledge of Microsoft Office or Google Suite (Excel/Sheets, Word/Docs, PowerPoint/Slides) and familiarity with budgeting or reporting tools Required License or Certification Valid Driver’s License required Must be able to obtain a valid NC Driver’s License within 60 days of hire and must be maintained Valid NC Driver's License required Yes Commercial Driver's License Required? No Recruitment Dates and Special Instructions Job Open Date 05/11/2026 Earliest Close Date---- (Positions will be posted until 5:00 PM ET on this date. Positions remaining posted after this date are still accepting applications but may close at any time.) 05/15/2026 Notice to Applicants Please make sure that the work history you list on your application is identical to the work history listed on your resume. The application must be filled out completely, do not use the phrase “see resume”. Special Instructions Please include a resume as an attachment. Position Details Position Number 00046995 Position Type SHRA Position Classification Band Title Building Environmental Services Technician Position Classification Band Level Advanced Position Classification Salary Range $ 33,540  -  $ 47,847 Salary Grade Equivalency NC02 Alternate Option If no applicants apply who meet the required competency level and training & experience requirements, then management may consider other applicants. Salary would be determined based on competencies, equity, budget, and market considerations. Full Time Equivalent (FTE) (1.0 = 40 hours/week) 1.00 Appointment 12 Month Recurring Mandatory Designation - Adverse Weather Mandatory - Adverse Weather Mandatory Designation - Emergency Events Mandatory - Fire/Explosions, Mandatory - Medical Emergencies, Mandatory - Hazardous Material Incidents, Mandatory - Transportation Accidents, Mandatory - Evacuations/Natural Hazards, Mandatory - Utilities/Infrastructure Failure, Mandatory - Threats of Violence/Terrorism/Interpersonal Emergencies Time Limited Position No Time-Limited Appointment Length (if applicable) Department Id 445080 - Environmental Services EEO NC State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal opportunities for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, and veteran status. The University encourages all qualified applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities, to apply. Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodations in the application and interview process are welcome to contact 919-513-0574 to speak with a representative of the Office of Equal Opportunity. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at (919) 515-2135 or workatncstate@ncsu.edu . Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. Degree(s) must be obtained prior to start date in order to meet qualifications and receive credit. NC State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn of this opportunity? NCSU Website Job Alert (automated email from our system) NCSU Executive Search Services Monster.com CareerBuilder.com InsideHigherEd.com HigherEdJobs.com Other Online Job Board Carolina Job Finder / Employment Guide Job / Career Fair The Chronicle of Higher Education Professional Journal Print Advertisement (Newspaper / Periodical) Radio / Television Advertisement Professional Organization Higher Education Recruitment Consortium (HERC) Direct Contact from NCSU HR Representative / Recruiter NCSU Employee Referral Social Media (LinkedIn, Twitter, Facebook, Other) Other If you learned about this vacancy from \"other source\" or \"other website\", please provide the source. (Open Ended Question) * Do you have knowledge of cleaning procedures, ability to follow instructions and to perform medium to heavy physical work; OR an equivalent combination of training and experience? Yes No * A valid driver's license (DL) is required and a North Carolina Driver's License (NCDL) must be obtained within 60 days of hire and maintained as a condition of employment. Do you have a valid driver's license or the ability to obtain one prior to start date, and the ability to obtain a North Carolina Driver's License within 60 days of hire? Yes, I have a valid NCDL and will maintain it as a condition of employment. Yes, I have a valid DL from another state and will obtain a NCDL within 60 days of hire and maintain it as a condition of employment. Yes, I have a valid DL from another state but cannot or will not obtain a NCDL within 60 days of hire. No, I do not have a valid DL from any state, but I will obtain a it within 60 days of hire and maintain it as a condition of employment. No, I do not have a valid DL from any state and cannot or will not obtain it. * In the space below, please describe your professional experience as it relates to this role. (Open Ended Question) Application Materials Required Required Documents Resume Optional Documents NC STATE UNIVERSITY RALEIGH, NC 27695 PHONE: (919) 515-2011 Privacy Accessibility Emergency Information Policies NC State Home © 2019 NC State University. All rights reserved To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
