    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/234041": {
      "title": "Transportation Supervisor",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | Transportation Supervisor Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) Transportation Supervisor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please include as attachments a resume/CV and cover letter. Posting Details Job Posting Information Posting Number PG195051SP Internal Recruitment No Working Title Transportation Supervisor Anticipated Hiring Range $43,260 - $45,940 Work Schedule 40 hours per week; work hours may vary based on business needs; work schedule may include nights, weekends and holidays. May be required to work some overtime. Job Location Raleigh, NC Department NCSU Dining About the Department Campus Enterprises is NC State University’s division of retail and hospitality organizations — NC State Dining, NC State Stores, Lonnie Poole Golf Course, NC State Student Centers (Witherspoon and Talley), and the One Card Office. Each department is dedicated to providing service excellence, value and enrichment of the student experience in support of academic success. Rave! Catering is a department within NC State Dining. The primary purpose of the organizational unit is to provide catering services to students, staff, and faculty on the North Carolina State University campus. NC State Dining provides campus wide food services to students, staff, and faculty on the North Carolina State University Campus. NC State Dining operates 10 cafes, 3 food courts and 6 dining halls, 4 markets, 1 restaurant, vending, a nutritional counseling service, and a catering department. The department employs approximately 1000 temporary and student employees and approximately 180 permanent EHRA and SHRA employees. Wolfpack Perks and Benefits As a Pack member, you belong here, and can enjoy exclusive perks designed to enhance your personal and professional well-being. As you consider this opportunity, we encourage you to review our Employee Value Proposition and learn more about what makes NC State the best place to learn and work for everyone. What we offer: Medical , Dental , and Vision Flexible Spending Account Retirement Programs Disability Plans Life Insurance Accident Plan Paid Time Off and Other Leave Programs 12 Holidays Each Year Tuition and Academic Assistance And so much more! Attain Work-life balance with our Childcare benefits, Wellness & Recreation Membership , and Wellness Programs that aim to build a thriving wolfpack community. Disclaimer: Perks and Benefit eligibility is based on Part-Time or Full-Time Employment status. Eligibility and Employer Sponsored Plans can be found within each of the links offered. Essential Job Duties Are you a logistical mastermind who loves the fast-paced world of catering and events? We are seeking a dynamic and organized Catering Driver Supervisor to lead our transportation and beverage/equipment teams. In this role, you will be the backbone of our event execution, ensuring that all catering equipment, beverages, and supplies are delivered safely, efficiently, and on schedule. Beyond driving, you will manage our vehicle fleet, oversee inventory, and lead a dedicated team to deliver outstanding service across the University. If you are a proactive leader with a knack for logistics and a commitment to excellence, we want you on our team! Key Responsibilities Team Leadership & Scheduling Supervise & Support: Lead, motivate, and manage the catering transportation and beverage/equipment teams. Staff Scheduling: Utilize specialized departmental software to create, distribute, and monitor employee schedules. Clear Communication: Foster a collaborative team environment and maintain professional communication with multiple levels of University employees, peers, and customers. Logistics, Driving & Event Execution Delivery Operations: Develop, distribute, and monitor the daily delivery and transportation schedules. Behind the Wheel: Drive various delivery trucks and vehicles to execute catering and dining deliveries safely. Event Support: Load and unload cargo at each location; actively assist with event setup and breakdown. Fast-Paced Adaptability: Thrive and maintain professionalism under pressure in a high-energy, fast-moving environment. Fleet Management & Safety Fleet Care: Ensure a well-maintained, clean, and safe fleet of catering and dining vehicles. Training & Records: Establish and maintain a driver training program and a comprehensive fleet service record-keeping system. Preventative Maintenance: Oversee routine inspections, fueling, and preventative maintenance schedules in strict accordance with the NCSU Motor Pool guidelines. Inventory & Supply Control Inventory Management: Oversee inventory control, receipt, storage, and issuance of a wide variety of catering supplies, materials, and equipment. Physical Stamina: Ability to handle physical demands including bending, twisting, pulling, pushing, and standing for extended periods. Lifting Capability: Must be able to lift 30 pounds above the head, and up to 60 pounds on rare occasions (with or without reasonable accommodation). We offer a collaborative, team-oriented workspace where your leadership directly impacts the success of major University events. If you are ready to drive your career forward, apply today! Other Responsibilities Model the Division’s mission and values, introduce the Division’s mission and values to the employees, and foster a positive, cohesive workplace and congeniality among co-workers. Understand the goals and culture of the organization, and understand how employees’ work activities, teamwork, and customer service impact clients. Work with your supervisor and colleagues to understand these goals and the culture. Adhere to all University policies, procedures, and regulations, and Division standard operating practices and protocols. Perform other duties as assigned to ensure NC State Dining business needs are met. Qualifications Minimum Experience/Education High school diploma or equivalency and two years of supervisory experience in the area of assignment; or an equivalent combination of training and experience. Preferred Qualifications Supervisory Experience: Proven track record of successfully leading and scheduling a team with excellent organizational skills with a commitment to completing all tasks and performance goals efficiently. Logistics & Supply Expertise: Experience in the receipt, storage, issuance, and inventory control of supplies and equipment. Tech-Savvy: Proficient in standard computer use with the ability to quickly learn new, specialized departmental software. Communication Excellence: Strong written and verbal communication skills; ability to follow complex written and verbal instructions. Customer Service: Demonstrated ability to provide outstanding customer service, remaining calm, respectful, and professional under pressure or in difficult situations. Required License or Certification Must possess a valid driver’s license and be capable of safely operating various delivery vehicles. NCDL within 60 days of hire, must be maintained as a condition of employment. State vehicle furnished to drive to events or other Campus Enterprises locations. Valid NC Driver's License required Yes Commercial Driver's License Required? No Recruitment Dates and Special Instructions Job Open Date 06/10/2026 Earliest Close Date---- (Positions will be posted until 5:00 PM ET on this date. Positions remaining posted after this date are still accepting applications but may close at any time.) 06/23/2026 Notice to Applicants Please make sure that the work history you list on your application is identical to the work history listed on your resume. The application must be filled out completely, do not use the phrase “see resume”. Special Instructions Please include as attachments a resume/CV and cover letter. Position Details Position Number 00044277 Position Type SHRA Position Classification Band Title Support Services Supervisor Position Classification Band Level Contributing Position Classification Salary Range $ 35,880  -  $ 100,808 Salary Grade Equivalency NC09 Alternate Option If no applicants apply who meet the required competency level and training & experience requirements, then management may consider other applicants. Salary would be determined based on competencies, equity, budget, and market considerations. Full Time Equivalent (FTE) (1.0 = 40 hours/week) 1.00 Appointment 12 Month Recurring Mandatory Designation - Adverse Weather Mandatory - Adverse Weather Mandatory Designation - Emergency Events Mandatory - Medical Emergencies Time Limited Position No Time-Limited Appointment Length (if applicable) Department Id 471501 - Dining Administration EEO NC State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal opportunities for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, and veteran status. The University encourages all qualified applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities, to apply. Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodations in the application and interview process are welcome to contact 919-513-0574 to speak with a representative of the Office of Equal Opportunity. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at (919) 515-2135 or workatncstate@ncsu.edu . Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. Degree(s) must be obtained prior to start date in order to meet qualifications and receive credit. NC State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn of this opportunity? NCSU website Craigslist Indeed.com Carolina Job Finder/Employment Guide NC Works Dress for Success Technical/Trade School Program Job Fair (Identify Job Fair in question #2 below) Direct Contact from NSCU Representative (identify person in question #2 below) Other Monster.com Other online job board NCSU employee referral Social Media (LinkedIn, Twitter, Facebook, Ohter) If you learned about this vacancy from \"other source\" or \"other website\", please provide the source. (Open Ended Question) * Please select the response below that best describes your experience/education for the Support Services Supervisor position. High school diploma/GED and at least two years of supervisory experience in the area of assignment Associate's, Bachelor's, Master's, and/or Doctorate in any field and at least two years of supervisory experience in the area of assignment Combination of post-high school education and experience to equal at least two years of related experience (ex: 1 year towards a degree and 1 year of experience), including two years of supervisory experience in the area of assignment Did not complete high school but have a combination of education and experience to equal at least six years of related experience, including two years of supervisory experience (ex. 1 year of high school and 5 years of experience) None of the above * Please describe your supervisory experience. (Open Ended Question) * Please describe your professional experience driving a box truck. (Open Ended Question) * A valid driver's license (DL) is required and a North Carolina Driver's License (NCDL) must be obtained within 60 days of hire and maintained as a condition of employment. Do you have a valid driver's license or the ability to obtain one prior to start date, and the ability to obtain a North Carolina Driver's License within 60 days of hire? Yes, I have a valid NCDL and will maintain it as a condition of employment. Yes, I have a valid DL from another state and will obtain a NCDL within 60 days of hire and maintain it as a condition of employment. Yes, I have a valid DL from another state but cannot or will not obtain a NCDL within 60 days of hire. No, I do not have a valid DL from any state, but I will obtain a it within 60 days of hire and maintain it as a condition of employment. No, I do not have a valid DL from any state and cannot or will not obtain it. Application Materials Required Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents NC STATE UNIVERSITY RALEIGH, NC 27695 PHONE: (919) 515-2011 Privacy Accessibility Emergency Information Policies NC State Home © 2019 NC State University. All rights reserved To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/227270": {
      "title": "Position Information",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | Temporary Summer Camp Nurse - Reidsville, NC Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) Temporary Summer Camp Nurse - Reidsville, NC Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Attach: Contact information for 3 references Posting Details Position Information Posting Number PG195746TM Position Number 11ASO3651 Position Type Temporary Essential Job Duties Betsy-Jeff Penn 4-H Educational Center is seeking licensed RNs to join our team for the 2026 Summer Camp season! The Camp Nurse serves as a vital member of the Camp Healthcare Team, and oversees all health care operations for approximately 120 residential campers each week. The ideal candidate will enjoy working with youth of all ages, have the ability to work in unpredictable outdoor conditions, and thrive in a fast-paced dynamic environment outside of the clinical setting. Due to the on-call nature of this position, applicants must be able to reside on-site (housing provided) or within a half-hour commute of camp for the duration of the summer season. If you want to apply your nursing skills to a residential camp setting and work with a team like no other, apply today! Primary Responsibilities: Ability to follow all health care policies/procedures as described in facility standing orders, treatment procedures, and Staff Manual On call to respond to medical emergencies at all times campers are on-site, including overnight Perform basic assessment and first aid for conditions including but not limited to: minor soft tissue and musculoskeletal injuries, insect bites/stings, dehydration, sunburns, general illness; providing follow-up checks as needed Facilitate proper medication administration, for both routine prescription and over the counter medications, during all administration periods throughout the day Maintain written medical records for all medications and treatments administered according to state and American Camp Association Standards Prepare and record insurance and accident report forms Oversee Sunday check-in and Friday check-out of all camper medications each week, discussing any medical concerns with parent/guardian as needed Review all camper health forms and communicate medical needs to counselors as necessary Manage a team of 1-2 Health Care Coordinators who may assist with primary and secondary responsibilities Prepare and distribute camper’s medication schedule list to all counselors before dinner on Sundays Secondary Responsibilities: Attend all relevant staff trainings Keep camp Infirmary and medical supply storage space clean and organized Prepare and distribute all campus first aid kits, conducting routine checks and restocks as necessary Perform medical supply/equipment inventory and place restock orders Work Schedule: The summer season runs from May 29th – August 7th, 2026. Workdays will begin at noon on Sunday of each week and end at noon on Friday. These positions demand a high level of responsibility and attention to detail. You will be on call 24/7 including overnight, meal times and during activities to ensure overall health of campers and staff. Lodging (7 days a week, if needed) and Meals (5 days a week) provided. Potential to modify to a part-time role based on applicant’s needs and experience, please contact us directly to discuss options. Child discount for camp is negotiable Is Time Limited No If Yes, Appointment Length Wolfpack Perks and Benefits As a Pack member, you belong here, and can enjoy exclusive perks designed to enhance your personal and professional well-being. As you consider this opportunity, we encourage you to review our Employee Value Proposition and learn more about what makes NC State the best place to learn and work for everyone. What we offer: Health Insurance for Temporary Employees Enhance your career with LEAD courses Attend non-revenue generating sporting events for free. Attain Work-life balance with our Childcare discounts , Wellness & Recreation Membership , and Wellness Programs that aim to build a thriving wolfpack community. Disclaimer: Perks and Benefit eligibility is based on Part-Time or Full-Time Employment status. Eligibility and Employer Sponsored Plans can be found within each of the links offered. Department Information Job City & State Reidsville, NC Department Betsy Jeff Penn, 4-H Youth Development System Information Classification Title Temporary-Technical/Paraprofessional Working Title Temporary Summer Camp Nurse - Reidsville, NC Position Information Requirements and Preferences Work Schedule 40 hours per week Other Work/Responsibilities n/a Minimum Experience/Education Currently licensed to practice as a LPN , RN, or APRN within the state of North Carolina Department Required Skills Must possess a positive attitude and professionalism Experience in nursing or medical field Ability to administer medication Ability to work independently & follow directions. Enjoy working with youth in an outdoor environment Ability to work in extreme weather conditions including high temperatures and inclement weather situations Ability to communicate effectively with camp staff, parents/guardians, and campers Ability to utilize critical thinking in emergency situations outside of the clinical environment and determine when a higher level of care is appropriate Preferred Years Experience, Skills, Training, Education First Aid/ CPR / AED certified Required License or Certification LPN , RN, or APRN Valid driver’s license Valid NC Driver's License required? Yes Commercial Driver's License Required? No Recruitment Recruitment Details Anticipated Hiring Range $28-$35/hr Recruitment Dates Job Open Date 01/28/2026 Applicant Information Quick Link https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/226897 EEO NC State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal opportunities for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, and veteran status. The University encourages all qualified applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities, to apply. Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodations in the application and interview process are welcome to contact 919-513-0574 to speak with a representative of the Office of Equal Opportunity. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at (919) 515-2135 or workatncstate@ncsu.edu . Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. Degree(s) must be obtained prior to start date in order to meet qualifications and receive credit. NC State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). How did you learn of this opportunity? NCSU Website Job Alert (automated email from our system) NCSU Executive Search Services Monster.com CareerBuilder.com InsideHigherEd.com HigherEdJobs.com Other Online Job Board Carolina Job Finder / Employment Guide Job / Career Fair The Chronicle of Higher Education Professional Journal Print Advertisement (Newspaper / Periodical) Radio / Television Advertisement Professional Organization Higher Education Recruitment Consortium (HERC) Direct Contact from NCSU HR Representative / Recruiter NCSU Employee Referral Social Media (LinkedIn, Twitter, Facebook, Other) Other If you learned about this vacancy from \"other source\" or \"other website\", please provide the source. (Open Ended Question) * Are you a currently licensed in North Carolina as a LPN, RN or APRN? Yes No * Describe your experience in the nursing/medical field. (Open Ended Question) * Do you possess the ability to administer medication? Yes No * Do you enjoy working with youth in an outdoor environment? Yes No * Are you able to communicate effectively with camp staff, parents/guardians, and campers? Yes No * Describe how you would handle an emergency situation outside of a clinical environment. How you would determine when higher level care is required. (Open Ended Question) * Do you have a valid driver’s license? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Contact Information for References Optional Documents NC STATE UNIVERSITY RALEIGH, NC 27695 PHONE: (919) 515-2011 Privacy Accessibility Emergency Information Policies NC State Home © 2019 NC State University. All rights reserved To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
