    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/232917": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor in Community Sport Development",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | Assistant/Associate Professor in Community Sport Development Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) Assistant/Associate Professor in Community Sport Development Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please include the following as part of your application materials: Cover Letter (1 page) CV Research Statement (1 page) Teaching Statement (1 page) Note: References and Letters of recommendations will be requested of finalists. Posting Details Posting Information Posting Number PG194745EP Internal Recruitment No Working Title Assistant/Associate Professor in Community Sport Development Anticipated Hiring Range Rank and Salary will be commensurate with education and experience Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 8:00 AM - 5:00 PM Job Location Raleigh, NC Department Parks, Recreation & Tourism Management About the Department The Department of Parks, Recreation and Tourism Management ( PRTM ) prepares students for planning and management careers in parks, recreation, tourism, golf, and sport. We are a national leader in research and extension, dedicated to finding real solutions for real problems and helping communities and people thrive. The PRTM Department offers undergraduate and graduates degree programs in a variety of concentration areas. Since 2000, we’ve graduated over 2,000 students with baccalaureate degrees and more than 500 students with Masters or other advanced degrees. Relevant coursework is paired with hands-on fieldwork and service-learning opportunities specific to a student’s chosen specialty. In addition, students conduct research, participate in national consortiums and learn on-the-job through internships and co-ops. PRTM places a heavy emphasis on research for our faculty and students. As part of a tier-one research university, we have the people and the skills needed to advance knowledge and develop innovations that solve real problems. PRTM researchers are deeply engaged in work in four broad areas: Health and Well-Being, Human Dimensions of Built and Natural Environments, Sustainable Tourism, and Geospatial Methods and Models. Wolfpack Perks and Benefits As a Pack member, you belong here, and can enjoy exclusive perks designed to enhance your personal and professional well-being. As you consider this opportunity, we encourage you to review our Employee Value Proposition and learn more about what makes NC State the best place to learn and work for everyone. What we offer: Medical , Dental , and Vision Flexible Spending Account Retirement Programs Disability Plans Life Insurance Accident Plan Paid Time Off and Other Leave Programs 12 Holidays Each Year Tuition and Academic Assistance And so much more! Attain Work-life balance with our Childcare benefits, Wellness & Recreation Membership , and Wellness Programs that aim to build a thriving wolfpack community. Disclaimer: Perks and Benefit eligibility is based on Part-Time or Full-Time Employment status. Eligibility and Employer Sponsored Plans can be found within each of the links offered. Essential Job Duties The Department of Parks, Recreation and Tourism Management ( PRTM ) in the College of Natural Resources at North Carolina State University invites applications for an Assistant or Associate Professor with expertise in community sport development. We are seeking an innovative scholar and educator whose research explores the role of sport in strengthening communities through sustainable development, cultural engagement, health and well-being, youth development, economic impact, or related areas. In this role, you will shape the future of community sport development through impactful research, meaningful teaching, and collaboration with students, colleagues, and community partners. You’ll have the opportunity to develop or expand a nationally recognized research program, mentor the next generation of sport leaders, and translate scholarship into practice through partnerships that improve communities across North Carolina and beyond. As part of NC State’s land-grant mission, your work will extend beyond the classroom—creating lasting connections between the university, industry, and communities while contributing to innovative solutions with local, national, and global impact. Key responsibilities include: Develop Research by or expanding a high-impact scholarly research program that attracts external funding and contributes to the field of community sport development. Teach and Mentor undergraduate and graduate students through engaging instruction, student mentorship, and supervision of research and scholarly activities. Publish and Disseminate research through peer-reviewed publications, professional presentations, and other scholarly activities that advance knowledge and practice. Collaborate with faculty, community organizations, industry partners, and government agencies to foster interdisciplinary research and strengthen community engagement. Shape Academic Programs by contributing to curriculum development, continuous program improvement, and innovative learning opportunities across the department. Serve the University and Profession through departmental, college, and university committees, professional organizations, and public service activities that support NC State’s land-grant mission. If you are an innovative scholar who thrives on collaboration, values student success, and is committed to advancing community sport development through impactful research and engagement, we encourage you to apply. Other Responsibilities In addition to the core responsibilities of this role, there will be occasional opportunities to take on additional duties. This offers an opportunity to build on your skills, explore new areas, and gain a deeper understanding of the department’s operations. Qualifications Minimum Education and Experience Earned doctoral degree in recreation, sport management, tourism, community development, or a closely related field by the position start date. Other Required Qualifications Demonstrated record of scholarship appropriate for appointment at the Assistant or Associate Professor rank. Evidence of effective teaching and student mentorship at the undergraduate and/or graduate level. Demonstrated ability to communicate scholarly work through publications, presentations, or other professional dissemination. Strong interpersonal, written, and verbal communication skills Preferred Qualifications Record of pursuing and securing external research funding from federal, state, foundation, or industry sponsors. Experience building collaborative partnerships with community organizations, industry, government agencies, or interdisciplinary research teams. Ability to teach across multiple instructional formats, including in-person, online, hybrid, experiential, or study abroad programs. Scholarly focus in youth sport, sport tourism, sport-for-all initiatives, health and well-being, cultural heritage, economic development, sport analytics, or related areas. Demonstrated mentorship of undergraduate, master’s, or doctoral students. Contributions to professional organizations through leadership, committee service, presentations, or scholarly engagement. Established domestic or international partnerships that advance research, teaching, or community engagement. Required License(s) or Certification(s) N/A Valid NC Driver's License required No Commercial Driver's License required No Recruitment Dates and Special Instructions Job Open Date 07/20/2026 Anticipated Close Date 7/31/2026; if posting is active we are still accepting and reviewing applications. Special Instructions to Applicants Please include the following as part of your application materials: Cover Letter (1 page) CV Research Statement (1 page) Teaching Statement (1 page) Note: References and Letters of recommendations will be requested of finalists. Position Details Position Number 00000690 Position Type Tenured/Tenure-Track Faculty Full Time Equivalent (FTE) (1.0 = 40 hours/week) 1.00 Appointment 9 Month Recurring Mandatory Designation - Adverse Weather Non Mandatory - Adverse Weather Mandatory Designation - Emergency Events Non Mandatory - Emergency Event Department ID 150201 - Parks, Recreation & Tourism Management EEO NC State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal opportunities for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, and veteran status. The University encourages all qualified applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities, to apply. Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodations in the application and interview process are welcome to contact 919-513-0574 to speak with a representative of the Office of Equal Opportunity. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at (919) 515-2135 or workatncstate@ncsu.edu . Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. Degree(s) must be obtained prior to start date in order to meet qualifications and receive credit. NC State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn of this opportunity? NCSU Website Job Alert (automated email from our system) NCSU Executive Search Services Monster.com CareerBuilder.com InsideHigherEd.com HigherEdJobs.com Other Online Job Board Carolina Job Finder / Employment Guide Job / Career Fair The Chronicle of Higher Education Professional Journal Print Advertisement (Newspaper / Periodical) Radio / Television Advertisement Professional Organization Higher Education Recruitment Consortium (HERC) Direct Contact from NCSU HR Representative / Recruiter NCSU Employee Referral Social Media (LinkedIn, Twitter, Facebook, Other) Other If you learned about this vacancy from \"other source\" or \"other website\", please provide the source. (Open Ended Question) * The position requires a Ph.D. in parks, recreation and tourism management or a closely related field and a strong interest in the scholarship of teaching. Do you meet these minimums? Yes No Application Materials Required Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Research Statement Teaching Statement Optional Documents Contact Information for References NC STATE UNIVERSITY RALEIGH, NC 27695 PHONE: (919) 515-2011 Privacy Accessibility Emergency Information Policies NC State Home © 2019 NC State University. All rights reserved To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
