    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/234443": {
      "title": "Temporary Farm to ECE Extension Coordinator",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | Temporary Farm to ECE Extension Coordinator Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) Temporary Farm to ECE Extension Coordinator Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number PG196183TM Position Number 11ASO3753 Position Type Temporary Essential Job Duties The Farm to Early Care & Education ( ECE ) Extension Coordinator will work with county-level Extension staff and community partners to assess community needs and coordinate implementation of Farm to ECE programming in Head Start and other ECE settings. The Coordinator will provide hands-on support for establishing and sustaining ECE gardens and garden education programs; provide virtual and in-person coaching and technical assistance to teachers, administrators, and other partners; coordinate delivery and setup of garden supplies and outdoor learning materials; support garden site preparation, planting, maintenance, and troubleshooting; participate in community and Extension meetings; support development of partner action plans; and assist with project research and evaluation activities, including data collection and site visits. Regular travel to participating counties and community sites is required. This is a part-time position averaging 10–15 hours per week. Regular travel to participating counties and ECE sites is an essential function of the position. The role includes outdoor, hands-on work related to garden establishment and maintenance and may require work in varying weather conditions, transport of supplies/materials, and assistance with setup or assembly of garden and outdoor learning materials. Is Time Limited No If Yes, Appointment Length Wolfpack Perks and Benefits As a Pack member, you belong here, and can enjoy exclusive perks designed to enhance your personal and professional well-being. As you consider this opportunity, we encourage you to review our Employee Value Proposition and learn more about what makes NC State the best place to learn and work for everyone. What we offer: Health Insurance for Temporary Employees Enhance your career with LEAD courses Attend non-revenue generating sporting events for free. Attain Work-life balance with our Childcare discounts , Wellness & Recreation Membership , and Wellness Programs that aim to build a thriving wolfpack community. Disclaimer: Perks and Benefit eligibility is based on Part-Time or Full-Time Employment status. Eligibility and Employer Sponsored Plans can be found within each of the links offered. Department Information Job City & State Raleigh, NC Department AHS System Information Classification Title Temporary-Technical/Paraprofessional Working Title Temporary Farm to ECE Extension Coordinator Position Information Requirements and Preferences Work Schedule 10-15/hrs per week, flexible during the normal work week, Monday-Friday, 8am-5pm Other Work/Responsibilities n/a Minimum Experience/Education High School Diploma or equivalency and one year of related office experience; or equivalent combination of training and experience. Department Required Skills Ability to work independently and collaboratively with Extension staff, early care and education partners, and community stakeholders Effective written and verbal communication and organizational skills Ability to provide hands-on support for garden establishment and maintenance Basic knowledge of gardening, horticulture, agriculture education, or a related field, including plant care, soils, fertilizers, seasonal planting, pest management, and garden troubleshooting Ability and willingness to travel regularly to participating counties and community sites Ability to perform outdoor work in varying weather conditions and transport/setup program materials Ability to complete required NC State human-subjects/ CITI training and follow research and site protocols Preferred Years Experience, Skills, Training, Education Experience translating gardening or agricultural knowledge into educational programming or technical assistance for non-expert audiences Experience working with early care and education, Head Start, Cooperative Extension, community-based programs, or Farm to ECE initiatives Experience providing coaching or technical assistance Experience supporting program implementation, evaluation, or data collection Required License or Certification Valid driver’s license Valid NC Driver's License required? Yes Commercial Driver's License Required? No Recruitment Recruitment Details Anticipated Hiring Range Up to $22/hr, depending on experience Recruitment Dates Job Open Date 08/31/2026 Applicant Information Quick Link https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/234434 EEO NC State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal opportunities for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, and veteran status. The University encourages all qualified applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities, to apply. Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodations in the application and interview process are welcome to contact 919-513-0574 to speak with a representative of the Office of Equal Opportunity. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at (919) 515-2135 or workatncstate@ncsu.edu . Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. Degree(s) must be obtained prior to start date in order to meet qualifications and receive credit. NC State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). How did you learn of this opportunity? NCSU Website Job Alert (automated email from our system) NCSU Executive Search Services Monster.com CareerBuilder.com InsideHigherEd.com HigherEdJobs.com Other Online Job Board Carolina Job Finder / Employment Guide Job / Career Fair The Chronicle of Higher Education Professional Journal Print Advertisement (Newspaper / Periodical) Radio / Television Advertisement Professional Organization Higher Education Recruitment Consortium (HERC) Direct Contact from NCSU HR Representative / Recruiter NCSU Employee Referral Social Media (LinkedIn, Twitter, Facebook, Other) Other If you learned about this vacancy from \"other source\" or \"other website\", please provide the source. (Open Ended Question) * Do you have a High School Diploma or equivalency and one year of related office experience; or equivalent combination of training and experience? Yes No * Are you able to work independently and collaboratively with Extension staff, early care and education partners, and community stakeholders? Yes No * Do you have effective written and verbal communication and organizational skills? Yes No * Do you possess the ability to provide hands-on support for garden establishment and maintenance? Yes No * Do you have basic knowledge of gardening, horticulture, agriculture education, or related field, including plant care, soils, fertilization, seasonal planting, pest management and garden troubleshooting? Yes No * Are you willing to travel regularly to participating counties and community sites? Yes No * Are you able to work in varying weather conditions (cold, heat, humidity, rain, pollen)? Yes No * Are you someone who is willing to complete the required NC State human-subjects/CITI training and follow research and site protocols? Yes No Do you have experience translating gardening or agricultural knowledge into educational programming or technical assistance for non-expert audiences? Yes No Do you have experience working with early care and education, Head Start, Cooperative Extension, community-based programs, or Farm to ECE initiatives? Yes No Do you have experience providing coaching or technical assistance? Yes No Do you have experience supporting program implementation, evaluation, or data collection? Yes No * Do you have a valid driver’s license? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Contact Information for References Optional Documents NC STATE UNIVERSITY RALEIGH, NC 27695 PHONE: (919) 515-2011 Privacy Accessibility Emergency Information Policies NC State Home © 2019 NC State University. All rights reserved To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
