    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/229616": {
      "title": "Position Information",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | Stock Clerk Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) Stock Clerk Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number PG195906TM Position Number 47FOUNTAINSTOCKCLERK0426 Position Type Temporary Essential Job Duties JOIN THE PACK ! NC State Dining offers meaningful opportunities for employment across our retail and hospitality units. We offer competitive pay, flexible schedules, and opportunity for learning, growth, and promotion. Dedicated and experienced professional staff are available to provide on-the-job training and assistance so you become a successful member of the team. We are seeking individuals to Join our Pack as a Stock Clerk. Essential Job Duties: • Assist in checking in food stock items, breaking down pallets, and putting away food stock in a timely fashion. • Place received items in appropriate storage areas. • Pull requisitioned stock items for usage in the units throughout the building. • Record a limited daily inventory of food items plus a complete monthly food inventory for unit. • Other duties as assigned to ensure NC State Dining business needs are met. Position may be asked to assist in other locations as necessary. This is an hourly position with a mandatory 32-day break at the end of 11 months. Excellent performance during this time may provide an opportunity to renew employment and/or advance. Is Time Limited No If Yes, Appointment Length Wolfpack Perks and Benefits As a Pack member, you belong here, and can enjoy exclusive perks designed to enhance your personal and professional well-being. As you consider this opportunity, we encourage you to review our Employee Value Proposition and learn more about what makes NC State the best place to learn and work for everyone. What we offer: Health Insurance for Temporary Employees Enhance your career with LEAD courses Attend non-revenue generating sporting events for free. Attain Work-life balance with our Childcare discounts , Wellness & Recreation Membership , and Wellness Programs that aim to build a thriving wolfpack community. Disclaimer: Perks and Benefit eligibility is based on Part-Time or Full-Time Employment status. Eligibility and Employer Sponsored Plans can be found within each of the links offered. Department Information Job City & State Raleigh, NC Department NC State Dining System Information Classification Title Temporary-Clerical Working Title Stock Clerk Position Information Requirements and Preferences Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 6:00am-2:30pm Other Work/Responsibilities Be an ambassador for NC State Dining and the university as a whole and enrich the quality of life for the campus community and support student success. Work as a cohesive team member and play an integral part in creating a positive work environment. Minimum Experience/Education High School Diploma or equivalency; or equivalent combination of training and experience. Department Required Skills Ability to work in a fast-paced environment Communicate effectively with customers, supervisors, and peers. Follow written and/or verbal instructions, and excellence in completing all tasks. Read shipping labels and/or storage labels. Provide outstanding customer service, including the ability to remain professional and respectful under pressure when dealing with difficult situations. Requires bending, twisting, pulling and pushing. Because of the nature of a food service operations and working in a kitchen, you must be able to work in extremely hot and cold conditions. Must be able to lift up to 60 lb with or without reasonable accommodation. Preferred Years Experience, Skills, Training, Education Previous experience working in a stock room. Required License or Certification N/A Valid NC Driver's License required? No Commercial Driver's License Required? No Recruitment Recruitment Details Anticipated Hiring Range $15.00/hour Recruitment Dates Job Open Date 04/14/2026 Applicant Information Quick Link https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/229425 EEO NC State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal opportunities for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, and veteran status. The University encourages all qualified applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities, to apply. Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodations in the application and interview process are welcome to contact 919-513-0574 to speak with a representative of the Office of Equal Opportunity. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at (919) 515-2135 or workatncstate@ncsu.edu . Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. Degree(s) must be obtained prior to start date in order to meet qualifications and receive credit. NC State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn of this opportunity? NCSU Website NCSU Executive Search Services Monster.com CareerBuilder.com InsideHigherEd.com Other Online Job Board Carolina Job Finder / Employment Guide Job / Career Fair The Chronicle of Higher Education HERC Professional Journal Print Advertisement (Newspaper / Periodical) Professional Organization Direct Contact from NCSU HR Representative / Recruiter NCSU Employee Referral Social Media (LinkedIn, Twitter