    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/233428": {
      "title": "Temporary Event Technician Pool, University Theatre, Backstage & Front of House",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | Temporary Event Technician Pool, University Theatre, Backstage &amp; Front of House Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) Temporary Event Technician Pool, University Theatre, Backstage & Front of House Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number PG191736TM Position Number 24UT01 Position Type Temporary Essential Job Duties The Division of Academic & Student Affairs ( DASA ) is where students discover connections and community. It is where students live, where they gather, where they improve themselves, each other, and their university. DASA is where students seek guidance and support, both in and outside of the classroom. The division serves all students at NC State through three integrated components: academic affairs, student affairs, and University College. NC State wants employees to achieve their highest potential at work, learn more about our employee value proposition here ( You Belong Here ). The Division of Academic and Student Affairs is the place to work for values-driven faculty and staff who are passionate about promoting the success of the whole student. University Theatre is the campus’ open access community theatre and operates multiple facilities: Stewart Theatre, in the Talley Student Center, and the Titmus Theatre and Kennedy McIlwee Studio Theatre, along with the associated shops and classroom spaces for producing theatre. Our mission is to create a welcoming, student-centered community that inspires meaningful connections grounded in the experience of making and sharing theatre. We present a wide variety of productions, experiences and provide spaces for campus organizations to present events. Please note : This position is based on need and availability. Applicants will be reviewed on a rolling basis. Event Technician will assist Operations and Event Coordinator, Technical and Assistant Technical Directors in day to day operations of University Theatre venues in support of campus events, rental clients and University Theatre performances as required. Duties will include: Backstage duties as assigned, including but not limited to lighting operation (lighting consoles, follow spotlights), sound reinforcement ( FOH console operation, audio system setup), load-in and load-out assistance, occasional system and facilities maintenance. Front of house technicians: position will serve as house manager, responsible for coordinating all Front-Of-House ( FOH ) operations in the Theatre spaces. Specific responsibilities include Training and supervising ushers Communicating with stage managers and technical supervisors during and in advance of performances Ensuring the safety of all patrons using theatre spaces. Experience in dealing with the public of all ages Sensitivity to the needs of patrons Upbeat, enthusiastic attitude in public relations Ability to enforce department safety regulations and communicate the same to the public Attention to detail Ability to troubleshoot problems and work for customer satisfaction Ability to work independently with limited direct supervision. Is Time Limited No If Yes, Appointment Length Wolfpack Perks and Benefits As a Pack member, you belong here , and can enjoy exclusive perks designed to enhance your personal and professional well-being. As you consider this opportunity, we encourage you to review our Employee Value Proposition and learn more about what makes NC State the best place to learn and work for everyone. What we offer: Health Insurance for Temporary Employees Enhance your career with LEAD courses Attend non-revenue generating sporting events for free. Attain Work-life balance with our Childcare discounts , Wellness & Recreation Membership , and Wellness Programs that aim to build a thriving wolfpack community. Disclaimer: Perks and Benefit eligibility is based on Part-Time or Full-Time Employment status. Eligibility and Employer Sponsored Plans can be found within each of the links offered. Department Information Job City & State Raleigh, NC Department University Theatre System Information Classification Title Temporary-Technical/Paraprofessional Working Title Temporary Event Technician Pool, University Theatre, Backstage & Front of House Position Information Requirements and Preferences Work Schedule As needed basis; nights and weekends typical Other Work/Responsibilities Minimum Experience/Education High School Diploma; or equivalent combination of training and experience Department Required Skills Desire to work with a variety of campus departments, student organizations and rental clients. Preferred Years Experience, Skills, Training, Education Experience with ETC lighting control systems ( EOS Family) and intelligent lighting. Live audio mixing experience on analog and digital mixing consoles. Experience in Customer service and public relations Required License or Certification N/A Valid NC Driver's License required? No Commercial Driver's License Required? No Recruitment Recruitment Details Anticipated Hiring Range $10.00 - $20.00 / hour (Commensurate with Experience) Recruitment Dates Job Open Date 07/27/2026 Applicant Information Quick Link https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/145837 EEO NC State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal opportunities for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, and veteran status. The University encourages all qualified applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities, to apply. Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodations in the application and interview process are welcome to contact 919-513-0574 to speak with a representative of the Office of Equal Opportunity. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at (919) 515-2135 or workatncstate@ncsu.edu . Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. Degree(s) must be obtained prior to start date in order to meet qualifications and receive credit. NC State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Briefly describe any experience, work or volunteer that you have working in production or presenting theatre facilities in lighting, sound, or technical crew. (Open Ended Question) * How did you learn of this opportunity? NCSU Website Job Alert (automated email from our system) NCSU Executive Search Services Monster.com CareerBuilder.com InsideHigherEd.com HigherEdJobs.com Other Online Job Board Carolina Job Finder / Employment Guide Job / Career Fair The Chronicle of Higher Education Professional Journal Print Advertisement (Newspaper / Periodical) Radio / Television Advertisement Professional Organization Higher Education Recruitment Consortium (HERC) Direct Contact from NCSU HR Representative / Recruiter NCSU Employee Referral Social Media (LinkedIn, Twitter, Facebook, Other) Other * If you learned about this vacancy from \"other source\" or \"other website\", please provide the source. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Contact Information for References Optional Documents Cover Letter NC STATE UNIVERSITY RALEIGH, NC 27695 PHONE: (919) 515-2011 Privacy Accessibility Emergency Information Policies NC State Home © 2019 NC State University. All rights reserved To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
