    "https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/232959": {
      "title": "Position Information",
      "description": "NCSU Employment Site | Postdoctoral Research Scholar Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Equal Opportunity at NC State News at NC State NC State Named Best Large Employer in North Carolina You Belong Here (Our Employee Value Proposition) Postdoctoral Research Scholar Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Cover letter that includes timing of availability and a description of how your research interests align with the position description, CV, contact information for three references. Posting Details Position Information Posting Number PG191735PD Position Number 00106345 Position Type Post Doc FLSA Exempt Departmental Information Department ID 111801 - Entomology and Plant Pathology Department 111801 - Entomology and Plant Pathology Job City & State Raleigh, NC Position Information Position Overview Essential Job Duties We are a dynamic research team focused on elucidating the molecular mechanisms of plant-virus-vector interactions. Our mission is to develop new foundational knowledge of plant viruses and to translate this information into new control strategies and biotechnology tools for crop improvement. Grapevine red blotch disease has emerged as a major threat to winegrape production throughout North America in recent decades. We aim to develop tools and protocols for grapevine red blotch virus ( GRBV ) detection in insects and plants. We will integrate these new technologies with established methods to better understand GRBV localization in the insect vector throughout circulative transmission and make strides in understanding GRBV latency in grapevine and experimental plant hosts. The detection tools developed will also have applications for red blotch diagnostics. Duties and Responsibilities: The postdoctoral research scholar will express GRBV proteins in prokaryotic and eukaryotic (insect and plant) cells and purify proteins for antibody production. (50%) Characterize GRBV dissemination and tissue tropism in insect vectors with in situ methods. (50%) Molecular analysis of viral genomes, gene expression, and gene function. Primer design, DNA / RNA handling, protein expression, Western blotting. Develop and test standardized procedures for determining vector competence on candidate vectors. Other Work/Responsibilities Develop weekly research reports for the PI and quarterly reports to the funding agency. Contribute to proposal writing and disseminating research findings to the broader community. Maintenance of virus and insect colonies. Training and mentoring other lab members. Wolfpack Perks and Benefits As a Pack member, you belong here, and can enjoy exclusive perks designed to enhance your personal and professional well-being. As you consider this opportunity, we encourage you to review our Employee Value Proposition and learn more about what makes NC State the best place to learn and work for everyone. What we offer: Medical, Dental, Vision, Retirement and Leave Faculty and Staff Assistance Program Enhance your career with LEAD courses Attend non-revenue generating sporting events for free. Attain Work-life balance with our Childcare benefits, Wellness & Recreation Membership , and Wellness Programs that aim to build a thriving wolfpack community. Disclaimer: Perks and Benefit eligibility is based on Part-Time or Full-Time Employment status. Eligibility and Employer Sponsored Plans can be found within each of the links offered. Requirements and Preferences Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 8am-5pm Department Required Skills Ability to generate infectious clones of plant viruses and/or gene expression experience. Demonstrated experience with experimental design and statistical analysis, molecular biology, handling plant and/or insect viruses. Molecular biology skills required: primer design, DNA / RNA handling, protein expression, Western blotting, and qRT- PCR . Preferred Years Experience, Skills, Training, Education We are searching for an independent researcher with: Excellent scientific and writing skills. Experience with cloning plant viruses, construction of full-length infectious clones and mutagenesis of regulatory regions. Experience and/or knowledge of maize genetics and pathogen interactions. Experience with transmission biology of insect-borne viruses, herbivorous insect husbandry and/or genome editing of plants is preferred. Mentoring experience or a desire to mentor undergraduate researchers is an important component of this position. Required License or Certification Valid NC Driver’s License or the ability to obtain one within 60 days of hire. Valid NC Driver's License required? Yes Commercial Driver's License Required? No Recruitment Recruitment Details Anticipated Hiring Range Commensurate with Experience If you anticipate multiple hires from this search, please indicate how many Recruitment Dates Job Open Date 07/16/2026 Applicant Information Quick Link https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/232852 EEO NC State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive equal opportunities for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, and veteran status. The University encourages all qualified applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities, to apply. Individuals with disabilities requiring disability-related accommodations in the application and interview process are welcome to contact 919-513-0574 to speak with a representative of the Office of Equal Opportunity. If you have general questions about the application process, you may contact Human Resources at (919) 515-2135 or workatncstate@ncsu.edu . Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. Degree(s) must be obtained prior to start date in order to meet qualifications and receive credit. NC State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn of this opportunity? NCSU Website NCSU Executive Search Services Monster.com CareerBuilder.com InsideHigherEd.com Other Online Job Board Carolina Job Finder / Employment Guide Job / Career Fair The Chronicle of Higher Education HERC Professional Journal Print Advertisement (Newspaper / Periodical) Professional Organization Direct Contact from NCSU HR Representative / Recruiter NCSU Employee Referral Social Media (LinkedIn, Twitter, Facebook, Other) Other If you learned about this vacancy from \"other source\" or \"other website\", please provide the source. (Open Ended Question) * Do you have a valid NC Driver's license or the ability to obtain one within 60 days of your start date? Yes No * Do you have, or will you have by the start date, a PhD in Virology, Plant Pathology, Entomology, or related discipline? Yes No * According to our university's regulations, a postdoctoral scholar needs to have successfully completed their terminal degree no more than 5 years from the start date of their appointment. Given this, please provide the date (MM/DD/YYYY) your terminal degree has been or will be confirmed. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Contact Information for References Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents NC STATE UNIVERSITY RALEIGH, NC 27695 PHONE: (919) 515-2011 Privacy Accessibility Emergency Information Policies NC State Home © 2019 NC State University. All rights reserved To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
